{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012XbfYnsmEbTxHtU48rSi8L","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# SteadyLetters\n     2→\n     3→**AI-Powered Physical Letter Sending Platform**\n     4→\n     5→A SaaS web application that enables users to create and send physical handwritten-style letters via Thanks.io API integration. Features AI letter generation, voice transcription, image generation, and subscription-based usage tiers.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Quick Start\n    10→\n    11→### Development Server\n    12→\n    13→```bash\n    14→npm install\n    15→npm run dev\n    16→```\n    17→\n    18→Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) to view the application.\n    19→\n    20→### Prerequisites\n    21→\n    22→- Node.js 20+\n    23→- PostgreSQL database (or Supabase account)\n    24→- Required API keys (see Environment Setup below)\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→## Tech Stack\n    29→\n    30→| Layer | Technology |\n    31→|-------|------------|\n    32→| Frontend | Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript |\n    33→| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui |\n    34→| Database | PostgreSQL (Supabase), Prisma ORM |\n    35→| Auth | Supabase Auth |\n    36→| Storage | Supabase Storage |\n    37→| AI | OpenAI GPT-4o, Whisper, DALL-E 3 |\n    38→| Mail API | Thanks.io |\n    39→| Payments | Stripe |\n    40→| Deployment | Vercel |\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## Environment Setup\n    45→\n    46→Create a `.env.local` file with the following variables:\n    47→\n    48→```env\n    49→# Database\n    50→DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...\n    51→\n    52→# Supabase\n    53→NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co\n    54→NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...\n    55→SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...\n    56→\n    57→# OpenAI\n    58→OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n    59→\n    60→# Stripe\n    61→STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n    62→NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\n    63→STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n    64→STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID=price_...\n    65→STRIPE_BUSINESS_PRICE_ID=price_...\n    66→\n    67→# Thanks.io\n    68→THANKS_IO_API_KEY=...\n    69→```\n    70→\n    71→See `DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md` for complete environment variable documentation.\n    72→\n    73→---\n    74→\n    75→## Project Structure\n    76→\n    77→```\n    78→/\n    79→├── src/\n    80→│   ├── app/                    # Next.js App Router\n    81→│   │   ├── actions/            # Server actions (CRUD operations)\n    82→│   │   ├── api/                # API routes\n    83→│   │   ├── dashboard/          # Dashboard page\n    84→│   │   ├── generate/           # Letter generation page\n    85→│   │   ├── send/               # Send letter page\n    86→│   │   ├── recipients/         # Recipient management\n    87→│   │   ├── templates/          # Template management\n    88→│   │   ├── orders/             # Order history\n    89→│   │   └── billing/            # Subscription management\n    90→│   ├── components/             # React components\n    91→│   │   ├── ui/                 # shadcn/ui components\n    92→│   │   ├── navbar.tsx\n    93→│   │   ├── voice-recorder.tsx\n    94→│   │   └── ...\n    95→│   └── lib/                    # Utility libraries\n    96→│       ├── thanks-io.ts        # Thanks.io API client\n    97→│       ├── openai.ts           # OpenAI integrations\n    98→│       ├── stripe.ts           # Stripe client\n    99→│       ├── usage.ts            # Usage tracking\n   100→│       └── tiers.ts            # Subscription tier logic\n   101→├── prisma/\n   102→│   └── schema.prisma           # Database schema\n   103→├── tests/                      # Test files (48+ tests)\n   104→│   ├── e2e/                    # Playwright E2E tests\n   105→│   └── unit/                   # Jest unit tests\n   106→└── PRD_*.md                    # Product requirement documents\n   107→```\n   108→\n   109→---\n   110→\n   111→## Available Scripts\n   112→\n   113→```bash\n   114→#