urface, borderRadius: 12, borderWidth: 1, borderColor: colors.border, paddingHorizontal: 14 },\n    45→    input: { flex: 1, paddingVertical: 14, fontSize: 16, color: colors.text, marginLeft: 10 },\n    46→    button: { backgroundColor: colors.primary, borderRadius: 12, padding: 16, alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 24 },\n    47→    buttonText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 17, fontWeight: '600' },\n    48→  });\n    49→\n    50→  return (\n    51→    <KeyboardAvoidingView style={s.container} behavior={Platform.OS === 'ios' ? 'padding' : undefined}>\n    52→      <View style={s.content}>\n    53→        <Text style={s.title}>Reset Password</Text>\n    54→        <Text style={s.subtitle}>Enter your email and we'll send a reset link.</Text>\n    55→        <View style={s.inputWrapper}>\n    56→          <Mail size={20} color={colors.textMuted} />\n    57→          <TextInput style={s.input} placeholder=\"Email\" placeholderTextColor={colors.textMuted} value={email} onChangeText={setEmail} autoCapitalize=\"none\" keyboardType=\"email-address\" />\n    58→        </View>\n    59→        <TouchableOpacity style={s.button} onPress={handleReset} disabled={isLoading}>\n    60→          {isLoading ? <ActivityIndicator color=\"#fff\" /> : <Text style={s.buttonText}>Send Reset Link</Text>}\n    61→        </TouchableOpacity>\n    62→      </View>\n    63→    </KeyboardAvoidingView>\n    64→  );\n    65→}\n    66→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019vJMKEcsvNCpXDUitC4Wta","session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"7d406749-e28a-4fee-9fd9-8bd6ec6f8343","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(auth)/forgot-password.tsx","content":"import React, { useState } from 'react';\nimport {\n  View,\n  Text,\n  TextInput,\n  TouchableOpacity,\n  StyleSheet,\n  Alert,\n  KeyboardAvoidingView,\n  Platform,\n  ActivityIndicator,\n} from 'react-native';\nimport { useTheme } from '@/providers/ThemeProvider';\nimport { useAuth } from '@/providers/AuthProvider';\nimport { useRouter } from 'expo-router';\nimport { Mail } from 'lucide-react-native';\n\nexport default function ForgotPasswordScreen() {\n  const { colors } = useTheme();\n  const { resetPassword } = useAuth();\n  const router = useRouter();\n\n  const [email, setEmail] = useState('');\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);\n\n  const handleReset = async () => {\n    if (!email) { Alert.alert('Missing Email', 'Please enter your email.'); return; }\n    setIsLoading(true);\n    try {\n      await resetPassword(email);\n      Alert.alert('Check Your Email', 'Password reset link sent.', [{ text: 'OK', onPress: () => router.back() }]);\n    } catch (error) {\n      Alert.alert('Error', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to send reset link');\n    } finally {\n      setIsLoading(false);\n    }\n  };\n\n  const s = StyleSheet.create({\n    container: { flex: 1, backgroundColor: colors.background },\n    content: { padding: 24, paddingTop: 40 },\n    title: { fontSize: 28, fontWeight: '700', color: colors.text, marginBottom: 8 },\n    subtitle: { fontSize: 16, color: colors.textSecondary, marginBottom: 32 },\n    inputWrapper: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', backgroundColor: colors.surface, borderRadius: 12, borderWidth: 1, borderColor: colors.border, paddingHorizontal: 14 },\n    input: { flex: 1, paddingVertical: 14, fontSize: 16, color: colors.text, marginLeft: 10 },\n    button: { backgroundColor: colors.primary, borderRadius: 12, padding: 16, alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 24 },\n    buttonText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 17, fontWeight: '600' },\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <KeyboardAvoidingView style={s.container} behavior={Platform.OS === 'ios' ? 'padding' : undefined}>\n      <View style={s.content}>\n        <Text style={s.title}>Reset Password</Text>\n        <Text style={s.subtitle}>Enter your email and we'll send a reset link.</Text>\n        <View style={s.inputWrapper}>\n          <Mail size={20} color={colors.textMuted} />\n          <TextInput style={s.input} placeholder=\"Email\" placeholderTextColor={colors.textMuted} value={email} onChangeText={setEmail} autoCapitalize=\"none\" keyboardType=\"email-address\" />\n        </View>\n        <TouchableOpacity style={s.button} onPress={handleReset} disabled={isLoading}>\n          {isLoading ? <ActivityIndicator color=\"#fff\" /> : <Text style={s.buttonText}>Send Reset Link</Text>}\n        </TouchableOpacity>\n      </View>\n    </KeyboardAvoidingView>\n  );\n}\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rnaq6c7L3uKjMYdewSXoGL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report based on all the information I've gathered. Let me create a final summary document:\n\n## Comprehensive Project Context Report\n\nBased on my exploration of the KindLetters project, here's the complete picture:\n\n### Project Overview\n\n**SteadyLetters** (formerly KindLetters) is a SaaS web application that enables users to create and send physical handwritten-style letters via the Thanks.io API. The project consists of:\n\n1. **Main Web Application** - Next.js 16 with React 19 and TypeScript\n2. **iOS Mobile App** - Recently scaffolded using Expo Router (React Native)\n3. **Supporting Backend Services** - Express backend service\n\n---\n\n### Current Status Summary\n\n#### Main Web Application (Next.js)\n- **Phase:** 6 - Mobile Optimization (in progress)\n- **Total Features:** 139 features defined\n- **Status:** 139/139 features showing as complete (100%) according to feature_list.json\n- **Latest Commit:** `feat: scaffold SteadyLetters iOS Expo Router app with full screen set, services, providers, live tests, and ACD config` (Feb 17)\n\n#### iOS Mobile App (NEW - Just Scaffolded)\n- **Framework:** Expo Router with React Native\n- **Status:** Newly created (Feb 17, 2026)\n- **Features Implemented:** 26 core features scaffolded and passing:\n  - **Auth:** Sign In, Sign Up, Forgot Password screens with SecureStore persistence\n  - **Letter Creation:** AI generation screen, voice-to-letter dictation, template browser\n  - **Send Flow:** Product selection, recipient picker, handwriting styles, Thanks.io integration\n  - **Recipients:** List with search, add form, delete functionality\n  - **Orders:** History list, status refresh capability\n  - **Settings:** Account profile, theme switcher, sign out\n  - **Navigation:** Tab navigation (5 tabs), modal stack, splash screen\n  - **Services:** Full Supabase, Thanks.io, OpenAI clients, CRUD API service\n- **Tests:** 5 live integration tests defined (not yet passing)\n- **Version:** 1.0.0\n\n---\n\n### Tech Stack\n\n#### Frontend (Web)\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Framework | Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript |\n| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui |\n| Icons | Lucide React |\n\n#### Frontend (iOS)\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| Framework | Expo Router (React Native) |\n| Package Manager | npm |\n| State Management | Zustand |\n| UI Framework | React Native with Lucide icons |\n| Permissions | expo-av (audio), expo-image-picker (photos), expo-secure-store (secure storage) |\n\n#### Backend & Services\n| Service | Technology |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Database | PostgreSQL (Supabase) |\n| ORM | Prisma |\n| Auth | Supabase Auth |\n| Storage | Supabase Storage |\n| AI | OpenAI (GPT-4o, Whisper, DALL-E 3) |\n| Mail API | Thanks.io |\n| Payments | Stripe |\n| Deployment | Vercel |\n| Analytics | PostHog, Meta Pixel |\n| Error Tracking | Sentry |\n\n---\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\n/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/\n├── src/                          # Main web app (Next.js)\n│   ├── app/                      # Next.js App Router\n│   │   ├── actions/              # Server actions (database operations)\n│   │   ├── api/                  # API routes\n│   │   ├── (auth)/               # Auth pages\n│   │   ├── dashboard/            # Dashboard\n│   │   ├── generate/             # Letter generation\n│   │   ├── send/                 # Send letter flow\n│   │   ├── recipients/           # Address book\n│   │   ├── templates/            # Template management\n│   │   ├── orders/               # Order history\n│   │   └── billing/              # Subscription management\n│   ├── components/               # React components\n│   ├── lib/                      # Utilities & API clients\n│   │   ├── thanks-io.ts\n│   │   ├── openai.ts\n│   │   ├── stripe.ts\n│   │   ├── usage.ts\n│   │   └── tiers.ts\n│   └── contexts/                 # React contexts\n├── ios/                          # NEW iOS app (Expo Router)\n│   ├── app/                      # Routes\n│   │   ├── (auth)/               # Auth screens\n│   │   ├── (tabs)/               # Main app tabs\n│   │   ├── _layout.tsx           # Root layout\n│   │   ├── send.tsx              # Send flow\n│   │   ├── add-recipient.tsx     # Add recipient form\n│   │   └── voice-recorder.tsx    # Voice recording\n│   ├── services/                 # API clients\n│   │   ├── api.ts                # Supabase CRUD\n│   │   ├── supabase.ts           # Supabase client\n│   │   ├── thanks-io.ts          # Thanks.io client\n│   │   └── openai.ts             # OpenAI client\n│   ├── providers/                # Context providers\n│   ├── constants/                # App constants\n│   ├── tests/                    # Live integration tests\n│   └── package.json\n├── prisma/                       # Database schema\n├── tests/                        # Web app tests (48+ files)\n├── scripts/                      # Utility scripts\n├── docs/                         # Documentation\n└── [Multiple PRD docs and guides]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Features Completed\n\n#### Core Functionality (All Phases 1-5)\n- **Letter Generation:** OpenAI GPT-4o with tone/occasion selection\n- **Voice Input:** Whisper transcription with browser recording\n- **Image Generation:** DALL-E 3 (4 images per request)\n- **Recipient Management:** Full CRUD, address extraction, bulk import\n- **Templates:** Create, save, reuse with variables\n- **Mail Products:** Postcards, letters, greeting cards, windowless letters\n- **Order Management:** Track status, webhook updates from Thanks.io\n- **Subscriptions:** Stripe integration with Free/Pro/Business tiers\n- **Usage Tracking:** Enforce tier-based limits\n- **Dashboard:** Analytics and recent orders\n\n#### Mobile (Phase 6 - In Progress)\n- **iOS App:** Fully scaffolded with all core features\n- **Navigation:** 5-tab layout with modal presentations\n- **Authentication:** Secure session persistence with SecureStore\n- **Live Tests:** Infrastructure for Thanks.io integration testing\n\n---\n\n### Important Documentation Files\n\n| Document | Purpose | Location |\n|----------|---------|----------|\n| `README.md` | Main project overview | /KindLetters/README.md |\n| `PRD_STEADYLETTERS.md` | Product requirements (139 features) | /KindLetters/ |\n| `DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md` | Complete developer guide | /KindLetters/ |\n| `SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md` | Full technical architecture | /KindLetters/ |\n| `QUICK_START.md` | Setup instructions | /KindLetters/ |\n| `TESTING_CHECKLIST.md` | Comprehensive test guide | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_MOBILE_OPTIMIZATION.md` | Mobile design requirements | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_SECURITY_HARDENING.md` | Security requirements | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_OBSERVABILITY.md` | Monitoring & analytics | /KindLetters/ |\n| `THANKS_IO_API_REFERENCE.md` | Mail API documentation | /KindLetters/ |\n\n---\n\n### Database Schema (Prisma)\n\n**Core Models:**\n- `User` - User accounts with Stripe fields\n- `UserUsage` - Usage tracking (letterGenerations, imageGenerations, tier)\n- `Recipient` - Address book entries\n- `Template` - Saved letter templates\n- `Order` - Order records with Thanks.io integration\n- `MailOrder` - Detailed mail orders (product type, cost)\n- `Event` - Analytics events\n\n**Location:** `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/prisma/schema.prisma`\n\n---\n\n### Subscription Tiers\n\n| Tier | Price | Letters/Month | Images/Month | Features |\n|------|-------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| **Free** | $0 | 5-10 | 3-5 | Postcards only |\n| **Pro** | $29 | 50-100 | 25-50 | + Letters, Greeting Cards |\n| **Business** | $99 | Unlimited | 100+ | + Windowless, API access |\n\n---\n\n### Environment Variables Required\n\n**Web App:**\n```\nDATABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\nOPENAI_API_KEY, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, THANKS_IO_API_KEY\n```\n\n**iOS App:**\n```\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY, EXPO_PUBLIC_THANKS_IO_API_KEY\n```\n\n---\n\n### Recent Development History (Last 30 Commits)\n\n1. **Feb 17, 2026:** `feat: scaffold SteadyLetters iOS Expo Router app` - Full iOS app scaffolded with all screens\n2. **Recent:** Comprehensive Thanks.io live testing improvements\n3. **Recent:** Phase 9 Live API Testing (LIVE-TEST-001 to LIVE-TEST-015) completed\n4. **Completed:** Features SL-099 through SL-115 (international support, QR codes, photos, etc.)\n5. **Completed:** Phase 5 - All core features implemented\n\n---\n\n### Git Worktrees\n\n- **001-complete-phase2** - Feature branch for Phase 2 completion work\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps / Known Issues\n\n**Priority 1 (Mobile):**\n- Complete iOS live API integration tests\n- Test end-to-end sending flow\n- Optimize performance for iOS\n\n**Priority 2 (Security):**\n- Add Thanks.io webhook signature verification\n- Rate limiting implementation\n- Security headers\n\n**Priority 3 (Polish):**\n- Mobile hamburger menu refinement\n- Touch-friendly UI improvements\n- Email notifications\n\n---\n\n### Key Files to Know\n\n**Web App Entry Points:**\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/_layout.tsx` - Root layout\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/(tabs)` - Main tab pages\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/api` - All API routes\n\n**iOS App Entry Points:**\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx` - Root layout\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)` - Main tabs (index, recipients, templates, orders, settings)\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services` - API clients (thanks-io.ts, openai.ts, api.ts, supabase.ts)\n\n---\n\n### External Services Dashboards\n\n- Vercel: https://vercel.com/dashboard\n- Supabase: https://supabase.com/dashboard\n- Stripe: https://dashboard.stripe.com\n- OpenAI: https://platform.openai.com\n- Thanks.io: https://thanks.io/dashboard\n\n---\n\nThis is a mature, feature-complete SaaS product with comprehensive documentation, extensive testing infrastructure, and a newly added mobile app built with Expo Router. The web app has reached 100% of 139 planned features, and the iOS app is freshly scaffolded with all core UI and service layers in place."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: afb8b4d (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"207fe51e-5b7c-454d-9c4c-cd6fffc3315e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the parent directory /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters to understand the broader project context. Look for:\n1. README files\n2. Any project description or specification documents\n3. Other directories/worktrees\n4. Any feature lists, requirements docs, or planning documents\n5. The git log for recent commits to understand what's been built\n\nRead any README.md, docs, or specification files you find.","agentId":"afb8b4d","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive report based on all the information I've gathered. Let me create a final summary document:\n\n## Comprehensive Project Context Report\n\nBased on my exploration of the KindLetters project, here's the complete picture:\n\n### Project Overview\n\n**SteadyLetters** (formerly KindLetters) is a SaaS web application that enables users to create and send physical handwritten-style letters via the Thanks.io API. The project consists of:\n\n1. **Main Web Application** - Next.js 16 with React 19 and TypeScript\n2. **iOS Mobile App** - Recently scaffolded using Expo Router (React Native)\n3. **Supporting Backend Services** - Express backend service\n\n---\n\n### Current Status Su