    # App constants\n│   ├── tests/                    # Live integration tests\n│   └── package.json\n├── prisma/                       # Database schema\n├── tests/                        # Web app tests (48+ files)\n├── scripts/                      # Utility scripts\n├── docs/                         # Documentation\n└── [Multiple PRD docs and guides]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Key Features Completed\n\n#### Core Functionality (All Phases 1-5)\n- **Letter Generation:** OpenAI GPT-4o with tone/occasion selection\n- **Voice Input:** Whisper transcription with browser recording\n- **Image Generation:** DALL-E 3 (4 images per request)\n- **Recipient Management:** Full CRUD, address extraction, bulk import\n- **Templates:** Create, save, reuse with variables\n- **Mail Products:** Postcards, letters, greeting cards, windowless letters\n- **Order Management:** Track status, webhook updates from Thanks.io\n- **Subscriptions:** Stripe integration with Free/Pro/Business tiers\n- **Usage Tracking:** Enforce tier-based limits\n- **Dashboard:** Analytics and recent orders\n\n#### Mobile (Phase 6 - In Progress)\n- **iOS App:** Fully scaffolded with all core features\n- **Navigation:** 5-tab layout with modal presentations\n- **Authentication:** Secure session persistence with SecureStore\n- **Live Tests:** Infrastructure for Thanks.io integration testing\n\n---\n\n### Important Documentation Files\n\n| Document | Purpose | Location |\n|----------|---------|----------|\n| `README.md` | Main project overview | /KindLetters/README.md |\n| `PRD_STEADYLETTERS.md` | Product requirements (139 features) | /KindLetters/ |\n| `DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md` | Complete developer guide | /KindLetters/ |\n| `SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md` | Full technical architecture | /KindLetters/ |\n| `QUICK_START.md` | Setup instructions | /KindLetters/ |\n| `TESTING_CHECKLIST.md` | Comprehensive test guide | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_MOBILE_OPTIMIZATION.md` | Mobile design requirements | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_SECURITY_HARDENING.md` | Security requirements | /KindLetters/ |\n| `PRD_OBSERVABILITY.md` | Monitoring & analytics | /KindLetters/ |\n| `THANKS_IO_API_REFERENCE.md` | Mail API documentation | /KindLetters/ |\n\n---\n\n### Database Schema (Prisma)\n\n**Core Models:**\n- `User` - User accounts with Stripe fields\n- `UserUsage` - Usage tracking (letterGenerations, imageGenerations, tier)\n- `Recipient` - Address book entries\n- `Template` - Saved letter templates\n- `Order` - Order records with Thanks.io integration\n- `MailOrder` - Detailed mail orders (product type, cost)\n- `Event` - Analytics events\n\n**Location:** `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/prisma/schema.prisma`\n\n---\n\n### Subscription Tiers\n\n| Tier | Price | Letters/Month | Images/Month | Features |\n|------|-------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| **Free** | $0 | 5-10 | 3-5 | Postcards only |\n| **Pro** | $29 | 50-100 | 25-50 | + Letters, Greeting Cards |\n| **Business** | $99 | Unlimited | 100+ | + Windowless, API access |\n\n---\n\n### Environment Variables Required\n\n**Web App:**\n```\nDATABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\nOPENAI_API_KEY, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, THANKS_IO_API_KEY\n```\n\n**iOS App:**\n```\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY, EXPO_PUBLIC_THANKS_IO_API_KEY\n```\n\n---\n\n### Recent Development History (Last 30 Commits)\n\n1. **Feb 17, 2026:** `feat: scaffold SteadyLetters iOS Expo Router app` - Full iOS app scaffolded with all screens\n2. **Recent:** Comprehensive Thanks.io live testing improvements\n3. **Recent:** Phase 9 Live API Testing (LIVE-TEST-001 to LIVE-TEST-015) completed\n4. **Completed:** Features SL-099 through SL-115 (international support, QR codes, photos, etc.)\n5. **Completed:** Phase 5 - All core features implemented\n\n---\n\n### Git Worktrees\n\n- **001-complete-phase2** - Feature branch for Phase 2 completion work\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps / Known Issues\n\n**Priority 1 (Mobile):**\n- Complete iOS live API integration tests\n- Test end-to-end sending flow\n- Optimize performance for iOS\n\n**Priority 2 (Security):**\n- Add Thanks.io webhook signature verification\n- Rate limiting implementation\n- Security headers\n\n**Priority 3 (Polish):**\n- Mobile hamburger menu refinement\n- Touch-friendly UI improvements\n- Email notifications\n\n---\n\n### Key Files to Know\n\n**Web App Entry Points:**\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/_layout.tsx` - Root layout\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/(tabs)` - Main tab pages\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/src/app/api` - All API routes\n\n**iOS App Entry Points:**\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx` - Root layout\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)` - Main tabs (index, recipients, templates, orders, settings)\n- `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services` - API clients (thanks-io.ts, openai.ts, api.ts, supabase.ts)\n\n---\n\n### External Services Dashboards\n\n- Vercel: https://vercel.com/dashboard\n- Supabase: https://supabase.com/dashboard\n- Stripe: https://dashboard.stripe.com\n- OpenAI: https://platform.openai.com\n- Thanks.io: https://thanks.io/dashboard\n\n---\n\nThis is a mature, feature-complete SaaS product with comprehensive documentation, extensive testing infrastructure, and a newly added mobile app built with Expo Router. The web app has reached 100% of 139 planned features, and the iOS app is freshly scaffolded with all core UI and service layers in place."}],"totalDurationMs":47803,"totalTokens":50137,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5432,"cache_read_input_tokens":41715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5432},"output_tokens":2983,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019vJMKEcsvNCpXDUitC4Wta","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document. Based on my thorough exploration, I'll provide a detailed analysis of the codebase.\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE CODEBASE EXPLORATION REPORT\n\n### 1. PROJECT TYPE & FRAMEWORK\n\n**SteadyLetters iOS** is a **React Native + Expo** application built with:\n- **Framework**: Expo with Expo Router (file-based routing)\n- **Language**: TypeScript\n- **Target Platforms**: iOS, Android, Web\n- **Package Manager**: npm\n\n### 2. COMPLETE DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/\n├── app/\n│   ├── (auth)/                          # Authentication screens (stack navigator)\n│   │   ├── _layout.tsx                  # Auth stack configuration\n│   │   ├── sign-in.tsx                  # Email/password sign-in\n│   │   ├── sign-up.tsx                  # Account creation with email verification\n│   │   └── forgot-password.tsx          # Password reset via email\n│   ├── (tabs)/                          # Main tabbed interface (5 tabs)\n│   │   ├── _layout.tsx                  # Tab navigation configuration\n│   │   ├── index.tsx                    # Create tab - AI letter generation\n│   │   ├── recipients.tsx               # Recipients tab - address book\n│   │   ├── templates.tsx                # Templates tab - saved letter templates\n│   │   ├── orders.tsx                   # Orders tab - letter delivery tracking\n│   │   └── settings.tsx                 # Settings tab - profile & preferences\n│   ├── _layout.tsx                      # Root layout with providers\n│   ├── send.tsx                         # Send flow modal - product/recipient/style selection\n│   ├── voice-recorder.tsx               # Voice-to-text modal - audio recording & transcription\n│   └── add-recipient.tsx                # Add recipient modal - new address form\n├── constants/\n│   ├── colors.ts                        # Light/dark theme color palettes\n│   ├── config.ts                        # API keys, tier configurations\n│   └── typography.ts                    # Font/text styling (likely)\n├── providers/\n│   ├── AuthProvider.tsx                 # React Context for authentication state\n│   └── ThemeProvider.tsx                # React Context for light/dark mode\n├── services/\n│   ├── supabase.ts                      # Supabase client with SecureStore integration\n│   ├── api.ts                           # CRUD operations (recipients, orders, templates, usage)\n│   ├── thanks-io.ts                     # Thanks.io API client (send physical mail)\n│   └── openai.ts                        # OpenAI integrations (GPT-4o, Whisper, DALL-E)\n├── tests/\n│   └── live/\n│       ├── config.ts                    # Live test configuration\n│       ├── jest.config.ts               # Jest configuration for live tests\n│       ├── send-postcard.test.ts        # Real postcard sending integration test\n│       ├── send-letter.test.ts          # Real letter sending integration test\n│       └── send-greeting-card.test.ts   # Real greeting card sending integration test\n├── package.json                          # Dependencies and scripts\n├── app.json                              # Expo configuration\n├── tsconfig.json                         # TypeScript configuration\n├── .env.example                          # Environment variables template\n├── .gitignore                            # Git ignore rules\n└── feature_list.json                     # Feature tracking (139 features)\n```\n\n### 3. PROJECT PURPOSE & CORE FEATURES\n\n**SteadyLetters** is an iOS app that allows users to:\n- **Generate AI-powered handwritten letters** using GPT-4o with customizable tone/occasion\n- **Send physical mail** (postcards, letters, greeting cards) via Thanks.io integration\n- **Manage recipients** in an address book\n- **Record and transcribe voice** into letter content using OpenAI Whisper\n- **Save letter templates** for reuse\n- **Track sent orders** with real-time delivery status\n- **Manage subscription tiers** (Free, Pro, Business)\n\n### 4. CONFIGURATION FILES\n\n#### **package.json**\n- **Dependencies**: React Native 0.76, Expo 52, React 18.3.1\n- **Key Libraries**:\n  - `expo-router`: File-based navigation\n  - `@supabase/supabase-js`: Backend authentication & database\n  - `expo-av`: Audio recording/playback\n  - `expo-secure-store`: Secure token storage\n  - `react-native-purchases`: RevenueCat for subscriptions\n  - `@stripe/stripe-react-native`: Stripe payments\n  - `lucide-react-native`: Icon library\n  - `zustand`: State management\n  - `posthog-react-native`: Analytics\n- **Scripts**:\n  - `npm start`: Start Expo dev server\n  - `npm run ios/android/web`: Run on platform\n  - `npm test`: Run Jest tests\n  - `npm run test:live`: Run integration tests with real Thanks.io API\n\n#### **app.json** (Expo Configuration)\n- **App Name**: SteadyLetters\n- **iOS Bundle ID**: com.steadyletters.app\n- **Android Package**: com.steadyletters.app\n- **Permissions**:\n  - Microphone (voice-to-letter recording)\n  - Camera (photo capture for letters)\n  - Photo Library (image selection)\n- **Plugins**:\n  - expo-router, expo-secure-store, expo-av, expo-image-picker\n  - Typed Routes enabled\n\n#### **tsconfig.json**\n- Extends `expo/tsconfig.base`\n- Strict mode enabled\n- Path aliases: `@/*` maps to current directory\n\n#### **.env.example**\nRequired environment variables:\n```\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_THANKS_IO_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST\nEXPO_PUBLIC_APP_URL\nEXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUCAT_API_KEY\n```\n\n### 5. SCREENS & PAGES (COMPLETE LIST)\n\n#### Authentication Stack\n- **sign-in.tsx**: Email/password login with forgot password link\n- **sign-up.tsx**: Account creation with password confirmation & validation\n- **forgot-password.tsx**: Password reset via email\n\n#### Tab Navigation (Main App - 5 tabs)\n1. **Create (index.tsx)**\n   - AI letter generation with GPT-4o\n   - Options: Occasion (8 types), Tone (5 types), Key Points, Recipient Context\n   - Generates 3 letter variations\n   - Send to letter directly from selection\n\n2. **Recipients (recipients.tsx)**\n   - Address book with search\n   - Display: Name, Address, City, State, ZIP\n   - Add/delete recipients\n   - Swipe-to-delete functionality\n\n3. **Templates (templates.tsx)**\n   - Browse saved letter templates\n   - Filter by occasion/tone\n   - Tap to prefill create screen\n   - System templates + user templates\n\n4. **Orders (orders.tsx)**\n   - View sent order history\n   - Status tracking: Queued, Processing, Sent, Delivered, Failed\n   - Pull-to-refresh\n   - Cost display\n   - Date/recipient info\n\n5. **Settings (settings.tsx)**\n   - Profile (email display)\n   - Theme toggle (Light/Dark/System)\n   - Subscription management\n   - Notifications\n   - Privacy/Help sections\n   - Sign out\n\n#### Modal Screens\n- **send.tsx**: Complete send flow\n  - Product type selection (postcard, letter, greeting card)\n  - Recipient dropdown selector\n  - Handwriting style selection (6 styles from Thanks.io)\n  - Message editor\n  - Price display\n  - Send confirmation dialog\n\n- **voice-recorder.tsx**: Voice-to-letter conversion\n  - Audio recording with timer\n  - Playback controls\n  - OpenAI Whisper transcription\n  - Pass transcription to create screen\n\n- **add-recipient.tsx**: New address entry\n  - Full form: Name, Address, Address2, City, State, ZIP, Country\n  - Validation before save\n  - Modal presentation\n\n### 6. SERVICES & API INTEGRATIONS\n\n#### **supabase.ts** - Backend Infrastructure\n- Supabase JS client initialization\n- SecureStore adapter for session persistence\n- Auto-refresh tokens enabled\n- Connection pooling configured\n\n#### **api.ts** - Database CRUD Operations\n**Recipients Management**:\n- `getRecipients()`: Fetch user's address book\n- `createRecipient()`: Add new recipient\n- `updateRecipient()`: Edit recipient\n- `deleteRecipient()`: Remove recipient\n\n**Orders Management**:\n- `getOrders()`: Fetch sent order history\n- `createOrder()`: Save order after sending\n\n**Templates**:\n- `getTemplates()`: Fetch user + system templates\n- `saveTemplate()`: Save generated letter as template\n\n**Usage Tracking**:\n- `getUsageStats()`: Fetch user's letter/image generation counts\n- `incrementUsage()`: Track letters sent, generations, etc.\n\n#### **thanks-io.ts** - Physical Mail API\n**Send Functions**:\n- `sendPostcard()`: Send 4x6, 6x9, or 6x11 postcards ($1.14-$1.83)\n- `sendLetter()`: Send windowed letter ($1.20)\n- `sendGreetingCard()`: Send premium greeting card ($3.00)\n- `sendWindowlessLetter()`: Send PDF-based letter ($2.52)\n\n**Configuration**:\n- Handwriting styles (supports 6+ styles)\n- Handwriting colors (blue, black, green, purple, red)\n- Product catalog with pricing tiers\n\n**Status Tracking**:\n- `getHandwritingStyles()`: Fetch available handwriting styles\n- `getOrderStatus()`: Check delivery status of order\n\n#### **openai.ts** - AI & Audio Services\n**Letter Generation**:\n- `generateLetter()`: GPT-4o generates 3 letter variations\n  - Parameters: occasion, tone, keyPoints, recipientContext, senderName\n  - Configurable occasions: thank_you, birthday, congratulations, thinking_of_you, sympathy, holiday, business, custom\n  - Tones: warm, professional, casual, formal, heartfelt\n\n**Image Generation**:\n- `generateImages()`: DALL-E 3 for card front images\n\n**Audio Transcription**:\n- `transcribeAudio()`: OpenAI Whisper for voice-to-text (m4a format)\n\n**Address Extraction**:\n- `extractAddress()`: Parse text into structured mailing address\n\n### 7. PROVIDERS & CONTEXT STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n#### **AuthProvider.tsx**\n- **State**: session, user, isLoading\n- **Methods**:\n  - `signIn(email, password)`: Supabase email auth\n  - `signUp(email, password, fullName)`: Account creation\n  - `signOut()`: Logout\n  - `resetPassword(email)`: Password reset\n- **Hooks**: `useAuth()` for consuming auth context\n- **Session Persistence**: Uses expo-secure-store for token storage\n\n#### **ThemeProvider.tsx**\n- **State**: theme (light/dark/system), colors, isDark\n- **Persistence**: SecureStore persists theme preference\n- **Reactive**: Uses `useColorScheme()` for system theme detection\n- **Colors**: Full light/dark palette with 20+ semantic color tokens\n- **Hook**: `useTheme()` for consuming theme context\n\n### 8. EXISTING TESTS\n\n#### Live Integration Tests (3 files)\n- **send-postcard.test.ts**: \n  - Real postcard sending via Thanks.io API\n  - Retrieves handwriting styles\n  - Checks order status\n  - Requires: `THANKS_IO_LIVE_TEST=true`\n\n- **send-letter.test.ts**:\n  - Real letter sending integration test\n  - Similar structure to postcard test\n\n- **send-greeting-card.test.ts**:\n  - Real greeting card sending integration test\n\n**Test Configuration** (config.ts):\n- Smoke, Standard, Full test profiles\n- Max spend limit ($15 default)\n- Configurable recipient address\n- Environment-based settings\n\n**Run Tests**:\n```bash\nnpm run test:live                    # Standard profile\nnpm run test:live:smoke             # Smoke test (subset)\nnpm run test:live:standard          # Standard profile\nnpm run test:live:full              # Full test suite\n```\n\n### 9. INSTALLED DEPENDENCIES\n\n#### Core Dependencies (19 total)\n- **React Native Ecosystem**: react-native@0.76, react@18.3.1, expo@52\n- **Navigation**: expo-router@4.0.0\n- **Backend**: @supabase/supabase-js@2.84.0\n- **Media**: expo-av@15, expo-image-picker@16, expo-image@2\n- **Secure Storage**: expo-secure-store@14, expo-crypto@14\n- **File System**: expo-file-system@18\n- **Permissions**: expo-auth-session@6\n- **UI**: lucide-react-native@0.469, expo-vector-icons@14\n- **State**: zustand@5\n- **Payments**: react-native-purchases@8, @stripe/stripe-react-native@0.38\n- **Analytics**: posthog-react-native@3\n- **Animations**: react-native-reanimated@3.16\n- **Navigation**: react-native-gesture-handler@2.20, react-native-screens@4.1, react-native-safe-area-context@4.12\n- **Graphics**: react-native-svg@15.8\n\n#### Dev Dependencies (6 total)\n- TypeScript@5.3\n- Jest@29.7 with ts-jest@29.1\n- jest-expo@52\n- @types/react@18.3, @types/jest@29.5\n- @babel/core@7.25\n\n### 10. APP'S PURPOSE & BUSINESS MODEL\n\n**Core Value Proposition**:\nSteadyLetters bridges physical and digital communication by allowing users to send personalized handwritten letters from their phones.\n\n**Key Features**:\n- AI-powered letter writing (removes writer's block)\n- Voice dictation (hands-free composition)\n- Physical mail delivery (authentic, memorable)\n- Template reuse (consistency for businesses)\n- Real-time tracking (delivery visibility)\n\n**Business Model**:\nThree-tier SaaS subscription:\n- **Free**: 5 letter generations, 2 letters sent, postcards only\n- **Pro** ($29/mo): 50 generations, 20 sent, postcards/letters/greeting cards\n- **Business** ($99/mo): Unlimited, all products including windowless letters/gift cards\n\n**Revenue Streams**:\n1. Subscription revenue (via RevenueCat)\n2. Per-letter fees (Thanks.io fulfillment)\n3. Stripe payment processing\n\n### 11. FEATURE COMPLETION STATUS\n\n**Implemented Features** (27/43 passing):\n- All authentication (sign-in, sign-up, password reset, protected routes)\n- All letter generation & voice transcription\n- All send flows (product selection, recipient picker, handwriting styles)\n- All recipient management\n- All order tracking & status\n- All template browsing\n- All theme/settings UI\n- Live Thanks.io API integration\n- Supabase authentication & database\n\n**Not Yet Implemented** (16 failing):\n- Live tests (need API credentials)\n- RevenueCat subscription integration\n- PostHog analytics\n- Push notifications\n- Error boundaries & loading skeletons\n- Haptic feedback\n- Empty state illustrations\n- Keyboard avoidance optimization\n\n### 12. SUMMARY OF KEY FILES\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/app/_layout.tsx` | Root layout with auth/theme providers |\n| `/app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` | Tab navigation structure |\n| `/app/(tabs)/index.tsx` | AI letter generation UI |\n| `/app/send.tsx` | Send flow (product/recipient/style) |\n| `/providers/AuthProvider.tsx` | Authentication state management |\n| `/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx` | Theme state management |\n| `/services/api.ts` | Supabase CRUD operations |\n| `/services/thanks-io.ts` | Physical mail API client |\n| `/services/openai.ts` | AI/audio services |\n| `/services/supabase.ts` | Supabase client initialization |\n| `/constants/config.ts` | API keys & tier configuration |\n| `/constants/colors.ts` | Light/dark theme colors |\n| `/tests/live/send-postcard.test.ts` | Integration test example |\n\nThis is a **production-ready, feature-rich iOS application** with comprehensive API integrations, proper state management, and a clear business model. The codebase demonstrates professional React Native development practices with Expo, TypeScript, and modern architectural patterns."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa50243 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"76d2caee-3cae-4094-8860-1886f4bd19b8","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Do a very thorough exploration of the codebase at /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios. I need to understand:\n\n1. What kind of project is this? (React Native, Expo, Swift, etc.)\n2. What is the complete directory structure?\n3. What features are already implemented?\n4. What configuration files exist (package.json, app.json, tsconfig, etc.)?\n5. What screens/pages exist?\n6. What services/API integrations exist?\n7. What providers/context exist?\n8. What is the app's purpose based on the code?\n9. Are there existing tests?\n10. What dependencies are installed?\n\nList out ALL files and directories, read key configuration files and source files to understand the full scope.","agentId":"aa50243","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document. Based on my thorough exploration, I'll provide a detailed analysis of the codebase.\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE CODEBASE EXPLORATION REPORT\n\n### 1. PROJECT TYPE & FRAMEWORK\n\n**SteadyLetters iOS** is a **React Native + Expo** application built with:\n- **Framework**: Expo with Expo Router (file-based routing)\n- **Language**: TypeScript\n- **Target Platforms**: iOS, Android, Web\n- **Package Manager**: npm\n\n### 2. COMPLETE DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/\n├── app/\n│   ├── (auth)/                          # Authentication screens (stack navigator)\n│   │   ├── _layout.tsx                  # Auth stack configuration\n│   │   ├── sign-in.tsx                  # Email/password sign-in\n│   │   ├── sign-up.tsx                  # Account creation with email verification\n│   │   └── forgot-password.tsx          # Password reset via email\n│   ├── (tabs)/                          # Main tabbed interface (5 tabs)\n│   │   ├── _layout.tsx                  # Tab navigation configuration\n│   │   ├── index.tsx                    # Create tab - AI letter generation\n│   │   ├── recipients.tsx               # Recipients tab - address book\n│   │   ├── templates.tsx                # Templates tab - saved letter templates\n│   │   ├── orders.tsx                   # Orders tab - letter delivery tracking\n│   │   └── settings.tsx                 # Settings tab - profile & preferences\n│   ├── _layout.tsx                      # Root layout with providers\n│   ├── send.tsx                         # Send flow modal - product/recipient/style selection\n│   ├── voice-recorder.tsx               # Voice-to-text modal - audio recording & transcription\n│   └── add-recipient.tsx                # Add recipient modal - new address form\n├── constants/\n│   ├── colors.ts                        # Light/dark theme color palettes\n│   ├── config.ts                        # API keys, tier configurations\n│   └── typography.ts                    # Font/text styling (likely)\n├── providers/\n│   ├── AuthProvider.tsx                 # React Context for authentication state\n│   └── ThemeProvider.tsx                # React Context for light/dark mode\n├── services/\n│   ├── supabase.ts                      # Supabase client with SecureStore integration\n│   ├── api.ts                           # CRUD operations (recipients, orders, templates, usage)\n│   ├── thanks-io.ts                     # Thanks.io API client (send physical mail)\n│   └── openai.ts                        # OpenAI integrations (GPT-4o, Whisper, DALL-E)\n├── tests/\n│   └── live/\n│       ├── config.ts                    # Live test configuration\n│       ├── jest.config.ts               # Jest configuration for live tests\n│       ├── send-postcard.test.ts        # Real postcard sending integration test\n│       ├── send-letter.test.ts          # Real letter sending integration test\n│       └── send-greeting-card.test.ts   # Real greeting card sending integration test\n├── package.json                          # Dependencies and scripts\n├── app.json                              # Expo configuration\n├── tsconfig.json                         # TypeScript configuration\n├── .env.example                          # Environment variables template\n├── .gitignore                            # Git ignore rules\n└── feature_list.json                     # Feature tracking (139 features)\n```\n\n### 3. PROJECT PURPOSE & CORE FEATURES\n\n**SteadyLetters** is an iOS app that allows users to:\n- **Generate AI-powered handwritten letters** using GPT-4o with customizable tone/occasion\n- **Send physical mail** (postcards, letters, greeting cards) via Thanks.io integration\n- **Manage recipients** in an address book\n- **Record and transcribe voice** into letter content using OpenAI Whisper\n- **Save letter templates** for reuse\n- **Track sent orders** with real-time delivery status\n- **Manage subscription tiers** (Free, Pro, Business)\n\n### 4. CONFIGURATION FILES\n\n#### **package.json**\n- **Dependencies**: React Native 0.76, Expo 52, React 18.3.1\n- **Key Libraries**:\n  - `expo-router`: File-based navigation\n  - `@supabase/supabase-js`: Backend authentication & database\n  - `expo-av`: Audio recording/playback\n  - `expo-secure-store`: Secure token storage\n  - `react-native-purchases`: RevenueCat for subscriptions\n  - `@stripe/stripe-react-native`: Stripe payments\n  - `lucide-react-native`: Icon library\n  - `zustand`: State management\n  - `posthog-react-native`: Analytics\n- **Scripts**:\n  - `npm start`: Start Expo dev server\n  - `npm run ios/android/web`: Run on platform\n  - `npm test`: Run Jest tests\n  - `npm run test:live`: Run integration tests with real Thanks.io API\n\n#### **app.json** (Expo Configuration)\n- **App Name**: SteadyLetters\n- **iOS Bundle ID**: com.steadyletters.app\n- **Android Package**: com.steadyletters.app\n- **Permissions**:\n  - Microphone (voice-to-letter recording)\n  - Camera (photo capture for letters)\n  - Photo Library (image selection)\n- **Plugins**:\n  - expo-router, expo-secure-store, expo-av, expo-image-picker\n  - Typed Routes enabled\n\n#### **tsconfig.json**\n- Extends `expo/tsconfig.base`\n- Strict mode enabled\n- Path aliases: `@/*` maps to current directory\n\n#### **.env.example**\nRequired environment variables:\n```\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nEXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_THANKS_IO_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_API_KEY\nEXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST\nEXPO_PUBLIC_APP_URL\nEXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUCAT_API_KEY\n```\n\n### 5. SCREENS & PAGES (COMPLETE LIST)\n\n#### Authentication Stack\n- **sign-in.tsx**: Email/password login with forgot password link\n- **sign-up.tsx**: Account creation with password confirmation & validation\n- **forgot-password.tsx**: Password reset via email\n\n#### Tab Navigation (Main App - 5 tabs)\n1. **Create (index.tsx)**\n   - AI letter generation with GPT-4o\n   - Options: Occasion (8 types), Tone (5 types), Key Points, Recipient Context\n   - Generates 3 letter variations\n   - Send to letter directly from selection\n\n2. **Recipients (recipients.tsx)**\n   - Address book with search\n   - Display: Name, Address, City, State, ZIP\n   - Add/delete recipients\n   - Swipe-to-delete functionality\n\n3. **Templates (templates.tsx)**\n   - Browse saved letter templates\n   - Filter by occasion/tone\n   - Tap to prefill create screen\n   - System templates + user templates\n\n4. **Orders (orders.tsx)**\n   - View sent order history\n   - Status tracking: Queued, Processing, Sent, Delivered, Failed\n   - Pull-to-refresh\n   - Cost display\n   - Date/recipient info\n\n5. **Settings (settings.tsx)**\n   - Profile (email display)\n   - Theme toggle (Light/Dark/System)\n   - Subscription management\n   - Notifications\n   - Privacy/Help sections\n   - Sign out\n\n#### Modal Screens\n- **send.tsx**: Complete send flow\n  - Product type selection (postcard, letter, greeting card)\n  - Recipient dropdown selector\n  - Handwriting style selection (6 styles from Thanks.io)\n  - Message editor\n  - Price display\n  - Send confirmation dialog\n\n- **voice-recorder.tsx**: Voice-to-letter conversion\n  - Audio recording with timer\n  - Playback controls\n  - OpenAI Whisper transcription\n  - Pass transcription to create screen\n\n- **add-recipient.tsx**: New address entry\n  - Full form: Name, Address, Address2, City, State, ZIP, Country\n  - Validation before save\n  - Modal presentation\n\n### 6. SERVICES & API INTEGRATIONS\n\n#### **supabase.ts** - Backend Infrastructure\n- Supabase JS client initialization\n- SecureStore adapter for session persistence\n- Auto-refresh tokens enabled\n- Connection pooling configured\n\n#### **api.ts** - Database CRUD Operations\n**Recipients Management**:\n- `getRecipients()`: Fetch user's address book\n- `createRecipient()`: Add new recipient\n- `updateRecipient()`: Edit recipient\n- `deleteRecipient()`: Remove recipient\n\n**Orders Management**:\n- `getOrders()`: Fetch sent order history\n- `createOrder()`: Save order after sending\n\n**Templates**:\n- `getTemplates()`: Fetch user + system templates\n- `saveTemplate()`: Save generated letter as template\n\n**Usage Tracking**:\n- `getUsageStats()`: Fetch user's letter/image generation counts\n- `incrementUsage()`: Track letters sent, generations, etc.\n\n#### **thanks-io.ts** - Physical Mail API\n**Send Functions**:\n- `sendPostcard()`: Send 4x6, 6x9, or 6x11 postcards ($1.14-$1.83)\n- `sendLetter()`: Send windowed letter ($1.20)\n- `sendGreetingCard()`: Send premium greeting card ($3.00)\n- `sendWindowlessLetter()`: Send PDF-based letter ($2.52)\n\n**Configuration**:\n- Handwriting styles (supports 6+ styles)\n- Handwriting colors (blue, black, green, purple, red)\n- Product catalog with pricing tiers\n\n**Status Tracking**:\n- `getHandwritingStyles()`: Fetch available handwriting styles\n- `getOrderStatus()`: Check delivery status of order\n\n#### **openai.ts** - AI & Audio Services\n**Letter Generation**:\n- `generateLetter()`: GPT-4o generates 3 letter variations\n  - Parameters: occasion, tone, keyPoints, recipientContext, senderName\n  - Configurable occasions: thank_you, birthday, congratulations, thinking_of_you, sympathy, holiday, business, custom\n  - Tones: warm, professional, casual, formal, heartfelt\n\n**Image Generation**:\n- `generateImages()`: DALL-E 3 for card front images\n\n**Audio Transcription**:\n- `transcribeAudio()`: OpenAI Whisper for voice-to-text (m4a format)\n\n**Address Extraction**:\n- `extractAddress()`: Parse text into structured mailing address\n\n### 7. PROVIDERS & CONTEXT STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n#### **AuthProvider.tsx**\n- **State**: session, user, isLoading\n- **Methods**:\n  - `signIn(email, password)`: Supabase email auth\n  - `signUp(email, password, fullName)`: Account creation\n  - `signOut()`: Logout\n  - `resetPassword(email)`: Password reset\n- **Hooks**: `useAuth()` for consuming auth context\n- **Session Persistence**: Uses expo-secure-store for token storage\n\n#### **ThemeProvider.tsx**\n- **State**: theme (light/dark/system), colors, isDark\n- **Persistence**: SecureStore persists theme preference\n- **Reactive**: Uses `useColorScheme()` for system theme detection\n- **Colors**: Full light/dark palette with 20+ semantic color tokens\n- **Hook**: `useTheme()` for consuming theme context\n\n### 8. EXISTING TESTS\n\n#### Live Integration Tests (3 files)\n- **send-postcard.test.ts**: \n  - Real postcard sending via Thanks.io API\n  - Retrieves handwriting styles\n  - Checks order status\n  - Requires: `THANKS_IO_LIVE_TEST=true`\n\n- **send-letter.test.ts**:\n  - Real letter sending integration test\n  - Similar structure to postcard test\n\n- **send-greeting-card.test.ts**:\n  - Real greeting card sending integration test\n\n**Test Configuration** (config.ts):\n- Smoke, Standard, Full test profiles\n- Max spend limit ($15 default)\n- Configurable recipient address\n- Environment-based settings\n\n**Run Tests**:\n```bash\nnpm run test:live                    # Standard profile\nnpm run test:live:smoke             # Smoke test (subset)\nnpm run test:live:standard          # Standard profile\nnpm run test:live:full              # Full test suite\n```\n\n### 9. INSTALLED DEPENDENCIES\n\n#### Core Dependencies (19 total)\n- **React Native Ecosystem**: react-native@0.76, react@18.3.1, expo@52\n- **Navigation**: expo-router@4.0.0\n- **Backend**: @supabase/supabase-js@2.84.0\n- **Media**: expo-av@15, expo-image-picker@16, expo-image@2\n- **Secure Storage**: expo-secure-store@14, expo-crypto@14\n- **File System**: expo-file-system@18\n- **Permissions**: expo-auth-session@6\n- **UI**: lucide-react-native@0.469, expo-vector-icons@14\n- **State**: zustand@5\n- **Payments**: react-native-purchases@8, @stripe/stripe-react-native@0.38\n- **Analytics**: posthog-react-native@3\n- **Animations**: react-native-reanimated@3.16\n- **Navigation**: react-native-gesture-handler@2.20, react-native-screens@4.1, react-native-safe-area-context@4.12\n- **Graphics**: react-native-svg@15.8\n\n#### Dev Dependencies (6 total)\n- TypeScript@5.3\n- Jest@29.7 with ts-jest@29.1\n- jest-expo@52\n- @types/react@18.3, @types/jest@29.5\n- @babel/core@7.25\n\n### 10. APP'S PURPOSE & BUSINESS MODEL\n\n**Core Value Proposition**:\nSteadyLetters bridges physical and digital communication by allowing users to send personalized handwritten letters from their phones.\n\n**Key Features**:\n- AI-powered letter writing (removes writer's block)\n- Voice dictation (hands-free composition)\n- Physical mail delivery (authentic, memorable)\n- Template reuse (consistency for businesses)\n- Real-time tracking (delivery visibility)\n\n**Business Model**:\nThree-tier SaaS subscription:\n- **Free**: 5 letter generations, 2 letters sent, postcards only\n- **Pro** ($29/mo): 50 generations, 20 sent, postcards/letters/greeting cards\n- **Business** ($99/mo): Unlimited, all products including windowless letters/gift cards\n\n**Revenue Streams**:\n1. Subscription revenue (via RevenueCat)\n2. Per-letter fees (Thanks.io fulfillment)\n3. Stripe payment processing\n\n### 11. FEATURE COMPLETION STATUS\n\n**Implemented Features** (27/43 passing):\n- All authentication (sign-in, sign-up, password reset, protected routes)\n- All letter generation & voice transcription\n- All send flows (product selection, recipient picker, handwriting styles)\n- All recipient management\n- All order tracking & status\n- All template browsing\n- All theme/settings UI\n- Live Thanks.io API integration\n- Supabase authentication & database\n\n**Not Yet Implemented** (16 failing):\n- Live tests (need API credentials)\n- RevenueCat subscription integration\n- PostHog analytics\n- Push notifications\n- Error boundaries & loading skeletons\n- Haptic feedback\n- Empty state illustrations\n- Keyboard avoidance optimization\n\n### 12. SUMMARY OF KEY FILES\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/app/_layout.tsx` | Root layout with auth/theme providers |\n| `/app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` | Tab navigation structure |\n| `/app/(tabs)/index.tsx` | AI letter generation UI |\n| `/app/send.tsx` | Send flow (product/recipient/style) |\n| `/providers/AuthProvider.tsx` | Authentication state management |\n| `/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx` | Theme state management |\n| `/services/api.ts` | Supabase CRUD operations |\n| `/services/thanks-io.ts` | Physical mail API client |\n| `/services/openai.ts` | AI/audio services |\n| `/services/supabase.ts` | Supabase client initialization |\n| `/constants/config.ts` | API keys & tier configuration |\n| `/constants/colors.ts` | Light/dark theme colors |\n| `/tests/live/send-postcard.test.ts` | Integration test example |\n\nThis is a **production-ready, feature-rich iOS application** with comprehensive API integrations, proper state management, and a clear business model. The codebase demonstrates professional React Native development practices with Expo, TypeScript, and modern architectural patterns."}],"totalDurationMs":65873,"totalTokens":67599,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3255,"cache_read_input_tokens":60148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3255},"output_tokens":4192,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}}
