{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0128tppGXeqKeYjqgZNzNcBG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# 📱 PRD: Mobile Optimization for SteadyLetters\n     2→\n     3→**Document Version:** 1.0  \n     4→**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n     5→**Priority:** High  \n     6→**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 days\n     7→\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→## 📋 Overview\n    11→\n    12→### Problem Statement\n    13→The SteadyLetters web app currently has limited mobile responsiveness. The navigation menu doesn't collapse on mobile devices, touch targets may be too small, and the overall mobile experience needs improvement.\n    14→\n    15→### Goal\n    16→Make SteadyLetters fully mobile-optimized with an excellent user experience on phones and tablets.\n    17→\n    18→### Success Metrics\n    19→- [ ] 100% of pages render correctly on mobile (320px - 768px width)\n    20→- [ ] All interactive elements have minimum 44x44px touch targets\n    21→- [ ] Navigation works seamlessly on mobile with hamburger menu\n    22→- [ ] No horizontal scrolling on any page\n    23→- [ ] Lighthouse mobile score ≥ 90\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→## 🎯 Requirements\n    28→\n    29→### 1. Mobile Navigation (Navbar)\n    30→\n    31→**Current State:** Navigation links overflow on mobile screens.\n    32→\n    33→**Required Changes:**\n    34→\n    35→| Component | Change Required | File to Modify |\n    36→|-----------|----------------|----------------|\n    37→| Navbar | Add hamburger menu icon | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n    38→| Navbar | Create slide-out mobile menu panel | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n    39→| Navbar | Hide desktop links on mobile | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n    40→| Navbar | Add overlay when menu is open | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n    41→\n    42→**Implementation Details:**\n    43→```tsx\n    44→// Add state for mobile menu\n    45→const [mobileMenuOpen, setMobileMenuOpen] = useState(false);\n    46→\n    47→// Add hamburger button (visible on mobile only)\n    48→<button className=\"md:hidden\" onClick={() => setMobileMenuOpen(!mobileMenuOpen)}>\n    49→  <Menu className=\"h-6 w-6\" />\n    50→</button>\n    51→\n    52→// Add mobile menu panel (slides in from right)\n    53→<div className={`fixed top-16 right-0 h-full w-72 bg-background transform transition-transform ${mobileMenuOpen ? 'translate-x-0' : 'translate-x-full'}`}>\n    54→  {/* Navigation links */}\n    55→</div>\n    56→```\n    57→\n    58→**Dependencies:**\n    59→- `lucide-react` (already installed) - for Menu and X icons\n    60→\n    61→---\n    62→\n    63→### 2. Global Mobile CSS Utilities\n    64→\n    65→**Current State:** No mobile-specific utility classes.\n    66→\n    67→**Required Changes:**\n    68→\n    69→| Utility | Purpose | File to Modify |\n    70→|---------|---------|----------------|\n    71→| `.touch-target` | Ensure 44x44px minimum tap targets | `src/app/globals.css` |\n    72→| `.safe-area-inset` | Handle notched devices (iPhone X+) | `src/app/globals.css` |\n    73→| Input font fix | Prevent iOS zoom on input focus | `src/app/globals.css` |\n    74→| Scroll utilities | Smooth mobile scrolling | `src/app/globals.css` |\n    75→\n    76→**Implementation Details:**\n    77→```css\n    78→/* Add to globals.css */\n    79→@layer utilities {\n    80→  /* Touch-friendly tap targets */\n    81→  .touch-target {\n    82→    min-height: 44px;\n    83→    min-width: 44px;\n    84→  }\n    85→\n    86→  /* Prevent iOS zoom on input focus */\n    87→  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n    88→    input, select, textarea {\n    89→      font-size: 16px !important;\n    90→    }\n    91→  }\n    92→\n    93→  /* Safe area for notched devices */\n    94→  .safe-area-inset {\n    95→    padding-left: env(safe-area-inset-left);\n    96→    padding-right: env(safe-area-inset-right);\n    97→    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);\n    98→  }\n    99→}\n   100→```\n   101→\n   102→---\n   103→\n   104→### 3. Page-Specific Mobile Fixes\n   105→\n   106→#### 3.1 Homepage (`src/app/page.tsx`)\n   107→\n   108→| Element | Issue | Fix |\n   109→|---------|-------|-----|\n   110→| Hero text | May be too large on small screens | Add `text-3xl sm:text-5xl md:text-7xl` |\n   111→| CTA buttons | Stack on mobile | Already uses `flex-col sm:flex-row` ✅ |\n   112→| Feature grid | 4 columns too narrow on mobile | Already uses `md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4` ✅ |\n   113→\n   114→#### 3.2 Dashboard (`src/app/dashboard/page.tsx`)\n   115→\n   116→| Element | Issue | Fix |\n   117→|---------|-------|-----|\n   118→| Stats cards | Grid may need adjustment | Add `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3` |\n   119→| Table | Horizontal scroll on mobile | Wrap in `overflow-x-auto` container |\n   120→| Action button | May be hard to tap | Add `touch-target` class |\n   121→\n   122→#### 3.3 Generate Page (`src/app/generate/page.tsx`)\n   123→\n   124→| Element | Issue | Fix |\n   125→|---------|-------|-----|\n   126→| Voice recorder button | Must be large enough to tap | Ensure 44x44px minimum |\n   127→| Text input | Font size must be 16px | Apply mobile input fix |\n   128→| Image upload | Touch-friendly area | Add visual feedback on touch |\n   129→\n   130→#### 3.4 Send Page (`src/app/send/page.tsx`)\n   131→\n   132→| Element | Issue | Fix |\n   133→|---------|-------|-----|\n   134→| Form fields | Need proper spacing | Add `space-y-4` between fields |\n   135→| Submit button | Full width on mobile | Add `w-full sm:w-auto` |\n   136→\n   137→---\n   138→\n   139→### 4. Component Updates\n   140→\n   141→#### 4.1 Button Component (`src/components/ui/button.tsx`)\n   142→\n   143→**Check:** Ensure all button variants have adequate touch targets.\n   144→\n   145→```tsx\n   146→// Verify these classes exist for mobile\n   147→className=\"min-h-[44px] px-4 py-2\"\n   148→```\n   149→\n   150→#### 4.2 Input Component (`src/components/ui/input.tsx`)\n   151→\n   152→**Check:** Ensure 16px font size on mobile to prevent iOS zoom.\n   153→\n   154→```tsx\n   155→// Add or verify\n   156→className=\"text-base md:text-sm\"\n   157→```\n   158→\n   159→#### 4.3 Voice Recorder (`src/components/voice-recorder.tsx`)\n   160→\n   161→**Requirements:**\n   162→- Record button must be prominently sized (60x60px recommended)\n   163→- Visual feedback during recording\n   164→- Works with mobile microphone permissions\n   165→\n   166→---\n   167→\n   168→### 5. Testing Requirements\n   169→\n   170→#### Device Testing Matrix\n   171→\n   172→| Device Type | Screen Width | Test Priority |\n   173→|-------------|--------------|---------------|\n   174→| iPhone SE | 375px | High |\n   175→| iPhone 12/13/14 | 390px | High |\n   176→| iPhone Plus/Max | 428px | Medium |\n   177→| Android Small | 360px | High |\n   178→| Android Medium | 412px | Medium |\n   179→| iPad Mini | 768px | Medium |\n   180→| iPad | 1024px | Low |\n   181→\n   182→#### Test Cases\n   183→\n   184→| ID | Test Case | Steps | Expected Result |\n   185→|----|-----------|-------|-----------------|\n   186→| M01 | Navbar hamburger menu | Tap menu icon | Menu slides in |\n   187→| M02 | Menu link navigation | Tap menu item | Navigates and closes menu |\n   188→| M03 | Menu close on outside tap | Tap overlay | Menu closes |\n   189→| M04 | Input focus (iOS) | Tap input field | No page zoom |\n   190→| M05 | Button tap targets | Tap all buttons | All buttons respond |\n   191→| M06 | Horizontal scroll | Scroll on any page | No horizontal scroll |\n   192→| M07 | Voice recording | Tap record button | Recording starts |\n   193→| M08 | Image upload | Tap upload area | File picker opens |\n   194→| M09 | Form submission | Fill and submit form | Form submits successfully |\n   195→| M10 | Landscape orientation | Rotate device | Layout adapts |\n   196→\n   197→---\n   198→\n   199→## 📁 Files to Modify\n   200→\n   201→### Priority 1 (Critical)\n   202→1. `src/components/navbar.tsx` - Mobile hamburger menu\n   203→2. `src/app/globals.css` - Mobile utility classes\n   204→\n   205→### Priority 2 (Important)\n   206→3. `src/app/dashboard/page.tsx` - Responsive table\n   207→4. `src/components/voice-recorder.tsx` - Touch targets\n   208→5. `src/components/ui/button.tsx` - Verify touch targets\n   209→6. `src/components/ui/input.tsx` - Prevent iOS zoom\n   210→\n   211→### Priority 3 (Nice to Have)\n   212→7. `src/app/page.tsx` - Hero text sizing\n   213→8. `src/app/send/page.tsx` - Form layout\n   214→9. All page layouts - General mobile polish\n   215→\n   216→---\n   217→\n   218→## 🔧 Implementation Steps\n   219→\n   220→### Step 1: Mobile Navbar (Day 1 - Morning)\n   221→1. Add `useState` for menu open/close\n   222→2. Import `Menu` and `X` icons from lucide-react\n   223→3. Create hamburger button (hidden on desktop)\n   224→4. Create slide-out panel with navigation links\n   225→5. Add overlay for closing menu\n   226→6. Test on mobile viewport\n   227→\n   228→### Step 2: Global CSS Utilities (Day 1 - Afternoon)\n   229→1. Add touch-target utility class\n   230→2. Add iOS input zoom prevention\n   231→3. Add safe-area-inset utility\n   232→4. Add scroll utilities\n   233→5. Test on various devices\n   234→\n   235→### Step 3: Component Updates (Day 2)\n   236→1. Review and update Button component\n   237→2. Review and update Input component\n   238→3. Update Voice Recorder touch targets\n   239→4. Test all interactive components\n   240→\n   241→### Step 4: Page-by-Page Fixes (Day 2-3)\n   242→1. Dashboard table responsiveness\n   243→2. Generate page mobile layout\n   244→3. Send page form layout\n   245→4. All other pages review\n   246→\n   247→### Step 5: Testing & Polish (Day 3)\n   248→1. Run through device testing matrix\n   249→2. Execute all test cases\n   250→3. Fix any issues found\n   251→4. Final Lighthouse audit\n   252→\n   253→---\n   254→\n   255→## ✅ Definition of Done\n   256→\n   257→- [ ] Hamburger menu works on mobile\n   258→- [ ] All pages render without horizontal scroll\n   259→- [ ] All buttons/inputs have 44x44px minimum tap targets\n   260→- [ ] iOS devices don't zoom on input focus\n   261→- [ ] Voice recorder works on mobile\n   262→- [ ] Image upload works on mobile\n   263→- [ ] All test cases pass\n   264→- [ ] Lighthouse mobile score ≥ 90\n   265→- [ ] Tested on iPhone and Android\n   266→- [ ] Code reviewed and merged\n   267→\n   268→---\n   269→\n   270→## 📚 Resources\n   271→\n   272→- [Mobile-First Design Principles](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS/CSS_layout/Responsive_Design)\n   273→- [Touch Target Size Guidelines](https://web.dev/accessible-tap-targets/)\n   274→- [Safe Area Insets](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/env)\n   275→- [Tailwind Responsive Design](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/responsive-design)\n   276→\n   277→---\n   278→\n   279→**Document Created:** December 2024  \n   280→**Author:** Development Team\n   281→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Av53iWMdyjdZVRqzr4ZYK7","session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"65e6e891-2bbe-42a6-86a1-6bea8352df6f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/PRD_MOBILE_OPTIMIZATION.md","content":"# 📱 PRD: Mobile Optimization for SteadyLetters\n\n**Document Version:** 1.0  \n**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n**Priority:** High  \n**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 days\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Overview\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe SteadyLetters web app currently has limited mobile responsiveness. The navigation menu doesn't collapse on mobile devices, touch targets may be too small, and the overall mobile experience needs improvement.\n\n### Goal\nMake SteadyLetters fully mobile-optimized with an excellent user experience on phones and tablets.\n\n### Success Metrics\n- [ ] 100% of pages render correctly on mobile (320px - 768px width)\n- [ ] All interactive elements have minimum 44x44px touch targets\n- [ ] Navigation works seamlessly on mobile with hamburger menu\n- [ ] No horizontal scrolling on any page\n- [ ] Lighthouse mobile score ≥ 90\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Requirements\n\n### 1. Mobile Navigation (Navbar)\n\n**Current State:** Navigation links overflow on mobile screens.\n\n**Required Changes:**\n\n| Component | Change Required | File to Modify |\n|-----------|----------------|----------------|\n| Navbar | Add hamburger menu icon | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n| Navbar | Create slide-out mobile menu panel | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n| Navbar | Hide desktop links on mobile | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n| Navbar | Add overlay when menu is open | `src/components/navbar.tsx` |\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n```tsx\n// Add state for mobile menu\nconst [mobileMenuOpen, setMobileMenuOpen] = useState(false);\n\n// Add hamburger button (visible on mobile only)\n<button className=\"md:hidden\" onClick={() => setMobileMenuOpen(!mobileMenuOpen)}>\n  <Menu className=\"h-6 w-6\" />\n</button>\n\n// Add mobile menu panel (slides in from right)\n<div className={`fixed top-16 right-0 h-full w-72 bg-background transform transition-transform ${mobileMenuOpen ? 'translate-x-0' : 'translate-x-full'}`}>\n  {/* Navigation links */}\n</div>\n```\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- `lucide-react` (already installed) - for Menu and X icons\n\n---\n\n### 2. Global Mobile CSS Utilities\n\n**Current State:** No mobile-specific utility classes.\n\n**Required Changes:**\n\n| Utility | Purpose | File to Modify |\n|---------|---------|----------------|\n| `.touch-target` | Ensure 44x44px minimum tap targets | `src/app/globals.css` |\n| `.safe-area-inset` | Handle notched devices (iPhone X+) | `src/app/globals.css` |\n| Input font fix | Prevent iOS zoom on input focus | `src/app/globals.css` |\n| Scroll utilities | Smooth mobile scrolling | `src/app/globals.css` |\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n```css\n/* Add to globals.css */\n@layer utilities {\n  /* Touch-friendly tap targets */\n  .touch-target {\n    min-height: 44px;\n    min-width: 44px;\n  }\n\n  /* Prevent iOS zoom on input focus */\n  @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {\n    input, select, textarea {\n      font-size: 16px !important;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* Safe area for notched devices */\n  .safe-area-inset {\n    padding-left: env(safe-area-inset-left);\n    padding-right: env(safe-area-inset-right);\n    padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Page-Specific Mobile Fixes\n\n#### 3.1 Homepage (`src/app/page.tsx`)\n\n| Element | Issue | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| Hero text | May be too large on small screens | Add `text-3xl sm:text-5xl md:text-7xl` |\n| CTA buttons | Stack on mobile | Already uses `flex-col sm:flex-row` ✅ |\n| Feature grid | 4 columns too narrow on mobile | Already uses `md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4` ✅ |\n\n#### 3.2 Dashboard (`src/app/dashboard/page.tsx`)\n\n| Element | Issue | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| Stats cards | Grid may need adjustment | Add `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3` |\n| Table | Horizontal scroll on mobile | Wrap in `overflow-x-auto` container |\n| Action button | May be hard to tap | Add `touch-target` class |\n\n#### 3.3 Generate Page (`src/app/generate/page.tsx`)\n\n| Element | Issue | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| Voice recorder button | Must be large enough to tap | Ensure 44x44px minimum |\n| Text input | Font size must be 16px | Apply mobile input fix |\n| Image upload | Touch-friendly area | Add visual feedback on touch |\n\n#### 3.4 Send Page (`src/app/send/page.tsx`)\n\n| Element | Issue | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| Form fields | Need proper spacing | Add `space-y-4` between fields |\n| Submit button | Full width on mobile | Add `w-full sm:w-auto` |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Component Updates\n\n#### 4.1 Button Component (`src/components/ui/button.tsx`)\n\n**Check:** Ensure all button variants have adequate touch targets.\n\n```tsx\n// Verify these classes exist for mobile\nclassName=\"min-h-[44px] px-4 py-2\"\n```\n\n#### 4.2 Input Component (`src/components/ui/input.tsx`)\n\n**Check:** Ensure 16px font size on mobile to prevent iOS zoom.\n\n```tsx\n// Add or verify\nclassName=\"text-base md:text-sm\"\n```\n\n#### 4.3 Voice Recorder (`src/components/voice-recorder.tsx`)\n\n**Requirements:**\n- Record button must be prominently sized (60x60px recommended)\n- Visual feedback during recording\n- Works with mobile microphone permissions\n\n---\n\n### 5. Testing Requirements\n\n#### Device Testing Matrix\n\n| Device Type | Screen Width | Test Priority |\n|-------------|--------------|---------------|\n| iPhone SE | 375px | High |\n| iPhone 12/13/14 | 390px | High |\n| iPhone Plus/Max | 428px | Medium |\n| Android Small | 360px | High |\n| Android Medium | 412px | Medium |\n| iPad Mini | 768px | Medium |\n| iPad | 1024px | Low |\n\n#### Test Cases\n\n| ID | Test Case | Steps | Expected Result |\n|----|-----------|-------|-----------------|\n| M01 | Navbar hamburger menu | Tap menu icon | Menu slides in |\n| M02 | Menu link navigation | Tap menu item | Navigates and closes menu |\n| M03 | Menu close on outside tap | Tap overlay | Menu closes |\n| M04 | Input focus (iOS) | Tap input field | No page zoom |\n| M05 | Button tap targets | Tap all buttons | All buttons respond |\n| M06 | Horizontal scroll | Scroll on any page | No horizontal scroll |\n| M07 | Voice recording | Tap record button | Recording starts |\n| M08 | Image upload | Tap upload area | File picker opens |\n| M09 | Form submission | Fill and submit form | Form submits successfully |\n| M10 | Landscape orientation | Rotate device | Layout adapts |\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Files to Modify\n\n### Priority 1 (Critical)\n1. `src/components/navbar.tsx` - Mobile hamburger menu\n2. `src/app/globals.css` - Mobile utility classes\n\n### Priority 2 (Important)\n3. `src/app/dashboard/page.tsx` - Responsive table\n4. `src/components/voice-recorder.tsx` - Touch targets\n5. `src/components/ui/button.tsx` - Verify touch targets\n6. `src/components/ui/input.tsx` - Prevent iOS zoom\n\n### Priority 3 (Nice to Have)\n7. `src/app/page.tsx` - Hero text sizing\n8. `src/app/send/page.tsx` - Form layout\n9. All page layouts - General mobile polish\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Implementation Steps\n\n### Step 1: Mobile Navbar (Day 1 - Morning)\n1. Add `useState` for menu open/close\n2. Import `Menu` and `X` icons from lucide-react\n3. Create hamburger button (hidden on desktop)\n4. Create slide-out panel with navigation links\n5. Add overlay for closing menu\n6. Test on mobile viewport\n\n### Step 2: Global CSS Utilities (Day 1 - Afternoon)\n1. Add touch-target utility class\n2. Add iOS input zoom prevention\n3. Add safe-area-inset utility\n4. Add scroll utilities\n5. Test on various devices\n\n### Step 3: Component Updates (Day 2)\n1. Review and update Button component\n2. Review and update Input component\n3. Update Voice Recorder touch targets\n4. Test all interactive components\n\n### Step 4: Page-by-Page Fixes (Day 2-3)\n1. Dashboard table responsiveness\n2. Generate page mobile layout\n3. Send page form layout\n4. All other pages review\n\n### Step 5: Testing & Polish (Day 3)\n1. Run through device testing matrix\n2. Execute all test cases\n3. Fix any issues found\n4. Final Lighthouse audit\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Hamburger menu works on mobile\n- [ ] All pages render without horizontal scroll\n- [ ] All buttons/inputs have 44x44px minimum tap targets\n- [ ] iOS devices don't zoom on input focus\n- [ ] Voice recorder works on mobile\n- [ ] Image upload works on mobile\n- [ ] All test cases pass\n- [ ] Lighthouse mobile score ≥ 90\n- [ ] Tested on iPhone and Android\n- [ ] Code reviewed and merged\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources\n\n- [Mobile-First Design Principles](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS/CSS_layout/Responsive_Design)\n- [Touch Target Size Guidelines](https://web.dev/accessible-tap-targets/)\n- [Safe Area Insets](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/env)\n- [Tailwind Responsive Design](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/responsive-design)\n\n---\n\n**Document Created:** December 2024  \n**Author:** Development Team\n","numLines":281,"startLine":1,"totalLines":281}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AB3nghMrXQKMSbuqWpk2FB","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# PRD: Security Hardening\n     2→\n     3→**Version:** 1.0  \n     4→**Date:** January 19, 2026  \n     5→**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n     6→**Priority:** High  \n     7→**Estimated Effort:** 1-2 days\n     8→\n     9→---\n    10→\n    11→## 1. Overview\n    12→\n    13→### Problem Statement\n    14→The SteadyLetters application has functional security through Supabase Auth and Stripe webhook verification, but lacks comprehensive protection against API abuse, webhook spoofing (Thanks.io), and standardized security headers.\n    15→\n    16→### Goals\n    17→1. Verify all webhook sources with cryptographic signatures\n    18→2. Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse\n    19→3. Add security headers for defense in depth\n    20→4. Standardize input validation\n    21→\n    22→### Success Metrics\n    23→- [ ] All webhooks verify signatures before processing\n    24→- [ ] Rate limiting active on all public endpoints\n    25→- [ ] Security headers score A+ on securityheaders.com\n    26→- [ ] No unvalidated external input reaches database\n    27→\n    28→---\n    29→\n    30→## 2. Requirements\n    31→\n    32→### 2.1 Thanks.io Webhook Signature Verification\n    33→\n    34→**Current State:** Webhook accepts any POST request with valid JSON\n    35→\n    36→**File:** `src/app/api/webhooks/thanks/route.ts`\n    37→\n    38→**Implementation:**\n    39→```typescript\n    40→import crypto from 'crypto';\n    41→\n    42→function verifyThanksSignature(payload: string, signature: string | null): boolean {\n    43→  if (!signature || !process.env.THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {\n    44→    return false;\n    45→  }\n    46→  \n    47→  const expectedSignature = crypto\n    48→    .createHmac('sha256', process.env.THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET)\n    49→    .update(payload)\n    50→    .digest('hex');\n    51→    \n    52→  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(\n    53→    Buffer.from(signature),\n    54→    Buffer.from(expectedSignature)\n    55→  );\n    56→}\n    57→\n    58→export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n    59→  const body = await request.text();\n    60→  const signature = request.headers.get('x-thanks-signature');\n    61→  \n    62→  if (!verifyThanksSignature(body, signature)) {\n    63→    console.warn('[Thanks.io Webhook] Invalid signature rejected');\n    64→    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid signature' }, { status: 401 });\n    65→  }\n    66→  \n    67→  const data = JSON.parse(body);\n    68→  // ... rest of handler\n    69→}\n    70→```\n    71→\n    72→**Environment Variable:**\n    73→```\n    74→THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_webhook_secret_here\n    75→```\n    76→\n    77→---\n    78→\n    79→### 2.2 Rate Limiting\n    80→\n    81→**Current State:** No rate limiting on API endpoints\n    82→\n    83→**Recommended Package:** `@upstash/ratelimit` with `@upstash/redis`\n    84→\n    85→**Implementation:**\n    86→\n    87→```typescript\n    88→// src/lib/rate-limit.ts\n    89→import { Ratelimit } from '@upstash/ratelimit';\n    90→import { Redis } from '@upstash/redis';\n    91→\n    92→const redis = new Redis({\n    93→  url: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL!,\n    94→  token: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN!,\n    95→});\n    96→\n    97→// Different limits for different endpoint types\n    98→export const rateLimiters = {\n    99→  // Generous limit for general API\n   100→  api: new Ratelimit({\n   101→    redis,\n   102→    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(100, '1 m'),\n   103→    analytics: true,\n   104→  }),\n   105→  \n   106→  // Stricter limit for expensive operations\n   107→  generation: new Ratelimit({\n   108→    redis,\n   109→    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(10, '1 m'),\n   110→    analytics: true,\n   111→  }),\n   112→  \n   113→  // Very strict for auth endpoints\n   114→  auth: new Ratelimit({\n   115→    redis,\n   116→    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(5, '1 m'),\n   117→    analytics: true,\n   118→  }),\n   119→};\n   120→\n   121→export async function checkRateLimit(\n   122→  limiter: keyof typeof rateLimiters,\n   123→  identifier: string\n   124→): Promise<{ success: boolean; remaining: number }> {\n   125→  const result = await rateLimiters[limiter].limit(identifier);\n   126→  return { success: result.success, remaining: result.remaining };\n   127→}\n   128→```\n   129→\n   130→**Usage in API Route:**\n   131→```typescript\n   132→import { checkRateLimit } from '@/lib/rate-limit';\n   133→\n   134→export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n   135→  const ip = request.headers.get('x-forwarded-for') || 'anonymous';\n   136→  const { success, remaining } = await checkRateLimit('generation', ip);\n   137→  \n   138→  if (!success) {\n   139→    return NextResponse.json(\n   140→      { error: 'Too many requests. Please try again later.' },\n   141→      { \n   142→        status: 429,\n   143→        headers: { 'X-RateLimit-Remaining': remaining.toString() }\n   144→      }\n   145→    );\n   146→  }\n   147→  \n   148→  // ... rest of handler\n   149→}\n   150→```\n   151→\n   152→---\n   153→\n   154→### 2.3 Security Headers\n   155→\n   156→**File:** `next.config.js` or middleware\n   157→\n   158→**Implementation:**\n   159→```javascript\n   160→// next.config.js\n   161→const securityHeaders = [\n   162→  {\n   163→    key: 'X-DNS-Prefetch-Control',\n   164→    value: 'on'\n   165→  },\n   166→  {\n   167→    key: 'Strict-Transport-Security',\n   168→    value: 'max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload'\n   169→  },\n   170→  {\n   171→    key: 'X-Frame-Options',\n   172→    value: 'SAMEORIGIN'\n   173→  },\n   174→  {\n   175→    key: 'X-Content-Type-Options',\n   176→    value: 'nosniff'\n   177→  },\n   178→  {\n   179→    key: 'Referrer-Policy',\n   180→    value: 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin'\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    key: 'Permissions-Policy',\n   184→    value: 'camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=()'\n   185→  }\n   186→];\n   187→\n   188→module.exports = {\n   189→  async headers() {\n   190→    return [\n   191→      {\n   192→        source: '/:path*',\n   193→        headers: securityHeaders,\n   194→      },\n   195→    ];\n   196→  },\n   197→};\n   198→```\n   199→\n   200→---\n   201→\n   202→### 2.4 Input Validation with Zod\n   203→\n   204→**Current State:** Basic validation in route handlers\n   205→\n   206→**Recommendation:** Standardize with Zod schemas\n   207→\n   208→```typescript\n   209→// src/lib/validations/letter.ts\n   210→import { z } from 'zod';\n   211→\n   212→export const letterGenerationSchema = z.object({\n   213→  context: z.string().min(10).max(5000),\n   214→  tone: z.enum(['warm', 'professional', 'casual', 'formal', 'heartfelt']),\n   215→  occasion: z.enum(['thank_you', 'birthday', 'congratulations', 'thinking_of_you', 'holiday', 'other']),\n   216→  holiday: z.string().optional(),\n   217→  imageAnalysis: z.string().optional(),\n   218→  length: z.enum(['short', 'medium', 'long']).optional(),\n   219→});\n   220→\n   221→export const recipientSchema = z.object({\n   222→  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),\n   223→  address1: z.string().min(1).max(200),\n   224→  address2: z.string().max(200).optional(),\n   225→  city: z.string().min(1).max(100),\n   226→  state: z.string().min(2).max(50),\n   227→  zip: z.string().regex(/^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$/),\n   228→  country: z.string().default('US'),\n   229→});\n   230→```\n   231→\n   232→**Usage:**\n   233→```typescript\n   234→const result = letterGenerationSchema.safeParse(body);\n   235→if (!result.success) {\n   236→  return NextResponse.json(\n   237→    { error: 'Invalid input', details: result.error.flatten() },\n   238→    { status: 400 }\n   239→  );\n   240→}\n   241→const { context, tone, occasion } = result.data;\n   242→```\n   243→\n   244→---\n   245→\n   246→## 3. Files to Modify\n   247→\n   248→| File | Change |\n   249→|------|--------|\n   250→| `src/app/api/webhooks/thanks/route.ts` | Add signature verification |\n   251→| `src/lib/rate-limit.ts` | Create new file |\n   252→| `src/app/api/generate/letter/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n   253→| `src/app/api/generate/images/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n   254→| `src/app/api/transcribe/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n   255→| `next.config.js` | Add security headers |\n   256→| `src/lib/validations/` | Create validation schemas |\n   257→\n   258→---\n   259→\n   260→## 4. Environment Variables Required\n   261→\n   262→```env\n   263→# Thanks.io Webhook\n   264→THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=\n   265→\n   266→# Upstash Redis (for rate limiting)\n   267→UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=\n   268→UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=\n   269→```\n   270→\n   271→---\n   272→\n   273→## 5. Testing Checklist\n   274→\n   275→- [ ] Thanks.io webhook rejects requests without valid signature\n   276→- [ ] Thanks.io webhook accepts requests with valid signature\n   277→- [ ] Rate limit returns 429 after threshold exceeded\n   278→- [ ] Rate limit resets after window expires\n   279→- [ ] Security headers present on all responses\n   280→- [ ] Invalid input returns 400 with helpful error message\n   281→\n   282→---\n   283→\n   284→## 6. Definition of Done\n   285→\n   286→- [ ] All webhooks verify signatures\n   287→- [ ] Rate limiting deployed and tested\n   288→- [ ] Security headers configured\n   289→- [ ] Input validation standardized with Zod\n   290→- [ ] Documentation updated\n   291→- [ ] Security scan passes (no critical/high issues)\n   292→\n   293→---\n   294→\n   295→**Document Created:** January 19, 2026  \n   296→**Author:** Development Team\n   297→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Av53iWMdyjdZVRqzr4ZYK7","session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"f06d4a92-46b6-4d42-b6ff-804f9fa906bb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/PRD_SECURITY_HARDENING.md","content":"# PRD: Security Hardening\n\n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Date:** January 19, 2026  \n**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n**Priority:** High  \n**Estimated Effort:** 1-2 days\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe SteadyLetters application has functional security through Supabase Auth and Stripe webhook verification, but lacks comprehensive protection against API abuse, webhook spoofing (Thanks.io), and standardized security headers.\n\n### Goals\n1. Verify all webhook sources with cryptographic signatures\n2. Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse\n3. Add security headers for defense in depth\n4. Standardize input validation\n\n### Success Metrics\n- [ ] All webhooks verify signatures before processing\n- [ ] Rate limiting active on all public endpoints\n- [ ] Security headers score A+ on securityheaders.com\n- [ ] No unvalidated external input reaches database\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### 2.1 Thanks.io Webhook Signature Verification\n\n**Current State:** Webhook accepts any POST request with valid JSON\n\n**File:** `src/app/api/webhooks/thanks/route.ts`\n\n**Implementation:**\n```typescript\nimport crypto from 'crypto';\n\nfunction verifyThanksSignature(payload: string, signature: string | null): boolean {\n  if (!signature || !process.env.THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  \n  const expectedSignature = crypto\n    .createHmac('sha256', process.env.THANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET)\n    .update(payload)\n    .digest('hex');\n    \n  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(\n    Buffer.from(signature),\n    Buffer.from(expectedSignature)\n  );\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  const body = await request.text();\n  const signature = request.headers.get('x-thanks-signature');\n  \n  if (!verifyThanksSignature(body, signature)) {\n    console.warn('[Thanks.io Webhook] Invalid signature rejected');\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid signature' }, { status: 401 });\n  }\n  \n  const data = JSON.parse(body);\n  // ... rest of handler\n}\n```\n\n**Environment Variable:**\n```\nTHANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_webhook_secret_here\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 Rate Limiting\n\n**Current State:** No rate limiting on API endpoints\n\n**Recommended Package:** `@upstash/ratelimit` with `@upstash/redis`\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/rate-limit.ts\nimport { Ratelimit } from '@upstash/ratelimit';\nimport { Redis } from '@upstash/redis';\n\nconst redis = new Redis({\n  url: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL!,\n  token: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN!,\n});\n\n// Different limits for different endpoint types\nexport const rateLimiters = {\n  // Generous limit for general API\n  api: new Ratelimit({\n    redis,\n    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(100, '1 m'),\n    analytics: true,\n  }),\n  \n  // Stricter limit for expensive operations\n  generation: new Ratelimit({\n    redis,\n    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(10, '1 m'),\n    analytics: true,\n  }),\n  \n  // Very strict for auth endpoints\n  auth: new Ratelimit({\n    redis,\n    limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(5, '1 m'),\n    analytics: true,\n  }),\n};\n\nexport async function checkRateLimit(\n  limiter: keyof typeof rateLimiters,\n  identifier: string\n): Promise<{ success: boolean; remaining: number }> {\n  const result = await rateLimiters[limiter].limit(identifier);\n  return { success: result.success, remaining: result.remaining };\n}\n```\n\n**Usage in API Route:**\n```typescript\nimport { checkRateLimit } from '@/lib/rate-limit';\n\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  const ip = request.headers.get('x-forwarded-for') || 'anonymous';\n  const { success, remaining } = await checkRateLimit('generation', ip);\n  \n  if (!success) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: 'Too many requests. Please try again later.' },\n      { \n        status: 429,\n        headers: { 'X-RateLimit-Remaining': remaining.toString() }\n      }\n    );\n  }\n  \n  // ... rest of handler\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Security Headers\n\n**File:** `next.config.js` or middleware\n\n**Implementation:**\n```javascript\n// next.config.js\nconst securityHeaders = [\n  {\n    key: 'X-DNS-Prefetch-Control',\n    value: 'on'\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'Strict-Transport-Security',\n    value: 'max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload'\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'X-Frame-Options',\n    value: 'SAMEORIGIN'\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'X-Content-Type-Options',\n    value: 'nosniff'\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'Referrer-Policy',\n    value: 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin'\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'Permissions-Policy',\n    value: 'camera=(), microphone=(self), geolocation=()'\n  }\n];\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  async headers() {\n    return [\n      {\n        source: '/:path*',\n        headers: securityHeaders,\n      },\n    ];\n  },\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Input Validation with Zod\n\n**Current State:** Basic validation in route handlers\n\n**Recommendation:** Standardize with Zod schemas\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/validations/letter.ts\nimport { z } from 'zod';\n\nexport const letterGenerationSchema = z.object({\n  context: z.string().min(10).max(5000),\n  tone: z.enum(['warm', 'professional', 'casual', 'formal', 'heartfelt']),\n  occasion: z.enum(['thank_you', 'birthday', 'congratulations', 'thinking_of_you', 'holiday', 'other']),\n  holiday: z.string().optional(),\n  imageAnalysis: z.string().optional(),\n  length: z.enum(['short', 'medium', 'long']).optional(),\n});\n\nexport const recipientSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1).max(100),\n  address1: z.string().min(1).max(200),\n  address2: z.string().max(200).optional(),\n  city: z.string().min(1).max(100),\n  state: z.string().min(2).max(50),\n  zip: z.string().regex(/^\\d{5}(-\\d{4})?$/),\n  country: z.string().default('US'),\n});\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```typescript\nconst result = letterGenerationSchema.safeParse(body);\nif (!result.success) {\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    { error: 'Invalid input', details: result.error.flatten() },\n    { status: 400 }\n  );\n}\nconst { context, tone, occasion } = result.data;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Files to Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/app/api/webhooks/thanks/route.ts` | Add signature verification |\n| `src/lib/rate-limit.ts` | Create new file |\n| `src/app/api/generate/letter/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n| `src/app/api/generate/images/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n| `src/app/api/transcribe/route.ts` | Add rate limiting |\n| `next.config.js` | Add security headers |\n| `src/lib/validations/` | Create validation schemas |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Environment Variables Required\n\n```env\n# Thanks.io Webhook\nTHANKS_IO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=\n\n# Upstash Redis (for rate limiting)\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] Thanks.io webhook rejects requests without valid signature\n- [ ] Thanks.io webhook accepts requests with valid signature\n- [ ] Rate limit returns 429 after threshold exceeded\n- [ ] Rate limit resets after window expires\n- [ ] Security headers present on all responses\n- [ ] Invalid input returns 400 with helpful error message\n\n---\n\n## 6. Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All webhooks verify signatures\n- [ ] Rate limiting deployed and tested\n- [ ] Security headers configured\n- [ ] Input validation standardized with Zod\n- [ ] Documentation updated\n- [ ] Security scan passes (no critical/high issues)\n\n---\n\n**Document Created:** January 19, 2026  \n**Author:** Development Team\n","numLines":297,"startLine":1,"totalLines":297}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01483XUnJv7cq1gdeMTvKPVt","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# PRD: Observability & Monitoring\n     2→\n     3→**Version:** 1.0  \n     4→**Date:** January 19, 2026  \n     5→**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n     6→**Priority:** Medium  \n     7→**Estimated Effort:** 1 day\n     8→\n     9→---\n    10→\n    11→## 1. Overview\n    12→\n    13→### Problem Statement\n    14→Currently, errors are logged to console only and there's no visibility into application performance, user behavior, or system health in production.\n    15→\n    16→### Goals\n    17→1. Capture and alert on application errors\n    18→2. Track key user flows and conversion metrics\n    19→3. Monitor API performance and latency\n    20→4. Enable debugging of production issues\n    21→\n    22→### Success Metrics\n    23→- [ ] 100% of unhandled errors captured\n    24→- [ ] Key user actions tracked (signup, generate, send)\n    25→- [ ] P95 latency visible for all API routes\n    26→- [ ] Alerts configured for error spikes\n    27→\n    28→---\n    29→\n    30→## 2. Requirements\n    31→\n    32→### 2.1 Error Tracking (Sentry)\n    33→\n    34→**Package:** `@sentry/nextjs`\n    35→\n    36→**Setup:**\n    37→```bash\n    38→npx @sentry/wizard@latest -i nextjs\n    39→```\n    40→\n    41→**Configuration:**\n    42→```typescript\n    43→// sentry.client.config.ts\n    44→import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\n    45→\n    46→Sentry.init({\n    47→  dsn: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN,\n    48→  environment: process.env.NODE_ENV,\n    49→  tracesSampleRate: 0.1, // 10% of transactions\n    50→  replaysSessionSampleRate: 0.1,\n    51→  replaysOnErrorSampleRate: 1.0,\n    52→});\n    53→```\n    54→\n    55→**Custom Error Boundaries:**\n    56→```typescript\n    57→// src/components/error-boundary.tsx\n    58→'use client';\n    59→\n    60→import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\n    61→import { useEffect } from 'react';\n    62→\n    63→export function ErrorFallback({ error, resetErrorBoundary }) {\n    64→  useEffect(() => {\n    65→    Sentry.captureException(error);\n    66→  }, [error]);\n    67→\n    68→  return (\n    69→    <div className=\"p-4 text-center\">\n    70→      <h2>Something went wrong</h2>\n    71→      <button onClick={resetErrorBoundary}>Try again</button>\n    72→    </div>\n    73→  );\n    74→}\n    75→```\n    76→\n    77→---\n    78→\n    79→### 2.2 Analytics (PostHog or Vercel Analytics)\n    80→\n    81→**Option A: Vercel Analytics (Simpler)**\n    82→```bash\n    83→npm install @vercel/analytics\n    84→```\n    85→\n    86→```typescript\n    87→// src/app/layout.tsx\n    88→import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';\n    89→\n    90→export default function RootLayout({ children }) {\n    91→  return (\n    92→    <html>\n    93→      <body>\n    94→        {children}\n    95→        <Analytics />\n    96→      </body>\n    97→    </html>\n    98→  );\n    99→}\n   100→```\n   101→\n   102→**Option B: PostHog (More Features)**\n   103→```typescript\n   104→// src/lib/posthog.ts\n   105→import posthog from 'posthog-js';\n   106→\n   107→export function initPostHog() {\n   108→  if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\n   109→    posthog.init(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY!, {\n   110→      api_host: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST,\n   111→      capture_pageview: false, // Manual control\n   112→    });\n   113→  }\n   114→}\n   115→\n   116→// Track custom events\n   117→export function trackEvent(event: string, properties?: Record<string, any>) {\n   118→  posthog.capture(event, properties);\n   119→}\n   120→```\n   121→\n   122→**Key Events to Track:**\n   123→| Event | Properties |\n   124→|-------|------------|\n   125→| `user_signed_up` | `{ method: 'email' \\| 'oauth' }` |\n   126→| `letter_generated` | `{ tone, occasion, tier }` |\n   127→| `image_generated` | `{ count, tier }` |\n   128→| `order_created` | `{ product_type, amount }` |\n   129→| `subscription_started` | `{ plan, price }` |\n   130→| `limit_reached` | `{ type, tier }` |\n   131→\n   132→---\n   133→\n   134→### 2.3 API Performance Monitoring\n   135→\n   136→**Middleware Approach:**\n   137→```typescript\n   138→// src/lib/api-timing.ts\n   139→import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\n   140→\n   141→export function withTiming<T>(\n   142→  name: string,\n   143→  fn: () => Promise<T>\n   144→): Promise<T> {\n   145→  const start = performance.now();\n   146→  \n   147→  return fn().finally(() => {\n   148→    const duration = performance.now() - start;\n   149→    \n   150→    // Log slow requests\n   151→    if (duration > 1000) {\n   152→      console.warn(`[SLOW] ${name}: ${duration.toFixed(0)}ms`);\n   153→      Sentry.captureMessage(`Slow API: ${name}`, {\n   154→        level: 'warning',\n   155→        extra: { duration },\n   156→      });\n   157→    }\n   158→  });\n   159→}\n   160→```\n   161→\n   162→**Usage:**\n   163→```typescript\n   164→export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n   165→  return withTiming('generate/letter', async () => {\n   166→    // ... handler logic\n   167→  });\n   168→}\n   169→```\n   170→\n   171→---\n   172→\n   173→### 2.4 Health Check Dashboard\n   174→\n   175→**Endpoint:** `GET /api/health`\n   176→\n   177→**Enhanced Response:**\n   178→```typescript\n   179→// src/app/api/health/route.ts\n   180→export async function GET() {\n   181→  const checks = {\n   182→    database: await checkDatabase(),\n   183→    supabase: await checkSupabase(),\n   184→    stripe: await checkStripe(),\n   185→    thanksIo: await checkThanksIo(),\n   186→  };\n   187→\n   188→  const allHealthy = Object.values(checks).every(c => c.status === 'ok');\n   189→\n   190→  return NextResponse.json({\n   191→    status: allHealthy ? 'healthy' : 'degraded',\n   192→    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n   193→    checks,\n   194→  }, { status: allHealthy ? 200 : 503 });\n   195→}\n   196→\n   197→async function checkDatabase() {\n   198→  try {\n   199→    await prisma.$queryRaw`SELECT 1`;\n   200→    return { status: 'ok' };\n   201→  } catch (error) {\n   202→    return { status: 'error', message: error.message };\n   203→  }\n   204→}\n   205→```\n   206→\n   207→---\n   208→\n   209→### 2.5 Logging Standards\n   210→\n   211→**Structured Logging:**\n   212→```typescript\n   213→// src/lib/logger.ts\n   214→type LogLevel = 'debug' | 'info' | 'warn' | 'error';\n   215→\n   216→interface LogEntry {\n   217→  level: LogLevel;\n   218→  message: string;\n   219→  timestamp: string;\n   220→  context?: Record<string, any>;\n   221→}\n   222→\n   223→export function log(level: LogLevel, message: string, context?: Record<string, any>) {\n   224→  const entry: LogEntry = {\n   225→    level,\n   226→    message,\n   227→    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n   228→    context,\n   229→  };\n   230→\n   231→  if (level === 'error') {\n   232→    console.error(JSON.stringify(entry));\n   233→  } else if (level === 'warn') {\n   234→    console.warn(JSON.stringify(entry));\n   235→  } else {\n   236→    console.log(JSON.stringify(entry));\n   237→  }\n   238→}\n   239→\n   240→// Convenience methods\n   241→export const logger = {\n   242→  debug: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('debug', msg, ctx),\n   243→  info: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('info', msg, ctx),\n   244→  warn: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('warn', msg, ctx),\n   245→  error: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('error', msg, ctx),\n   246→};\n   247→```\n   248→\n   249→---\n   250→\n   251→## 3. Environment Variables\n   252→\n   253→```env\n   254→# Sentry\n   255→NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=\n   256→SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n   257→\n   258→# PostHog (if using)\n   259→NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=\n   260→NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com\n   261→```\n   262→\n   263→---\n   264→\n   265→## 4. Alerts Configuration\n   266→\n   267→| Alert | Trigger | Channel |\n   268→|-------|---------|---------|\n   269→| Error spike | >10 errors in 5 min | Slack/Email |\n   270→| Slow API | P95 > 3s for 10 min | Slack |\n   271→| Health check fail | 3 consecutive failures | PagerDuty/Email |\n   272→| Subscription churn | User cancels | Email |\n   273→\n   274→---\n   275→\n   276→## 5. Files to Create/Modify\n   277→\n   278→| File | Action |\n   279→|------|--------|\n   280→| `sentry.client.config.ts` | Create |\n   281→| `sentry.server.config.ts` | Create |\n   282→| `sentry.edge.config.ts` | Create |\n   283→| `src/lib/logger.ts` | Create |\n   284→| `src/lib/posthog.ts` | Create (if using) |\n   285→| `src/app/layout.tsx` | Add Analytics component |\n   286→| `src/app/api/health/route.ts` | Enhance |\n   287→\n   288→---\n   289→\n   290→## 6. Definition of Done\n   291→\n   292→- [ ] Sentry capturing errors in production\n   293→- [ ] Analytics tracking key user events\n   294→- [ ] Health check endpoint returns service status\n   295→- [ ] Structured logging implemented\n   296→- [ ] Alerts configured for critical issues\n   297→- [ ] Dashboard accessible to team\n   298→\n   299→---\n   300→\n   301→**Document Created:** January 19, 2026  \n   302→**Author:** Development Team\n   303→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Av53iWMdyjdZVRqzr4ZYK7","session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"146949af-36a1-4801-a5e1-0fd521b0dc1e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/PRD_OBSERVABILITY.md","content":"# PRD: Observability & Monitoring\n\n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Date:** January 19, 2026  \n**Status:** Ready for Implementation  \n**Priority:** Medium  \n**Estimated Effort:** 1 day\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\n### Problem Statement\nCurrently, errors are logged to console only and there's no visibility into application performance, user behavior, or system health in production.\n\n### Goals\n1. Capture and alert on application errors\n2. Track key user flows and conversion metrics\n3. Monitor API performance and latency\n4. Enable debugging of production issues\n\n### Success Metrics\n- [ ] 100% of unhandled errors captured\n- [ ] Key user actions tracked (signup, generate, send)\n- [ ] P95 latency visible for all API routes\n- [ ] Alerts configured for error spikes\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### 2.1 Error Tracking (Sentry)\n\n**Package:** `@sentry/nextjs`\n\n**Setup:**\n```bash\nnpx @sentry/wizard@latest -i nextjs\n```\n\n**Configuration:**\n```typescript\n// sentry.client.config.ts\nimport * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\n\nSentry.init({\n  dsn: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN,\n  environment: process.env.NODE_ENV,\n  tracesSampleRate: 0.1, // 10% of transactions\n  replaysSessionSampleRate: 0.1,\n  replaysOnErrorSampleRate: 1.0,\n});\n```\n\n**Custom Error Boundaries:**\n```typescript\n// src/components/error-boundary.tsx\n'use client';\n\nimport * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\nimport { useEffect } from 'react';\n\nexport function ErrorFallback({ error, resetErrorBoundary }) {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error);\n  }, [error]);\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 text-center\">\n      <h2>Something went wrong</h2>\n      <button onClick={resetErrorBoundary}>Try again</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 Analytics (PostHog or Vercel Analytics)\n\n**Option A: Vercel Analytics (Simpler)**\n```bash\nnpm install @vercel/analytics\n```\n\n```typescript\n// src/app/layout.tsx\nimport { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }) {\n  return (\n    <html>\n      <body>\n        {children}\n        <Analytics />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Option B: PostHog (More Features)**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/posthog.ts\nimport posthog from 'posthog-js';\n\nexport function initPostHog() {\n  if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\n    posthog.init(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY!, {\n      api_host: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST,\n      capture_pageview: false, // Manual control\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n// Track custom events\nexport function trackEvent(event: string, properties?: Record<string, any>) {\n  posthog.capture(event, properties);\n}\n```\n\n**Key Events to Track:**\n| Event | Properties |\n|-------|------------|\n| `user_signed_up` | `{ method: 'email' \\| 'oauth' }` |\n| `letter_generated` | `{ tone, occasion, tier }` |\n| `image_generated` | `{ count, tier }` |\n| `order_created` | `{ product_type, amount }` |\n| `subscription_started` | `{ plan, price }` |\n| `limit_reached` | `{ type, tier }` |\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 API Performance Monitoring\n\n**Middleware Approach:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/api-timing.ts\nimport * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';\n\nexport function withTiming<T>(\n  name: string,\n  fn: () => Promise<T>\n): Promise<T> {\n  const start = performance.now();\n  \n  return fn().finally(() => {\n    const duration = performance.now() - start;\n    \n    // Log slow requests\n    if (duration > 1000) {\n      console.warn(`[SLOW] ${name}: ${duration.toFixed(0)}ms`);\n      Sentry.captureMessage(`Slow API: ${name}`, {\n        level: 'warning',\n        extra: { duration },\n      });\n    }\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```typescript\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  return withTiming('generate/letter', async () => {\n    // ... handler logic\n  });\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Health Check Dashboard\n\n**Endpoint:** `GET /api/health`\n\n**Enhanced Response:**\n```typescript\n// src/app/api/health/route.ts\nexport async function GET() {\n  const checks = {\n    database: await checkDatabase(),\n    supabase: await checkSupabase(),\n    stripe: await checkStripe(),\n    thanksIo: await checkThanksIo(),\n  };\n\n  const allHealthy = Object.values(checks).every(c => c.status === 'ok');\n\n  return NextResponse.json({\n    status: allHealthy ? 'healthy' : 'degraded',\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    checks,\n  }, { status: allHealthy ? 200 : 503 });\n}\n\nasync function checkDatabase() {\n  try {\n    await prisma.$queryRaw`SELECT 1`;\n    return { status: 'ok' };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { status: 'error', message: error.message };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2.5 Logging Standards\n\n**Structured Logging:**\n```typescript\n// src/lib/logger.ts\ntype LogLevel = 'debug' | 'info' | 'warn' | 'error';\n\ninterface LogEntry {\n  level: LogLevel;\n  message: string;\n  timestamp: string;\n  context?: Record<string, any>;\n}\n\nexport function log(level: LogLevel, message: string, context?: Record<string, any>) {\n  const entry: LogEntry = {\n    level,\n    message,\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    context,\n  };\n\n  if (level === 'error') {\n    console.error(JSON.stringify(entry));\n  } else if (level === 'warn') {\n    console.warn(JSON.stringify(entry));\n  } else {\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(entry));\n  }\n}\n\n// Convenience methods\nexport const logger = {\n  debug: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('debug', msg, ctx),\n  info: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('info', msg, ctx),\n  warn: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('warn', msg, ctx),\n  error: (msg: string, ctx?: Record<string, any>) => log('error', msg, ctx),\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Environment Variables\n\n```env\n# Sentry\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=\nSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=\n\n# PostHog (if using)\nNEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=\nNEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Alerts Configuration\n\n| Alert | Trigger | Channel |\n|-------|---------|---------|\n| Error spike | >10 errors in 5 min | Slack/Email |\n| Slow API | P95 > 3s for 10 min | Slack |\n| Health check fail | 3 consecutive failures | PagerDuty/Email |\n| Subscription churn | User cancels | Email |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files to Create/Modify\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| `sentry.client.config.ts` | Create |\n| `sentry.server.config.ts` | Create |\n| `sentry.edge.config.ts` | Create |\n| `src/lib/logger.ts` | Create |\n| `src/lib/posthog.ts` | Create (if using) |\n| `src/app/layout.tsx` | Add Analytics component |\n| `src/app/api/health/route.ts` | Enhance |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Sentry capturing errors in production\n- [ ] Analytics tracking key user events\n- [ ] Health check endpoint returns service status\n- [ ] Structured logging implemented\n- [ ] Alerts configured for critical issues\n- [ ] Dashboard accessible to team\n\n---\n\n**Document Created:** January 19, 2026  \n**Author:** Development Team\n","numLines":303,"startLine":1,"totalLines":303}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G9cXLFQf5TuahWuJDWNwZo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# SteadyLetters\n     2→\n     3→**AI-Powered Physical Letter Sending Platform**\n     4→\n     5→A SaaS web application that enables users to create and send physical handwritten-style letters via Thanks.io API integration. Features AI letter generation, voice transcription, image generation, and subscription-based usage tiers.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## Quick Start\n    10→\n    11→### Development Server\n    12→\n    13→```bash\n    14→npm install\n    15→npm run dev\n    16→```\n    17→\n    18→Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) to view the application.\n    19→\n    20→### Prerequisites\n    21→\n    22→- Node.js 20+\n    23→- PostgreSQL database (or Supabase account)\n    24→- Required API keys (see Environment Setup below)\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→## Tech Stack\n    29→\n    30→| Layer | Technology |\n    31→|-------|------------|\n    32→| Frontend | Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript |\n    33→| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4, shadcn/ui |\n    34→| Database | PostgreSQL (Supabase), Prisma ORM |\n    35→| Auth | Supabase Auth |\n    36→| Storage | Supabase Storage |\n    37→| AI | OpenAI GPT-4o, Whisper, DALL-E 3 |\n    38→| Mail API | Thanks.io |\n    39→| Payments | Stripe |\n    40→| Deployment | Vercel |\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## Environment Setup\n    45→\n    46→Create a `.env.local` file with the following variables:\n    47→\n    48→```env\n    49→# Database\n    50→DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...\n    51→\n    52→# Supabase\n    53→NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co\n    54→NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...\n    55→SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...\n    56→\n    57→# OpenAI\n    58→OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n    59→\n    60→# Stripe\n    61→STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n    62→NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\n    63→STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...\n    64→STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID=price_...\n    65→STRIPE_BUSINESS_PRICE_ID=price_...\n    66→\n    67→# Thanks.io\n    68→THANKS_IO_API_KEY=...\n    69→```\n    70→\n    71→See `DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md` for complete environment variable documentation.\n    72→\n    73→---\n    74→\n    75→## Project Structure\n    76→\n    77→```\n    78→/\n    79→├── src/\n    80→│   ├── app/                    # Next.js App Router\n    81→│   │   ├── actions/            # Server actions (CRUD operations)\n    82→│   │   ├── api/                # API routes\n    83→│   │   ├── dashboard/          # Dashboard page\n    84→│   │   ├── generate/           # Letter generation page\n    85→│   │   ├── send/               # Send letter page\n    86→│   │   ├── recipients/         # Recipient management\n    87→│   │   ├── templates/          # Template management\n    88→│   │   ├── orders/             # Order history\n    89→│   │   └── billing/            # Subscription management\n    90→│   ├── components/             # React components\n    91→│   │   ├── ui/                 # shadcn/ui components\n    92→│   │   ├── navbar.tsx\n    93→│   │   ├── voice-recorder.tsx\n    94→│   │   └── ...\n    95→│   └── lib/                    # Utility libraries\n    96→│       ├── thanks-io.ts        # Thanks.io API client\n    97→│       ├── openai.ts           # OpenAI integrations\n    98→│       ├── stripe.ts           # Stripe client\n    99→│       ├── usage.ts            # Usage tracking\n   100→│       └── tiers.ts            # Subscription tier logic\n   101→├── prisma/\n   102→│   └── schema.prisma           # Database schema\n   103→├── tests/                      # Test files (48+ tests)\n   104→│   ├── e2e/                    # Playwright E2E tests\n   105→│   └── unit/                   # Jest unit tests\n   106→└── PRD_*.md                    # Product requirement documents\n   107→```\n   108→\n   109→---\n   110→\n   111→## Available Scripts\n   112→\n   113→```bash\n   114→# Development\n   115→npm run dev              # Start dev server\n   116→npm run build            # Build for production\n   117→npm run start            # Start production server\n   118→\n   119→# Testing\n   120→npm test                 # Run Jest tests\n   121→npm run test:e2e         # Run Playwright E2E tests\n   122→npm run test:all         # Run all tests\n   123→\n   124→# Database\n   125→npx prisma generate      # Generate Prisma client\n   126→npx prisma db push       # Push schema changes\n   127→npx prisma migrate dev   # Run migrations\n   128→npx prisma studio        # Open database GUI\n   129→\n   130→# Diagnostics\n   131→npm run check:env        # Verify environment variables\n   132→npm run validate:keys    # Validate API keys\n   133→npm run diagnose         # Run full diagnostic suite\n   134→```\n   135→\n   136→---\n   137→\n   138→## Development Status\n   139→\n   140→**Current Phase:** 6 - Mobile Optimization\n   141→**Features Completed:** 31/71 (43.7%)\n   142→**Latest Update:** January 20, 2026\n   143→\n   144→### ✅ Phase 1-5 Complete\n   145→- AI letter generation (GPT-4o)\n   146→- Voice transcription (Whisper)\n   147→- Image generation (DALL-E 3)\n   148→- Recipient management\n   149→- Template management\n   150→- Order creation and tracking\n   151→- Stripe subscriptions and billing\n   152→- Dashboard analytics\n   153→\n   154→### 🚧 Phase 6 - In Progress\n   155→- Mobile hamburger menu\n   156→- Touch-friendly UI\n   157→- Mobile responsive layouts\n   158→- iOS optimizations\n   159→\n   160→### 📋 Phase 7 - Planned\n   161→- Webhook signature verification\n   162→- Rate limiting\n   163→- Security headers\n   164→- Input validation\n   165→\n   166→See `feature_list.json` for complete feature tracking.\n   167→\n   168→---\n   169→\n   170→## Autonomous Development\n   171→\n   172→This project uses an autonomous coding harness for incremental feature development.\n   173→\n   174→### Key Files\n   175→- `feature_list.json` 