context, sender name\n    - Temperature 0.8 for creative variation\n    - Returns array of 3 letters or fallback to raw content\n  - **generateImages()**: Calls DALL-E-3 to generate card images\n  - **transcribeAudio()**: Calls Whisper-1 model for speech-to-text\n    - Reads audio from file URI\n    - Handles FormData for audio file upload\n  - **extractAddress()**: Uses GPT-4o with temperature 0 for structured address extraction\n- **API Integration**: Real OpenAI API with Bearer token authentication\n- **TODOs**: None\n- **Status**: Complete and production-ready\n\n#### **thanks-io.ts - Thanks.io Integration**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real, comprehensive API layer\n- **Mock Data**: None\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - **Handwriting Styles**: `getHandwritingStyles()` - fetches available styles from Thanks.io\n  - **Order Status**: `getOrderStatus()` - real-time status tracking\n  - **Send Functions**: \n    - `sendPostcard()` - sends postcard with message and handwriting\n    - `sendLetter()` - sends letter with optional additional pages\n    - `sendGreetingCard()` - sends greeting card with envelope style\n    - `sendWindowlessLetter()` - sends PDF-based letter\n  - **Product Catalog**: Complete with real pricing\n    - Postcard: $1.14\n    - Letter: $1.20\n    - Greeting Card: $3.00\n    - Windowless Letter: $2.52\n    - Gift Card: $3.00\n  - **Tier System**: Proper tier-based product restrictions\n  - **Pricing Functions**: `getPostcardPrice()`, `getProductsForTier()`\n- **API Integration**: Real Thanks.io API with Bearer token authentication\n- **TODOs**: None\n- **Status**: Complete and production-ready\n\n---\n\n### PROVIDERS (/providers directory)\n\n#### **ThemeProvider.tsx**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real, fully functional\n- **Mock Data**: None\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - Theme management (light/dark/system)\n  - Persists theme preference to secure storage\n  - Uses system color scheme as fallback\n  - Provides useTheme hook for accessing colors and theme state\n- **Status**: Complete\n\n#### **AuthProvider.tsx**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real, fully functional\n- **Mock Data**: None\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - Session and user state management\n  - `signIn()` - real Supabase authentication\n  - `signUp()` - real Supabase user creation with full name metadata\n  - `signOut()` - real Supabase sign out\n  - `resetPassword()` - real Supabase password reset email\n  - Auth state change listener for persistent sessions\n  - Loading state during initialization\n- **API Integration**: Real Supabase authentication\n- **TODOs**: None\n- **Status**: Complete and production-ready\n\n---\n\n### CONSTANTS (/constants directory)\n\n#### **config.ts**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real configuration structure\n- **Environment Variables**: All key configs use environment variables:\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_THANKS_IO_API_KEY`\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY`\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (defined but not used in reviewed code)\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_API_KEY` (defined but not used)\n  - `EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUCAT_API_KEY` (defined but not used)\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - App metadata (name, slug, scheme)\n  - Development mode flag\n  - Tier definitions with limits and pricing:\n    - Free: 5 letter generations, 3 image generations, 2 letters sent, postcard only\n    - Pro: 50 letter generations, 25 image generations, 20 letters sent, postcard/letter/greeting\n    - Business: Unlimited letter generations, 100 image generations, 100 letters sent, all products\n- **Status**: Complete\n\n#### **colors.ts**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real color scheme\n- **Mock Data**: None\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - Light theme colors (navy primary, white background, full color palette)\n  - Dark theme colors (light blue primary, dark background, matching palette)\n  - Comprehensive color variables for UI components\n- **Status**: Complete\n\n#### **typography.ts**\n- **Implementation Level**: Real typography system\n- **Mock Data**: None\n- **Real Functionality**:\n  - Platform-specific font families (System for iOS, Roboto for Android)\n  - Font size scale (xs-3xl)\n  - Font weights (regular-bold)\n  - Line height presets\n- **Status**: Complete\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY OF FINDINGS\n\n### Overall Code Quality:\n- **95% Real Implementation**: The codebase is predominantly real and production-ready\n- **Minimal Scaffolding**: Only 5-10% is placeholder/scaffold code\n- **No Hardcoded Fake Data**: All services use real APIs with proper environment variable configuration\n\n### What's Complete and Production-Ready:\n1. Authentication flow (sign-in, sign-up, password reset)\n2. All three real APIs integrated: Supabase, OpenAI, Thanks.io\n3. Full CRUD operations for recipients and orders\n4. Letter generation with AI (GPT-4o)\n5. Audio transcription (Whisper API)\n6. Direct physical mail sending via Thanks.io\n7. Usage tracking and tier management\n8. Theme system with persistence\n9. Voice recording functionality\n10. Product catalog with accurate pricing\n\n### What's Incomplete (Placeholders Only):\n1. **Settings Screen** has three placeholder navigation items:\n   - Notifications settings\n   - Privacy Policy\n   - Help & FAQ\n   - Subscription plan management (routes to empty handler)\n\n### Key API Integrations Confirmed:\n- **Supabase**: Auth, recipients, orders, templates, usage tracking\n- **OpenAI**: Letter generation (GPT-4o), audio transcription (Whisper), address extraction\n- **Thanks.io**: Handwriting styles, order status tracking, postcard/letter/greeting card sending\n- **expo-secure-store**: Secure token and theme persistence\n\n### No Critical Issues Found:\n- No mock API responses\n- No fake data in production paths\n- Proper error handling throughout\n- Real environment variable configuration\n- All API calls use proper authentication headers\n\nThis is a **genuinely functional application** ready for production deployment, with only minor UI placeholder elements in the Settings screen."}],"totalDurationMs":45174,"totalTokens":54718,"totalToolUseCount":27,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2463,"cache_read_input_tokens":48500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2463},"output_tokens":3748,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Av53iWMdyjdZVRqzr4ZYK7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive report on the iOS app requirements.\n\n## Complete iOS App Requirements for SteadyLetters\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the KindLetters/SteadyLetters documentation and iOS project structure, here is the comprehensive feature specification for the iOS app:\n\n---\n\n## iOS App Feature Summary\n\n**Project:** SteadyLetters iOS (Expo Router)  \n**Current Status:** 27/44 features complete (61.4%)  \n**Framework:** React Native with Expo Router  \n**Platform:** iOS (portrait orientation, iPad support)  \n**Architecture:** Expo-based, uses Tab Navigation + Modal Stack\n\n---\n\n## Core Features Documentation\n\n### 1. Authentication Module (IOS-AUTH-001 through 005) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nThe iOS app includes a complete authentication system:\n\n- **Sign In Screen** - Email/password authentication with Supabase Auth, error handling, and loading states\n- **Sign Up Screen** - Account creation with full name, email, password, confirmation, and email verification\n- **Forgot Password Screen** - Password reset via Supabase with email verification\n- **Auth Provider with SecureStore** - React context managing auth state with secure token persistence using `expo-secure-store`\n- **Protected Route Guard** - Redirect unauthenticated users from tabs to sign-in screen\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase Auth, expo-secure-store, React Context\n\n---\n\n### 2. Letter Generation (IOS-LETTER-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nThree approaches to create letters on iOS:\n\n#### AI Letter Generation Screen\n- Generate 3 letter variations using GPT-4o\n- Configurable parameters:\n  - Occasion (thank you, birthday, congratulations, thinking of you, holiday, other)\n  - Tone (warm, professional, casual, formal, heartfelt)\n  - Key points to include (optional)\n  - Recipient context (optional)\n- Display multiple options for user selection\n\n#### Voice-to-Letter Dictation\n- Record audio using `expo-av`\n- Transcribe using OpenAI Whisper API\n- Use transcribed text as letter content\n- Real-time audio visualization\n- Start/stop recording controls\n\n#### Letter Template Browser\n- Browse saved templates\n- Filter by occasion and tone\n- Tap to prefill the generate screen\n- Quick reuse of previous successful letters\n\n**Technologies:** OpenAI GPT-4o, OpenAI Whisper, expo-av\n\n---\n\n### 3. Send Flow (IOS-SEND-001 through 004) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nComplete workflow to send physical mail from the app:\n\n#### Product Selection\n- Choose between:\n  - Postcard (4x6\")\n  - Letter (standard business envelope)\n  - Greeting Card (premium with stamp)\n- Display pricing per product type\n\n#### Recipient Picker\n- Select from address book dropdown\n- Address preview before sending\n- Ability to add new recipient inline\n\n#### Handwriting Style Selection\n- Choose from Thanks.io available handwriting styles\n- Visual preview of handwriting options\n- Color selection (blue, black, green, purple, red, or hex)\n\n#### Thanks.io Integration\n- Actually send postcards/letters/greeting cards via Thanks.io API\n- Create order record in database\n- Real order tracking with status updates\n\n**Technologies:** Thanks.io API, Supabase database\n\n---\n\n### 4. Address Book Management (IOS-RECIP-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nFull recipient/address management:\n\n#### Recipients List with Search\n- Display all saved recipients\n- Search filter functionality\n- Show name, address, city for each recipient\n- Pull-to-refresh for updated data\n\n#### Add Recipient Form\n- Input fields for:\n  - Full name\n  - Address line 1\n  - Address line 2 (optional)\n  - City\n  - State/Province\n  - ZIP/Postal code\n  - Country\n- Form validation\n- Modal presentation\n\n#### Delete Recipient\n- Swipe-to-delete or button-based deletion\n- Confirmation alert to prevent accidents\n- Real-time list update after deletion\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase Auth + Database, React Native Gesture Handler\n\n---\n\n### 5. Order History & Tracking (IOS-ORDER-001 through 002) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nComplete order management interface:\n\n#### Order History List\n- View all past orders\n- Display per order:\n  - Status badges (pending, processing, sent, delivered, failed)\n  - Product type (postcard, letter, greeting card)\n  - Recipient name\n  - Cost\n  - Date created\n\n#### Order Status Refresh\n- Pull-to-refresh to check latest status\n- Tap-to-check button for manual refresh\n- Live status updates via Thanks.io API\n- Real-time status synchronization\n\n**Technologies:** Thanks.io API, Supabase\n\n---\n\n### 6. Settings & Account (IOS-SETTINGS-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nUser account and app settings:\n\n#### Account Profile Section\n- Display user email\n- Show profile info from Supabase\n- Basic user information interface\n\n#### Theme Switcher\n- Light/dark/system theme toggle\n- Persistent preference storage via SecureStore\n- Automatic theme switching based on system preference\n\n#### Sign Out\n- Sign out with confirmation alert\n- Clear session and secure storage\n- Redirect to authentication screens\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase, expo-secure-store, React Native\n\n---\n\n### 7. Navigation Structure (IOS-NAV-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nApp navigation uses Expo Router with proper hierarchy:\n\n#### Tab Navigation (5 tabs)\n1. **Create** - Letter generation and composition\n2. **Recipients** - Address book management\n3. **Templates** - Saved letter templates\n4. **Orders** - Order history and tracking\n5. **Settings** - Account and app settings\n\nEach tab with custom icons (lucide-react-native)\n\n#### Modal Stack Navigation\n- Send flow as modal presentation\n- Voice recorder as modal\n- Add recipient as modal\n- Smooth transitions and dismissal\n\n#### Splash Screen\n- Custom splash screen with app logo\n- Auto-hide after app layout loads\n- Proper initialization sequence\n\n**Technologies:** Expo Router, lucide-react-native\n\n---\n\n### 8. Backend Services (IOS-SERVICE-001 through 004) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nCore API clients and services:\n\n#### Supabase Client with SecureStore\n- Configured Supabase JS client\n- Secure token persistence using expo-secure-store\n- User session management\n- Database access with proper authentication\n\n#### Thanks.io API Client\nFull Thanks.io integration with methods:\n- `sendPostcard()` - Send postcard\n- `sendLetter()` - Send handwritten letter\n- `sendGreetingCard()` - Send greeting card\n- `getHandwritingStyles()` - List available handwriting styles\n- `getOrderStatus()` - Check order status\n\n#### OpenAI Client\n- `generateLetter()` - GPT-4o letter composition\n- `transcribeAudio()` - Whisper audio transcription\n\n#### API CRUD Service\nSupabase database operations for:\n- Recipients (create, read, update, delete)\n- Orders (create, read, list, status update)\n- Templates (create, read, update, delete)\n- Usage tracking (increment counters, check limits)\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase JS SDK, OpenAI API, Thanks.io API, Zustand for state management\n\n---\n\n### 9. Live Integration Tests (IOS-TEST-001 through 005) - PENDING (0/5)\n\nReal integration tests that hit live APIs:\n\n- **Live Postcard Send Test** - Actually sends test postcard via Thanks.io\n- **Live Letter Send Test** - Sends actual handwritten letter via Thanks.io\n- **Live Greeting Card Send Test** - Sends greeting card via Thanks.io\n- **Handwriting Styles API Test** - Retrieves available handwriting styles\n- **Order Status Check Test** - Verifies order status after sending\n\n**Status:** Framework in place, tests pending configuration  \n**Technologies:** Jest, expo test utilities\n\n---\n\n### 10. Billing & In-App Purchases (IOS-BILLING-001 through 003) - PENDING (0/3)\n\nSubscription management for iOS:\n\n#### RevenueCat SDK Setup\n- Initialize with API key\n- Configure subscription offerings\n- Handle purchase events\n\n#### Subscription Paywall Screen\n- Display subscription tiers with pricing\n- Show feature differences per tier\n- Implement in-app purchase flow via RevenueCat\n- Handle purchase success/failure\n\n#### Entitlement Checking\n- Check user subscription status\n- Gate premium features based on tier\n- Display upgrade prompts for limits\n\n**Technologies:** RevenueCat (in-app purchases), react-native-purchases\n\n---\n\n### 11. Analytics & Event Tracking (IOS-ANALYTICS-001 through 002) - PENDING (0/2)\n\nUser behavior tracking:\n\n#### PostHog SDK Setup\n- Initialize PostHog React Native SDK\n- Identify users after authentication\n- Track sessions and user properties\n\n#### Event Tracking\nKey events to track:\n- `letter_created` - User generates a letter\n- `letter_sent` - User sends a letter\n- `recipient_added` - New recipient added\n- `template_used` - User reuses a template\n- `subscription_purchased` - User upgrades tier\n- `order_status_checked` - User checks order status\n\n**Technologies:** PostHog React Native SDK, posthog-react-native\n\n---\n\n### 12. Push Notifications (IOS-NOTIF-001 through 002) - PENDING (0/2)\n\nIn-app and push notification system:\n\n#### Push Notification Setup\n- Configure `expo-notifications`\n- Request user permissions\n- Register device token for push notifications\n\n#### Order Status Notifications\n- Send push notifications on:\n  - Order sent\n  - Order delivered\n  - Order failed\n- Deep link to order details screen when tapped\n\n**Technologies:** expo-notifications\n\n---\n\n### 13. Polish & UX (IOS-POLISH-001 through 005) - PENDING (0/5)\n\nFinal polish and user experience refinements:\n\n#### Error Boundary\n- Global error boundary component\n- User-friendly error fallback UI\n- Error logging integration\n\n#### Loading Skeletons\n- Skeleton loading states for:\n  - Recipients list\n  - Orders list\n  - Templates list\n- Shimmer animation effects\n\n#### Haptic Feedback\n- Haptic feedback on button presses using `expo-haptics`\n- Success haptics on completed actions\n- Error vibrations for validation failures\n\n#### Empty States\n- Polished empty state illustrations\n- Per-screen custom messaging (no recipients, no orders, etc.)\n- Call-to-action buttons\n\n#### Keyboard Avoidance\n- Proper keyboard avoidance on all form screens\n- Modal adjustments when keyboard appears\n- Smooth keyboard transitions\n\n**Technologies:** expo-haptics, react-native-safe-area-context, Reanimated\n\n---\n\n## App Configuration & Permissions\n\n**Bundle ID:** `com.steadyletters.app`  \n**Orientation:** Portrait primary (iPad support enabled)\n\n### iOS Permissions (in app.json)\n```\nNSMicrophoneUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs microphone access for voice-to-letter recording\"\nNSCameraUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs camera access to take photos for letter images\"\nNSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs photo library access to select images for letters\"\n```\n\n### Android Permissions\n```\nRECORD_AUDIO, CAMERA, READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE\n```\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| **Framework** | Expo 52, React Native 0.76, Expo Router 4 |\n| **Language** | TypeScript 5.3 |\n| **State Management** | Zustand 5.0, React Context (Auth) |\n| **Backend API** | Supabase JS SDK 2.84 |\n| **Mail Sending** | Thanks.io API |\n| **AI/ML** | OpenAI GPT-4o, Whisper, (no image generation on mobile) |\n| **Authentication** | Supabase Auth + expo-secure-store |\n| **In-App Purchases** | RevenueCat + react-native-purchases |\n| **Analytics** | PostHog React Native |\n| **Notifications** | expo-notifications |\n| **UI Components** | Lucide React Native, native React Native components |\n| **Media Handling** | expo-av (audio), expo-image-picker, expo-image |\n| **Testing** | Jest 29.7 + jest-expo 52 |\n| **Icons** | Expo Vector Icons + Lucide React Native |\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n**Completion Status:** 27/44 features (61.4%)\n\n### Complete (27 features)\n- All 5 authentication screens and context\n- All 3 letter generation approaches\n- All 4 send flow screens\n- All 3 recipient management screens\n- All 2 order tracking screens\n- All 3 settings screens\n- All 3 navigation components\n- All 4 backend service clients\n\n### Pending (17 features)\n- 5 live integration tests (awaiting configuration)\n- 3 billing/RevenueCat features\n- 2 PostHog analytics features\n- 2 push notification features\n- 5 polish/UX features (error boundary, skeletons, haptics, empty states, keyboard avoidance)\n\n---\n\n## Subscription Tiers (from main PRD)\n\n| Tier | Price | Letters/Month | Images/Month | Features |\n|------|-------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| **Free** | $0 | 10 | 5 | Postcards only |\n| **Pro** | $29/month | 100 | 50 | + Letters, Greeting Cards |\n| **Business** | $99/month | Unlimited | Unlimited | + Windowless Letters, Gift Cards, API |\n\n---\n\n## Integration Points\n\nThe iOS app connects to:\n- **Supabase** - User auth, recipients, orders, templates storage\n- **Thanks.io API** - Actually send physical mail\n- **OpenAI** - GPT-4o letter generation, Whisper transcription\n- **RevenueCat** - In-app purchases and subscription management\n- **PostHog** - Event tracking and analytics\n- **Push Notification Service** - APNs for iOS notifications\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive iOS app implementation provides all core functionality for creating and sending physical letters, with pending features for billing, analytics, notifications, and UI polish. The app is 61% complete with solid foundation for the remaining work."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1fd2c7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"1f00639e-6ad4-4776-991d-b1bd855a4aa2","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Thoroughly explore /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ for all PRD and requirements documents. Read these files completely:\n1. PRD_STEADYLETTERS.md\n2. PRD_MOBILE_OPTIMIZATION.md\n3. PRD_SECURITY_HARDENING.md\n4. PRD_OBSERVABILITY.md\n5. README.md\n6. DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md\n7. SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md\n8. Any other requirements or planning documents\n\nI need the complete feature requirements for the iOS app. What should the iOS app include? What features are documented in the PRDs?","agentId":"a1fd2c7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive report on the iOS app requirements.\n\n## Complete iOS App Requirements for SteadyLetters\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the KindLetters/SteadyLetters documentation and iOS project structure, here is the comprehensive feature specification for the iOS app:\n\n---\n\n## iOS App Feature Summary\n\n**Project:** SteadyLetters iOS (Expo Router)  \n**Current Status:** 27/44 features complete (61.4%)  \n**Framework:** React Native with Expo Router  \n**Platform:** iOS (portrait orientation, iPad support)  \n**Architecture:** Expo-based, uses Tab Navigation + Modal Stack\n\n---\n\n## Core Features Documentation\n\n### 1. Authentication Module (IOS-AUTH-001 through 005) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nThe iOS app includes a complete authentication system:\n\n- **Sign In Screen** - Email/password authentication with Supabase Auth, error handling, and loading states\n- **Sign Up Screen** - Account creation with full name, email, password, confirmation, and email verification\n- **Forgot Password Screen** - Password reset via Supabase with email verification\n- **Auth Provider with SecureStore** - React context managing auth state with secure token persistence using `expo-secure-store`\n- **Protected Route Guard** - Redirect unauthenticated users from tabs to sign-in screen\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase Auth, expo-secure-store, React Context\n\n---\n\n### 2. Letter Generation (IOS-LETTER-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nThree approaches to create letters on iOS:\n\n#### AI Letter Generation Screen\n- Generate 3 letter variations using GPT-4o\n- Configurable parameters:\n  - Occasion (thank you, birthday, congratulations, thinking of you, holiday, other)\n  - Tone (warm, professional, casual, formal, heartfelt)\n  - Key points to include (optional)\n  - Recipient context (optional)\n- Display multiple options for user selection\n\n#### Voice-to-Letter Dictation\n- Record audio using `expo-av`\n- Transcribe using OpenAI Whisper API\n- Use transcribed text as letter content\n- Real-time audio visualization\n- Start/stop recording controls\n\n#### Letter Template Browser\n- Browse saved templates\n- Filter by occasion and tone\n- Tap to prefill the generate screen\n- Quick reuse of previous successful letters\n\n**Technologies:** OpenAI GPT-4o, OpenAI Whisper, expo-av\n\n---\n\n### 3. Send Flow (IOS-SEND-001 through 004) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nComplete workflow to send physical mail from the app:\n\n#### Product Selection\n- Choose between:\n  - Postcard (4x6\")\n  - Letter (standard business envelope)\n  - Greeting Card (premium with stamp)\n- Display pricing per product type\n\n#### Recipient Picker\n- Select from address book dropdown\n- Address preview before sending\n- Ability to add new recipient inline\n\n#### Handwriting Style Selection\n- Choose from Thanks.io available handwriting styles\n- Visual preview of handwriting options\n- Color selection (blue, black, green, purple, red, or hex)\n\n#### Thanks.io Integration\n- Actually send postcards/letters/greeting cards via Thanks.io API\n- Create order record in database\n- Real order tracking with status updates\n\n**Technologies:** Thanks.io API, Supabase database\n\n---\n\n### 4. Address Book Management (IOS-RECIP-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nFull recipient/address management:\n\n#### Recipients List with Search\n- Display all saved recipients\n- Search filter functionality\n- Show name, address, city for each recipient\n- Pull-to-refresh for updated data\n\n#### Add Recipient Form\n- Input fields for:\n  - Full name\n  - Address line 1\n  - Address line 2 (optional)\n  - City\n  - State/Province\n  - ZIP/Postal code\n  - Country\n- Form validation\n- Modal presentation\n\n#### Delete Recipient\n- Swipe-to-delete or button-based deletion\n- Confirmation alert to prevent accidents\n- Real-time list update after deletion\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase Auth + Database, React Native Gesture Handler\n\n---\n\n### 5. Order History & Tracking (IOS-ORDER-001 through 002) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nComplete order management interface:\n\n#### Order History List\n- View all past orders\n- Display per order:\n  - Status badges (pending, processing, sent, delivered, failed)\n  - Product type (postcard, letter, greeting card)\n  - Recipient name\n  - Cost\n  - Date created\n\n#### Order Status Refresh\n- Pull-to-refresh to check latest status\n- Tap-to-check button for manual refresh\n- Live status updates via Thanks.io API\n- Real-time status synchronization\n\n**Technologies:** Thanks.io API, Supabase\n\n---\n\n### 6. Settings & Account (IOS-SETTINGS-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nUser account and app settings:\n\n#### Account Profile Section\n- Display user email\n- Show profile info from Supabase\n- Basic user information interface\n\n#### Theme Switcher\n- Light/dark/system theme toggle\n- Persistent preference storage via SecureStore\n- Automatic theme switching based on system preference\n\n#### Sign Out\n- Sign out with confirmation alert\n- Clear session and secure storage\n- Redirect to authentication screens\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase, expo-secure-store, React Native\n\n---\n\n### 7. Navigation Structure (IOS-NAV-001 through 003) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nApp navigation uses Expo Router with proper hierarchy:\n\n#### Tab Navigation (5 tabs)\n1. **Create** - Letter generation and composition\n2. **Recipients** - Address book management\n3. **Templates** - Saved letter templates\n4. **Orders** - Order history and tracking\n5. **Settings** - Account and app settings\n\nEach tab with custom icons (lucide-react-native)\n\n#### Modal Stack Navigation\n- Send flow as modal presentation\n- Voice recorder as modal\n- Add recipient as modal\n- Smooth transitions and dismissal\n\n#### Splash Screen\n- Custom splash screen with app logo\n- Auto-hide after app layout loads\n- Proper initialization sequence\n\n**Technologies:** Expo Router, lucide-react-native\n\n---\n\n### 8. Backend Services (IOS-SERVICE-001 through 004) - ALL COMPLETE\n\nCore API clients and services:\n\n#### Supabase Client with SecureStore\n- Configured Supabase JS client\n- Secure token persistence using expo-secure-store\n- User session management\n- Database access with proper authentication\n\n#### Thanks.io API Client\nFull Thanks.io integration with methods:\n- `sendPostcard()` - Send postcard\n- `sendLetter()` - Send handwritten letter\n- `sendGreetingCard()` - Send greeting card\n- `getHandwritingStyles()` - List available handwriting styles\n- `getOrderStatus()` - Check order status\n\n#### OpenAI Client\n- `generateLetter()` - GPT-4o letter composition\n- `transcribeAudio()` - Whisper audio transcription\n\n#### API CRUD Service\nSupabase database operations for:\n- Recipients (create, read, update, delete)\n- Orders (create, read, list, status update)\n- Templates (create, read, update, delete)\n- Usage tracking (increment counters, check limits)\n\n**Technologies:** Supabase JS SDK, OpenAI API, Thanks.io API, Zustand for state management\n\n---\n\n### 9. Live Integration Tests (IOS-TEST-001 through 005) - PENDING (0/5)\n\nReal integration tests that hit live APIs:\n\n- **Live Postcard Send Test** - Actually sends test postcard via Thanks.io\n- **Live Letter Send Test** - Sends actual handwritten letter via Thanks.io\n- **Live Greeting Card Send Test** - Sends greeting card via Thanks.io\n- **Handwriting Styles API Test** - Retrieves available handwriting styles\n- **Order Status Check Test** - Verifies order status after sending\n\n**Status:** Framework in place, tests pending configuration  \n**Technologies:** Jest, expo test utilities\n\n---\n\n### 10. Billing & In-App Purchases (IOS-BILLING-001 through 003) - PENDING (0/3)\n\nSubscription management for iOS:\n\n#### RevenueCat SDK Setup\n- Initialize with API key\n- Configure subscription offerings\n- Handle purchase events\n\n#### Subscription Paywall Screen\n- Display subscription tiers with pricing\n- Show feature differences per tier\n- Implement in-app purchase flow via RevenueCat\n- Handle purchase success/failure\n\n#### Entitlement Checking\n- Check user subscription status\n- Gate premium features based on tier\n- Display upgrade prompts for limits\n\n**Technologies:** RevenueCat (in-app purchases), react-native-purchases\n\n---\n\n### 11. Analytics & Event Tracking (IOS-ANALYTICS-001 through 002) - PENDING (0/2)\n\nUser behavior tracking:\n\n#### PostHog SDK Setup\n- Initialize PostHog React Native SDK\n- Identify users after authentication\n- Track sessions and user properties\n\n#### Event Tracking\nKey events to track:\n- `letter_created` - User generates a letter\n- `letter_sent` - User sends a letter\n- `recipient_added` - New recipient added\n- `template_used` - User reuses a template\n- `subscription_purchased` - User upgrades tier\n- `order_status_checked` - User checks order status\n\n**Technologies:** PostHog React Native SDK, posthog-react-native\n\n---\n\n### 12. Push Notifications (IOS-NOTIF-001 through 002) - PENDING (0/2)\n\nIn-app and push notification system:\n\n#### Push Notification Setup\n- Configure `expo-notifications`\n- Request user permissions\n- Register device token for push notifications\n\n#### Order Status Notifications\n- Send push notifications on:\n  - Order sent\n  - Order delivered\n  - Order failed\n- Deep link to order details screen when tapped\n\n**Technologies:** expo-notifications\n\n---\n\n### 13. Polish & UX (IOS-POLISH-001 through 005) - PENDING (0/5)\n\nFinal polish and user experience refinements:\n\n#### Error Boundary\n- Global error boundary component\n- User-friendly error fallback UI\n- Error logging integration\n\n#### Loading Skeletons\n- Skeleton loading states for:\n  - Recipients list\n  - Orders list\n  - Templates list\n- Shimmer animation effects\n\n#### Haptic Feedback\n- Haptic feedback on button presses using `expo-haptics`\n- Success haptics on completed actions\n- Error vibrations for validation failures\n\n#### Empty States\n- Polished empty state illustrations\n- Per-screen custom messaging (no recipients, no orders, etc.)\n- Call-to-action buttons\n\n#### Keyboard Avoidance\n- Proper keyboard avoidance on all form screens\n- Modal adjustments when keyboard appears\n- Smooth keyboard transitions\n\n**Technologies:** expo-haptics, react-native-safe-area-context, Reanimated\n\n---\n\n## App Configuration & Permissions\n\n**Bundle ID:** `com.steadyletters.app`  \n**Orientation:** Portrait primary (iPad support enabled)\n\n### iOS Permissions (in app.json)\n```\nNSMicrophoneUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs microphone access for voice-to-letter recording\"\nNSCameraUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs camera access to take photos for letter images\"\nNSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription: \"SteadyLetters needs photo library access to select images for letters\"\n```\n\n### Android Permissions\n```\nRECORD_AUDIO, CAMERA, READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE\n```\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology |\n|-------|-----------|\n| **Framework** | Expo 52, React Native 0.76, Expo Router 4 |\n| **Language** | TypeScript 5.3 |\n| **State Management** | Zustand 5.0, React Context (Auth) |\n| **Backend API** | Supabase JS SDK 2.84 |\n| **Mail Sending** | Thanks.io API |\n| **AI/ML** | OpenAI GPT-4o, Whisper, (no image generation on mobile) |\n| **Authentication** | Supabase Auth + expo-secure-store |\n| **In-App Purchases** | RevenueCat + react-native-purchases |\n| **Analytics** | PostHog React Native |\n| **Notifications** | expo-notifications |\n| **UI Components** | Lucide React Native, native React Native components |\n| **Media Handling** | expo-av (audio), expo-image-picker, expo-image |\n| **Testing** | Jest 29.7 + jest-expo 52 |\n| **Icons** | Expo Vector Icons + Lucide React Native |\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n**Completion Status:** 27/44 features (61.4%)\n\n### Complete (27 features)\n- All 5 authentication screens and context\n- All 3 letter generation approaches\n- All 4 send flow screens\n- All 3 recipient management screens\n- All 2 order tracking screens\n- All 3 settings screens\n- All 3 navigation components\n- All 4 backend service clients\n\n### Pending (17 features)\n- 5 live integration tests (awaiting configuration)\n- 3 billing/RevenueCat features\n- 2 PostHog analytics features\n- 2 push notification features\n- 5 polish/UX features (error boundary, skeletons, haptics, empty states, keyboard avoidance)\n\n---\n\n## Subscription Tiers (from main PRD)\n\n| Tier | Price | Letters/Month | Images/Month | Features |\n|------|-------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| **Free** | $0 | 10 | 5 | Postcards only |\n| **Pro** | $29/month | 100 | 50 | + Letters, Greeting Cards |\n| **Business** | $99/month | Unlimited | Unlimited | + Windowless Letters, Gift Cards, API |\n\n---\n\n## Integration Points\n\nThe iOS app connects to:\n- **Supabase** - User auth, recipients, orders, templates storage\n- **Thanks.io API** - Actually send physical mail\n- **OpenAI** - GPT-4o letter generation, Whisper transcription\n- **RevenueCat** - In-app purchases and subscription management\n- **PostHog** - Event tracking and analytics\n- **Push Notification Service** - APNs for iOS notifications\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive iOS app implementation provides all core functionality for creating and sending physical letters, with pending features for billing, analytics, notifications, and UI polish. The app is 61% complete with solid foundation for the remaining work."}],"totalDurationMs":52527,"totalTokens":61717,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1818,"cache_read_input_tokens":56417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1818},"output_tokens":3480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}}
