{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019qXciwE6Be73eBVuW9qefr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TFrXYaZctKGd2fwgLfD8j4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/claude-progress.txt","content":"# SteadyLetters iOS - Claude Agent Progress Log\n\n## Session 1: Initializer Agent (2026-02-17)\n\n### Mission\nTransform the existing scaffolded SteadyLetters iOS app into a structured, testable development environment for autonomous coding agents.\n\n### Project Analysis\n- **App**: SteadyLetters iOS - AI-powered physical letter sending app\n- **Framework**: Expo Router (React Native) with TypeScript\n- **Backend**: Supabase (auth, database), Thanks.io (mail), OpenAI (AI generation)\n- **Business Model**: Free/Pro/Business subscription tiers via RevenueCat\n\n### Current State Assessment\nThe iOS app was scaffolded in a single commit with the following status:\n- **Source code**: 95% real implementation, 5% placeholder (settings screen sections)\n- **Services**: All 4 service clients (Supabase, API CRUD, Thanks.io, OpenAI) are fully implemented with real API integration\n- **Screens**: 12 screens across auth, tabs, and modals - all functional\n- **Providers**: AuthProvider and ThemeProvider fully implemented\n- **Not Yet Built**: Billing (RevenueCat), Analytics (PostHog), Push Notifications, Polish/UX features\n\n### Actions Taken\n1. [DONE] Analyzed complete project structure and all source files\n2. [DONE] Read parent project PRDs and documentation for full requirements\n3. [DONE] Created comprehensive feature_list.json with 156 features across 18 categories, ALL marked as passes: false\n4. [DONE] Created this progress log\n5. [TODO] Create test harness script for feature verification\n6. [TODO] Verify project dependencies install cleanly\n7. [TODO] Document development workflow in README\n\n### Feature Breakdown (156 total)\n| Category | Count | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| auth | 18 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| letter-generation | 18 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| send-flow | 14 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| recipients | 9 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| orders | 8 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| templates | 3 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| settings | 14 | Partially implemented |\n| navigation | 8 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| services | 27 | Implemented, needs verification |\n| billing | 8 | Not yet built |\n| analytics | 7 | Not yet built |\n| notifications | 5 | Not yet built |\n| polish | 14 | Not yet built |\n| accessibility | 4 | Not yet built |\n| security | 6 | Needs audit |\n| performance | 4 | Needs verification |\n| testing | 9 | Test infrastructure exists |\n| config | 8 | Implemented, needs verification |\n\n### Priority Order for Future Agents\n1. **Phase 1 - Verify Core** (auth, services, config, navigation): Verify existing code passes feature requirements\n2. **Phase 2 - Verify Screens** (letter-generation, send-flow, recipients, orders, templates): Verify all screen implementations\n3. **Phase 3 - Settings Completion** (settings placeholders): Implement missing settings sections\n4. **Phase 4 - Security & Performance**: Audit and fix security/performance features\n5. **Phase 5 - Billing**: Implement RevenueCat integration\n6. **Phase 6 - Analytics**: Implement PostHog integration\n7. **Phase 7 - Notifications**: Implement push notifications\n8. **Phase 8 - Polish**: Error boundaries, skeletons, haptics, empty states, keyboard avoidance\n9. **Phase 9 - Accessibility**: VoiceOver labels and screen reader support\n10. **Phase 10 - Testing**: Live integration tests passing\n\n### Key Files\n- `feature_list.json` - 156 features, all passes: false\n- `scripts/verify-features.ts` - Feature verification harness\n- `package.json` - Dependencies and scripts\n- `app.json` - Expo configuration\n- `constants/config.ts` - Environment and tier configuration\n\n### Notes for Next Agent\n- All features are marked as `passes: false` - verify each one by reading source code\n- Many features are ALREADY implemented but unverified - start with code review verification\n- No mock data exists in production code (confirmed)\n- All API integrations use real endpoints with env vars\n- The billing, analytics, notifications, and polish categories require NEW code to be written\n- Settings screen has placeholder onPress handlers for Notifications, Privacy, Help sections\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":80907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"58134725-dbfb-4830-8579-2a319740d7c9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019qXciwE6Be73eBVuW9qefr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0173nGkGTPeN7jSgXfJfxTxQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/scripts/verify-features.ts","content":"#!/usr/bin/env ts-node\n/**\n * SteadyLetters iOS Feature Verification Harness\n *\n * This script reads feature_list.json and provides a summary of feature\n * completion status. It can also be used by autonomous agents to update\n * feature pass/fail status after verification.\n *\n * Usage:\n *   npx ts-node scripts/verify-features.ts                  # Show summary\n *   npx ts-node scripts/verify-features.ts --category auth  # Show auth features\n *   npx ts-node scripts/verify-features.ts --failing         # Show failing features\n *   npx ts-node scripts/verify-features.ts --passing         # Show passing features\n *   npx ts-node scripts/verify-features.ts --set IOS-AUTH-001 true  # Mark feature as passing\n */\n\nimport * as fs from 'fs';\nimport * as path from 'path';\n\ninterface Feature {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  category: string;\n  description: string;\n  file: string;\n  passes: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface FeatureList {\n  project: string;\n  platform: string;\n  framework: string;\n  version: string;\n  total_features: number;\n  categories: string[];\n  features: Feature[];\n}\n\nconst FEATURE_LIST_PATH = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', 'feature_list.json');\n\nfunction loadFeatures(): FeatureList {\n  const raw = fs.readFileSync(FEATURE_LIST_PATH, 'utf-8');\n  return JSON.parse(raw) as FeatureList;\n}\n\nfunction saveFeatures(data: FeatureList): void {\n  fs.writeFileSync(FEATURE_LIST_PATH, JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + '\\n', 'utf-8');\n}\n\nfunction printSummary(data: FeatureList): void {\n  const total = data.features.length;\n  const passing = data.features.filter(f => f.passes).length;\n  const failing = total - passing;\n  const pct = ((passing / total) * 100).toFixed(1);\n\n  console.log('');\n  console.log('='.repeat(60));\n  console.log(`  ${data.project} - Feature Status`);\n  console.log('='.repeat(60));\n  console.log(`  Total:   ${total}`);\n  console.log(`  Passing: ${passing} (${pct}%)`);\n  console.log(`  Failing: ${failing}`);\n  console.log('='.repeat(60));\n  console.log('');\n\n  // Category breakdown\n  const categories = new Map<string, { total: number; passing: number }>();\n  for (const f of data.features) {\n    const cat = categories.get(f.category) || { total: 0, passing: 0 };\n    cat.total++;\n    if (f.passes) cat.passing++;\n    categories.set(f.category, cat);\n  }\n\n  console.log('  Category Breakdown:');\n  console.log('  ' + '-'.repeat(56));\n  console.log(`  ${'Category'.padEnd(20)} ${'Pass'.padStart(6)} ${'Total'.padStart(6)} ${'%'.padStart(8)}`);\n  console.log('  ' + '-'.repeat(56));\n\n  for (const [cat, stats] of categories) {\n    const catPct = ((stats.passing / stats.total) * 100).toFixed(0);\n    const bar = stats.passing === stats.total ? ' [DONE]' : '';\n    console.log(\n      `  ${cat.padEnd(20)} ${String(stats.passing).padStart(6)} ${String(stats.total).padStart(6)} ${(catPct + '%').padStart(7)}${bar}`\n    );\n  }\n  console.log('  ' + '-'.repeat(56));\n  console.log('');\n}\n\nfunction printFeatures(features: Feature[], label: string): void {\n  console.log(`\\n  ${label} (${features.length}):`);\n  console.log('  ' + '-'.repeat(76));\n  for (const f of features) {\n    const status = f.passes ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL';\n    const icon = f.passes ? '+' : '-';\n    console.log(`  [${icon}] ${f.id.padEnd(18)} ${f.name.substring(0, 40).padEnd(42)} ${status}`);\n  }\n  console.log('');\n}\n\nfunction main(): void {\n  const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n  const data = loadFeatures();\n\n  if (args.includes('--set') && args.length >= 3) {\n    const setIdx = args.indexOf('--set');\n    const featureId = args[setIdx + 1];\n    const value = args[setIdx + 2] === 'true';\n    const feature = data.features.find(f => f.id === featureId);\n    if (!feature) {\n      console.error(`Feature not found: ${featureId}`);\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    feature.passes = value;\n    data.total_features = data.features.length;\n    saveFeatures(data);\n    console.log(`  Updated ${featureId}: passes = ${value}`);\n    printSummary(data);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (args.includes('--category')) {\n    const catIdx = args.indexOf('--category');\n    const category = args[catIdx + 1];\n    const filtered = data.features.filter(f => f.category === category);\n    if (filtered.length === 0) {\n      console.error(`No features found for category: ${category}`);\n      console.log(`  Available categories: ${data.categories.join(', ')}`);\n      process.exit(1);\n    }\n    printFeatures(filtered, `Category: ${category}`);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (args.includes('--failing')) {\n    const failing = data.features.filter(f => !f.passes);\n    printFeatures(failing, 'Failing Features');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (args.includes('--passing')) {\n    const passing = data.features.filter(f => f.passes);\n    printFeatures(passing, 'Passing Features');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Default: show summary\n  printSummary(data);\n}\n\nmain();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":80907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344},"output_tokens":2856,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd7b65f-b41a-4d36-961b-3254f3a5b35c","uuid":"57a5d23a-005d-4499-b2a9-c3ccbfa7dc1a"}
