{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NENj6rvfTcWRLSwaMi8kVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K6SsBic6pTarwV5azhJV6J","name":"Task","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Create BillingProvider and paywall","prompt":"Create two files for the SteadyLetters iOS Expo app at /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios:\n\n1. **providers/BillingProvider.tsx** - RevenueCat billing provider with:\n   - Import Purchases from 'react-native-purchases'\n   - Import REVENUECAT_API_KEY from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useAuth from '@/providers/AuthProvider'\n   - React context exposing: tier (TierName), isSubscribed, offerings, purchasePackage, restorePurchases, isLoading\n   - Initialize Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY }) on mount\n   - Identify user with Supabase user.id when auth changes\n   - Check entitlements to determine tier ('pro' or 'business' entitlements, default 'free')\n   - purchasePackage function calls Purchases.purchasePackage()\n   - restorePurchases function calls Purchases.restorePurchases()\n   - Gate features: canUseProduct(productType) checks tier\n   - checkUsageLimit(usage, field) compares against TIERS limits\n   - useBilling() hook\n\n2. **app/paywall.tsx** - Paywall screen with:\n   - Import TIERS, TierName from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useBilling from '@/providers/BillingProvider'\n   - Import useTheme from '@/providers/ThemeProvider'\n   - Display Free, Pro ($29/mo), Business ($99/mo) tiers in cards\n   - Feature comparison list for each tier\n   - Purchase buttons that call purchasePackage\n   - Restore purchases button at bottom\n   - Loading state while purchasing\n   - Current plan indicator\n   - Modal presentation style\n   - Register as modal in app/_layout.tsx (DO NOT modify _layout.tsx, just create paywall.tsx)\n   - Use lucide-react-native icons: Check, Crown, Star, Zap\n\nUse real RevenueCat SDK patterns. Use the same styling patterns as other screens (useTheme(), StyleSheet.create, colors object). Import TierName from '@/constants/config'.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20954,"cache_read_input_tokens":94922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20954},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c21e72c-e8bd-4a15-a613-a3101b4dd352","uuid":"9df41f57-919e-4b83-b6dd-88bff85d3e9e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NENj6rvfTcWRLSwaMi8kVW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J97ydhUoyTF5v7iQpApQgv","name":"Task","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Create AnalyticsProvider and notifications","prompt":"Create two files for the SteadyLetters iOS Expo app at /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios:\n\n1. **providers/AnalyticsProvider.tsx** - PostHog analytics provider with:\n   - Import PostHogProvider from 'posthog-react-native' (the package is already installed)\n   - Import POSTHOG_API_KEY, POSTHOG_HOST from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useAuth from '@/providers/AuthProvider'\n   - React context exposing: capture(event, properties), identify(userId, traits), reset()\n   - Wrap children with PostHogProvider configured with apiKey and host\n   - Enable session recording: autocapture: true, captureScreens: true\n   - Identify user when auth state changes (user.id, email)\n   - Reset on sign out\n   - useAnalytics() hook that returns { capture, identify, reset }\n\n2. **services/notifications.ts** - Push notification service with:\n   - Import * as Notifications from 'expo-notifications'\n   - Import * as Device from 'expo-device' (for push token)\n   - Import { router } from 'expo-router'\n   - Import { supabase } from './supabase'\n   - registerForPushNotifications() - request permissions, get ExpoPushToken, save to Supabase push_tokens table\n   - setupNotificationHandlers() - set notification received handler, set response handler that deep links to orders tab\n   - sendOrderDeliveredNotification(orderId, recipientName) - schedule local notification with deep link data\n   - All using expo-notifications APIs\n\nUse the same coding patterns as the existing services and providers. Keep it clean and production-ready. Use proper TypeScript types.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequ