s`\n\nThis service follows the same patterns as the existing services (`api.ts`, `supabase.ts`) -- pure exported async functions, Supabase auth checks with `supabase.auth.getUser()`, and `if (error) throw error` error handling.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n\n- **Section separators**: Uses the same `// -------------------------------------------------------------------` comment blocks as `api.ts` for visual organization.\n\n- **Global notification handler** (lines 11-19): Calls `Notifications.setNotificationHandler` at module level so foreground notifications display alerts, play sounds, and update badges.\n\n- **`registerForPushNotifications()`** (lines 25-58): Checks `Device.isDevice` (simulators cannot receive push tokens), requests permissions if not already granted, sets up an Android notification channel, gets the Expo push token, and persists it to the `push_tokens` Supabase table via `savePushToken()`.\n\n- **`savePushToken()`** (lines 61-78): Private helper that upserts the token to `push_tokens` with `user_id`, `token`, `platform`, and `updated_at`. Uses `onConflict: 'user_id,token'` to avoid duplicates. Follows the same auth guard pattern (`if (!user) throw new Error('Not authenticated')`) used throughout `api.ts`.\n\n- **`setupNotificationHandlers()`** (lines 84-107): Registers two listeners -- one for notifications received while the app is foregrounded (logs the identifier), and one for notification responses (user taps). The response handler reads `data.screen` or `data.orderId` from the notification payload and deep links to `/(tabs)/orders` using `expo-router`. Returns a cleanup function that removes both subscriptions, suitable for use in a `useEffect`.\n\n- **`sendOrderDeliveredNotification()`** (lines 113-128): Schedules an immediate local notification (`trigger: null`) with a title, body referencing the recipient name, default sound, and data payload containing the `orderId` and `screen: 'orders'` for deep linking when tapped.\n","prompt":"Create two files for the SteadyLetters iOS Expo app at /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios:\n\n1. **providers/AnalyticsProvider.tsx** - PostHog analytics provider with:\n   - Import PostHogProvider from 'posthog-react-native' (the package is already installed)\n   - Import POSTHOG_API_KEY, POSTHOG_HOST from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useAuth from '@/providers/AuthProvider'\n   - React context exposing: capture(event, properties), identify(userId, traits), reset()\n   - Wrap children with PostHogProvider configured with apiKey and host\n   - Enable session recording: autocapture: true, captureScreens: true\n   - Identify user when auth state changes (user.id, email)\n   - Reset on sign out\n   - useAnalytics() hook that returns { capture, identify, reset }\n\n2. **services/notifications.ts** - Push notification service with:\n   - Import * as Notifications from 'expo-notifications'\n   - Import * as Device from 'expo-device' (for push token)\n   - Import { router } from 'expo-router'\n   - Import { supabase } from './supabase'\n   - registerForPushNotifications() - request permissions, get ExpoPushToken, save to Supabase push_tokens table\n   - setupNotificationHandlers() - set notification received handler, set response handler that deep links to orders tab\n   - sendOrderDeliveredNotification(orderId, recipientName) - schedule local notification with deep link data\n   - All using expo-notifications APIs\n\nUse the same coding patterns as the existing services and providers. Keep it clean and production-ready. Use proper TypeScript types.","result":"[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.{ts,tsx}\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"providers/*.tsx\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"services/*.ts\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"services/*.ts\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AuthProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/supabase.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/api.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/config.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/config.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/openai.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AnalyticsProvider.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { createContext, useCallback, useContext, useEffect, useRef } from 'react';\\nimport { PostHogProvider, usePostHog } from 'posthog-react-native';\\nimport { POSTHOG_API_KEY, POSTHOG_HOST } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useAuth } from '@/providers/AuthProvider';\\n\\ninterface AnalyticsContextType {\\n  capture: (event: string, properties?: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\\n  identify: (userId: string, traits?: Record<string, unknown>) => void;\\n  reset: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nconst AnalyticsContext = createContext<AnalyticsContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nfunction AnalyticsSync({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\n  const posthog = usePostHog();\\n  const { user } = useAuth();\\n  const previousUserId = useRef<string | null>(null);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (user) {\\n      posthog.identify(user.id, {\\n        email: user.email,\\n        created_at: user.created_at,\\n      });\\n      previousUserId.current = user.id;\\n    } else if (previousUserId.current) {\\n      posthog.reset();\\n      previousUserId.current = null;\\n    }\\n  }, [user, posthog]);\\n\\n  const capture = useCallback(\\n    (event: string, properties?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n      posthog.capture(event, properties);\\n    },\\n    [posthog],\\n  );\\n\\n  const identify = useCallback(\\n    (userId: string, traits?: Record<string, unknown>) => {\\n      posthog.identify(userId, traits);\\n    },\\n    [posthog],\\n  );\\n\\n  const reset = useCallback(() => {\\n    posthog.reset();\\n  }, [posthog]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <AnalyticsContext.Provider value={{ capture, identify, reset }}>\\n      {children}\\n    </AnalyticsContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function AnalyticsProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\n  if (!POSTHOG_API_KEY) {\\n    return (\\n      <AnalyticsContext.Provider\\n        value={{\\n          capture: () => {},\\n          identify: () => {},\\n          reset: () => {},\\n        }}\\n      >\\n        {children}\\n      </AnalyticsContext.Provider>\\n    );\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <PostHogProvider\\n      apiKey={POSTHOG_API_KEY}\\n      options={{\\n        host: POSTHOG_HOST,\\n        enableSessionReplay: true,\\n      }}\\n      autocapture={{\\n        captureScreens: true,\\n        captureTouches: true,\\n        captureLifecycleEvents: true,\\n      }}\\n    >\\n      <AnalyticsSync>{children}</AnalyticsSync>\\n    </PostHogProvider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function useAnalytics(): AnalyticsContextType {\\n  const context = useContext(AnalyticsContext);\\n  if (!context) throw new Error('useAnalytics must be used within AnalyticsProvider');\\n  return context;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/notifications.ts\",\"content\":\"import * as Notifications from 'expo-notifications';\\nimport * as Device from 'expo-device';\\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\\nimport { router } from 'expo-router';\\nimport { supabase } from './supabase';\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Configuration\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nNotifications.setNotificationHandler({\\n  handleNotification: async () => ({\\n    shouldShowAlert: true,\\n    shouldPlaySound: true,\\n    shouldSetBadge: true,\\n    shouldShowBanner: true,\\n    shouldShowList: true,\\n  }),\\n});\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Push token registration\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport async function registerForPushNotifications(): Promise<string | null> {\\n  if (!Device.isDevice) {\\n    console.warn('Push notifications require a physical device');\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  const { status: existingStatus } = await Notifications.getPermissionsAsync();\\n  let finalStatus = existingStatus;\\n\\n  if (existingStatus !== 'granted') {\\n    const { status } = await Notifications.requestPermissionsAsync();\\n    finalStatus = status;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (finalStatus !== 'granted') {\\n    console.warn('Push notification permission not granted');\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (Platform.OS === 'android') {\\n    await Notifications.setNotificationChannelAsync('default', {\\n      name: 'Default',\\n      importance: Notifications.AndroidImportance.MAX,\\n      vibrationPattern: [0, 250, 250, 250],\\n      lightColor: '#FF6B35',\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  const tokenData = await Notifications.getExpoPushTokenAsync();\\n  const token = tokenData.data;\\n\\n  await savePushToken(token);\\n\\n  return token;\\n}\\n\\nasync function savePushToken(token: string): Promise<void> {\\n  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\\n  if (!user) throw new Error('Not authenticated');\\n\\n  const { error } = await supabase\\n    .from('push_tokens')\\n    .upsert(\\n      {\\n        user_id: user.id,\\n        token,\\n        platform: Platform.OS,\\n        updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\\n      },\\n      { onConflict: 'user_id,token' },\\n    );\\n\\n  if (error) throw error;\\n}\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Notification handlers\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport function setupNotificationHandlers(): () => void {\\n  const receivedSubscription = Notifications.addNotificationReceivedListener(\\n    (notification) => {\\n      console.log('Notification received:', notification.request.identifier);\\n    },\\n  );\\n\\n  const responseSubscription = Notifications.addNotificationResponseReceivedListener(\\n    (response) => {\\n      const data = response.notification.request.content.data as\\n        | { screen?: string; orderId?: string }\\n        | undefined;\\n\\n      if (data?.screen === 'orders' || data?.orderId) {\\n        router.push('/(tabs)/orders');\\n      }\\n    },\\n  );\\n\\n  return () => {\\n    receivedSubscription.remove();\\n    responseSubscription.remove();\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Local notifications\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport async function sendOrderDeliveredNotification(\\n  orderId: string,\\n  recipientName: string,\\n): Promise<string> {\\n  const identifier = await Notifications.scheduleNotificationAsync({\\n    content: {\\n      title: 'Letter Delivered!',\\n      body: `Your letter to ${recipientName} has been delivered.`,\\n      sound: 'default',\\n      data: { screen: 'orders', orderId },\\n    },\\n    trigger: null,\\n  });\\n\\n  return identifier;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/notifications.ts\",\"content\":\"import * as Notifications from 'expo-notifications';\\nimport * as Device from 'expo-device';\\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\\nimport { router } from 'expo-router';\\nimport { supabase } from './supabase';\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Configuration\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nNotifications.setNotificationHandler({\\n  handleNotification: async () => ({\\n    shouldShowAlert: true,\\n    shouldPlaySound: true,\\n    shouldSetBadge: true,\\n    shouldShowBanner: true,\\n    shouldShowList: true,\\n  }),\\n});\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Push token registration\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport async function registerForPushNotifications(): Promise<string | null> {\\n  if (!Device.isDevice) {\\n    console.warn('Push notifications require a physical device');\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  const { status: existingStatus } = await Notifications.getPermissionsAsync();\\n  let finalStatus = existingStatus;\\n\\n  if (existingStatus !== 'granted') {\\n    const { status } = await Notifications.requestPermissionsAsync();\\n    finalStatus = status;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (finalStatus !== 'granted') {\\n    console.warn('Push notification permission not granted');\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (Platform.OS === 'android') {\\n    await Notifications.setNotificationChannelAsync('default', {\\n      name: 'Default',\\n      importance: Notifications.AndroidImportance.MAX,\\n      vibrationPattern: [0, 250, 250, 250],\\n      lightColor: '#FF6B35',\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  const tokenData = await Notifications.getExpoPushTokenAsync();\\n  const token = tokenData.data;\\n\\n  await savePushToken(token);\\n\\n  return token;\\n}\\n\\nasync function savePushToken(token: string): Promise<void> {\\n  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\\n  if (!user) throw new Error('Not authenticated');\\n\\n  const { error } = await supabase\\n    .from('push_tokens')\\n    .upsert(\\n      {\\n        user_id: user.id,\\n        token,\\n        platform: Platform.OS,\\n        updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\\n      },\\n      { onConflict: 'user_id,token' },\\n    );\\n\\n  if (error) throw error;\\n}\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Notification handlers\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport function setupNotificationHandlers(): () => void {\\n  const receivedSubscription = Notifications.addNotificationReceivedListener(\\n    (notification) => {\\n      console.log('Notification received:', notification.request.identifier);\\n    },\\n  );\\n\\n  const responseSubscription = Notifications.addNotificationResponseReceivedListener(\\n    (response) => {\\n      const data = response.notification.request.content.data as\\n        | { screen?: string; orderId?: string }\\n        | undefined;\\n\\n      if (data?.screen === 'orders' || data?.orderId) {\\n        router.push('/(tabs)/orders');\\n      }\\n    },\\n  );\\n\\n  return () => {\\n    receivedSubscription.remove();\\n    responseSubscription.remove();\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// Local notifications\\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport async function sendOrderDeliveredNotification(\\n  orderId: string,\\n  recipientName: string,\\n): Promise<string> {\\n  const identifier = await Notifications.scheduleNotificationAsync({\\n    content: {\\n      title: 'Letter Delivered!',\\n      body: `Your letter to ${recipientName} has been delivered.`,\\n      sound: 'default',\\n      data: { screen: 'orders', orderId },\\n    },\\n    trigger: null,\\n  });\\n\\n  return identifier;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AnalyticsProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/notifications.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/notifications.ts\"}\n\n--- RESULT ---\nBoth files are created and verified. Here is a detailed summary of what was created:\n\n---\n\n## File 1: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AnalyticsProvider.tsx`\n\nThis provider follows the exact same patterns as the existing `AuthProvider.tsx` and `ThemeProvider.tsx` -- context with an interface, `createContext<T | undefined>`, exported provider component, and exported hook with a guard.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n\n- **Two-layer architecture**: `AnalyticsProvider` wraps the PostHog SDK's `PostHogProvider`, and an inner `AnalyticsSync` component handles the context value and auth syncing. This separation is needed because `usePostHog()` can only be called inside `PostHogProvider`, so the sync logic lives in a child component.\n\n- **Graceful degradation**: When `POSTHOG_API_KEY` is empty (common in development), the provider returns a context with no-op functions instead of initializing PostHog. This prevents crashes and avoids unnecessary network requests.\n\n- **Auth state syncing** (lines 19-29): Uses `useEffect` watching the `user` from `useAuth()`. When a user signs in, it calls `posthog.identify()` with `user.id`, `email`, and `created_at`. A `useRef` tracks the previous user ID so that `posthog.reset()` is only called on actual sign-out transitions (not on initial mount when user is null).\n\n- **Autocapture configuration** (lines 79-83): Enables `captureScreens`, `captureTouches`, and `captureLifecycleEvents` via the `autocapture` prop, plus `enableSessionReplay` in options.\n\n- **Memoized callbacks**: `capture`, `identify`, and `reset` are wrapped in `useCallback` to provide stable references for consumers.\n\n- **Exported hook**: `useAnalytics()` returns `{ capture, identify, reset }` with the standard guard pattern matching `useAuth()` and `useTheme()`.\n\n---\n\n## File 2: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/services/notifications.ts`\n\nThis service follows the same patterns as the existing services (`api.ts`, `supabase.ts`) -- pure exported async functions, Supabase auth checks with `supabase.auth.getUser()`, and `if (error) throw error` error handling.\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n\n- **Section separators**: Uses the same `// -------------------------------------------------------------------` comment blocks as `api.ts` for visual organization.\n\n- **Global notification handler** (lines 11-19): Calls `Notifications.setNotificationHandler` at module level so foreground notifications display alerts, play sounds, and update badges.\n\n- **`registerForPushNotifications()`** (lines 25-58): Checks `Device.isDevice` (simulators cannot receive push tokens), requests permissions if not already granted, sets up an Android notification channel, gets the Expo push token, and persists it to the `push_tokens` Supabase table via `savePushToken()`.\n\n- **`savePushToken()`** (lines 61-78): Private helper that upserts the token to `push_tokens` with `user_id`, `token`, `platform`, and `updated_at`. Uses `onConflict: 'user_id,token'` to avoid duplicates. Follows the same auth guard pattern (`if (!user) throw new Error('Not authenticated')`) used throughout `api.ts`.\n\n- **`setupNotificationHandlers()`** (lines 84-107): Registers two listeners -- one for notifications received while the app is foregrounded (logs the identifier), and one for notification responses (user taps). The response handler reads `data.screen` or `data.orderId` from the notification payload and deep links to `/(tabs)/orders` using `expo-router`. Returns a cleanup function that removes both subscriptions, suitable for use in a `useEffect`.\n\n- **`sendOrderDeliveredNotification()`** (lines 113-128): Schedules an immediate local notification (`trigger: null`) with a title, body referencing the recipient name, default sound, and data payload containing the `orderId` and `screen: 'orders'` for deep linking when tapped.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nu7h6rCNtPhmpDZ4wGxGyh","type":"tool_result","content":"<retrieval_status>success</retrieval_status>\n\n<task_id>a0f9a54</task_id>\n\n<task_type>local_agent</task_type>\n\n<status>completed</status>\n\n<output>\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.tsx\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.ts\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/config.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AuthProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/send.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/colors.ts\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react';\\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\\nimport Purchases, {\\n  type PurchasesOfferings,\\n  type PurchasesPackage,\\n  type CustomerInfo,\\n} from 'react-native-purchases';\\nimport { REVENUECAT_API_KEY, TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useAuth } from '@/providers/AuthProvider';\\n\\ninterface BillingContextType {\\n  tier: TierName;\\n  isSubscribed: boolean;\\n  offerings: PurchasesOfferings | null;\\n  purchasePackage: (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => Promise<void>;\\n  restorePurchases: () => Promise<void>;\\n  isLoading: boolean;\\n  canUseProduct: (productType: string) => boolean;\\n  checkUsageLimit: (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free) => boolean;\\n}\\n\\nconst BillingContext = createContext<BillingContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nfunction determineTier(customerInfo: CustomerInfo): TierName {\\n  const entitlements = customerInfo.entitlements.active;\\n  if (entitlements['business']) return 'business';\\n  if (entitlements['pro']) return 'pro';\\n  return 'free';\\n}\\n\\nexport function BillingProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\n  const { user } = useAuth();\\n  const [tier, setTier] = useState<TierName>('free');\\n  const [offerings, setOfferings] = useState<PurchasesOfferings | null>(null);\\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\\n\\n  // Initialize RevenueCat on mount\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function init() {\\n      try {\\n        Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY });\\n\\n        const fetchedOfferings = await Purchases.getOfferings();\\n        setOfferings(fetchedOfferings);\\n\\n        const customerInfo = await Purchases.getCustomerInfo();\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('BillingProvider init error:', error);\\n      } finally {\\n        setIsLoading(false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    init();\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Identify user when auth changes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function identify() {\\n      if (!user?.id) return;\\n      try {\\n        const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.logIn(user.id);\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('RevenueCat identify error:', error);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    identify();\\n  }, [user?.id]);\\n\\n  // Listen for customer info updates\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const listener = (info: CustomerInfo) => {\\n      setTier(determineTier(info));\\n    };\\n    Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    return () => {\\n      Purchases.removeCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const purchasePackage = useCallback(async (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error: any) {\\n      if (!error.userCancelled) {\\n        throw error;\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const restorePurchases = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const customerInfo = await Purchases.restorePurchases();\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      throw error;\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const isSubscribed = tier !== 'free';\\n\\n  const canUseProduct = useCallback(\\n    (productType: string): boolean => {\\n      const tierConfig = TIERS[tier];\\n      return tierConfig.products.includes(productType as any);\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  const checkUsageLimit = useCallback(\\n    (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free): boolean => {\\n      const limit = TIERS[tier][field];\\n      if (typeof limit !== 'number') return false;\\n      if (limit === -1) return true; // unlimited\\n      return usage < limit;\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  return (\\n    <BillingContext.Provider\\n      value={{\\n        tier,\\n        isSubscribed,\\n        offerings,\\n        purchasePackage,\\n        restorePurchases,\\n        isLoading,\\n        canUseProduct,\\n        checkUsageLimit,\\n      }}\\n    >\\n      {children}\\n    </BillingContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function useBilling() {\\n  const context = useContext(BillingContext);\\n  if (!context) throw new Error('useBilling must be used within BillingProvider');\\n  return context;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport {\\n  View,\\n  Text,\\n  ScrollView,\\n  TouchableOpacity,\\n  StyleSheet,\\n  Alert,\\n  ActivityIndicator,\\n} from 'react-native';\\nimport { useRouter } from 'expo-router';\\nimport { TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useBilling } from '@/providers/BillingProvider';\\nimport { useTheme } from '@/providers/ThemeProvider';\\nimport { Check, Crown, Star, Zap } from 'lucide-react-native';\\n\\nconst TIER_KEYS: TierName[] = ['free', 'pro', 'business'];\\n\\nconst TIER_META: Record<TierName, { icon: typeof Crown; tagline: string; badge: string | null }> = {\\n  free: { icon: Zap, tagline: 'Get started with the basics', badge: null },\\n  pro: { icon: Star, tagline: 'For individuals who send regularly', badge: 'Most Popular' },\\n  business: { icon: Crown, tagline: 'Unlimited power for your business', badge: 'Best Value' },\\n};\\n\\nconst FEATURE_ROWS: { label: string; field: keyof typeof TIERS.free }[] = [\\n  { label: 'Letter generations / mo', field: 'letterGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Image generations / mo', field: 'imageGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Letters sent / mo', field: 'lettersSent' },\\n];\\n\\nfunction formatLimit(value: number): string {\\n  if (value === -1) return 'Unlimited';\\n  return String(value);\\n}\\n\\nfunction formatProducts(products: readonly string[]): string {\\n  const names: Record<string, string> = {\\n    postcard: 'Postcards',\\n    letter: 'Letters',\\n    greeting: 'Greeting Cards',\\n    windowless_letter: 'Windowless Letters',\\n    giftcard: 'Gift Cards',\\n  };\\n  return products.map((p) => names[p] || p).join(', ');\\n}\\n\\nexport default function PaywallScreen() {\\n  const { colors } = useTheme();\\n  const router = useRouter();\\n  const {\\n    tier: currentTier,\\n    offerings,\\n    purchasePackage,\\n    restorePurchases,\\n    isLoading,\\n  } = useBilling();\\n\\n  const [purchasing, setPurchasing] = useState<TierName | null>(null);\\n\\n  const handlePurchase = async (tierKey: TierName) => {\\n    if (tierKey === 'free' || tierKey === currentTier) return;\\n\\n    const currentOffering = offerings?.current;\\n    if (!currentOffering) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', 'Subscription packages are not available right now. Please try again later.');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Match the RevenueCat package identifier to the tier\\n    const pkg = currentOffering.availablePackages.find((p) =>\\n      p.identifier.toLowerCase().includes(tierKey),\\n    );\\n\\n    if (!pkg) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', `The ${TIERS[tierKey].name} package could not be found.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    setPurchasing(tierKey);\\n    try {\\n      await purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      Alert.alert('Success', `You are now on the ${TIERS[tierKey].name} plan!`, [\\n        { text: 'OK', onPress: () => router.back() },\\n      ]);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Purchase Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Something went wrong.');\\n    } finally {\\n      setPurchasing(null);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleRestore = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      await restorePurchases();\\n      Alert.alert('Restored', 'Your purchases have been restored.');\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Restore Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Could not restore purchases.');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const s = StyleSheet.create({\\n    container: { flex: 1, backgroundColor: colors.background },\\n    content: { padding: 16, paddingBottom: 60 },\\n    header: { fontSize: 28, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 8 },\\n    subtitle: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textSecondary, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 6, marginBottom: 24 },\\n    card: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.card,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      borderWidth: 1,\\n      borderColor: colors.border,\\n      padding: 20,\\n      marginBottom: 16,\\n    },\\n    cardHighlighted: {\\n      borderColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderWidth: 2,\\n    },\\n    badgeContainer: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: -12,\\n      alignSelf: 'center',\\n      left: 0,\\n      right: 0,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n    },\\n    badge: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      paddingHorizontal: 14,\\n      paddingVertical: 4,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n    },\\n    badgeText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 12, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    cardHeader: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    tierName: { fontSize: 22, fontWeight: '700', color: colors.text },\\n    tagline: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textMuted, marginBottom: 12 },\\n    priceRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'baseline', marginBottom: 16 },\\n    price: { fontSize: 36, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text },\\n    priceUnit: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textMuted, marginLeft: 4 },\\n    divider: { height: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth, backgroundColor: colors.border, marginVertical: 14 },\\n    featureRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 10 },\\n    featureText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textSecondary, flex: 1 },\\n    featureValue: { fontSize: 14, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.text },\\n    productsLabel: { fontSize: 13, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.textMuted, marginTop: 4, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    productsText: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textSecondary, lineHeight: 18 },\\n    purchaseButton: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n      paddingVertical: 14,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n      marginTop: 16,\\n    },\\n    purchaseButtonDisabled: { opacity: 0.5 },\\n    purchaseButtonCurrent: { backgroundColor: colors.successLight },\\n    purchaseButtonText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 16, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    purchaseButtonTextCurrent: { color: colors.success },\\n    currentBadge: {\\n      flexDirection: 'row',\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      gap: 6,\\n    },\\n    restoreButton: {\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      paddingVertical: 16,\\n      marginTop: 8,\\n    },\\n    restoreText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textMuted, textDecorationLine: 'underline' },\\n    closeButton: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: 16,\\n      right: 16,\\n      zIndex: 10,\\n      width: 32,\\n      height: 32,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      backgroundColor: colors.surface,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n    },\\n    closeText: { fontSize: 18, color: colors.textSecondary, fontWeight: '600' },\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <ScrollView style={s.container} contentContainerStyle={s.content}>\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.closeButton} onPress={() => router.back()}>\\n        <Text style={s.closeText}>X</Text>\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n\\n      <Text style={s.header}>Choose Your Plan</Text>\\n      <Text style={s.subtitle}>Unlock more letters, designs, and products</Text>\\n\\n      {TIER_KEYS.map((tierKey) => {\\n        const config = TIERS[tierKey];\\n        const meta = TIER_META[tierKey];\\n        const Icon = meta.icon;\\n        const isCurrent = tierKey === currentTier;\\n        const isHighlighted = tierKey === 'pro';\\n        const isPurchasing = purchasing === tierKey;\\n        const isDisabled = isLoading || isPurchasing || isCurrent || tierKey === 'free';\\n\\n        return (\\n          <View key={tierKey} style={[s.card, isHighlighted && s.cardHighlighted]}>\\n            {meta.badge && (\\n              <View style={s.badgeContainer}>\\n                <View style={s.badge}>\\n                  <Text style={s.badgeText}>{meta.badge}</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              </View>\\n            )}\\n\\n            <View style={s.cardHeader}>\\n              <Icon size={24} color={colors.primary} />\\n              <Text style={s.tierName}>{config.name}</Text>\\n            </View>\\n            <Text style={s.tagline}>{meta.tagline}</Text>\\n\\n            <View style={s.priceRow}>\\n              <Text style={s.price}>\\n                {config.price === 0 ? 'Free' : `$${config.price}`}\\n              </Text>\\n              {config.price > 0 && <Text style={s.priceUnit}>/mo</Text>}\\n            </View>\\n\\n            <View style={s.divider} />\\n\\n            {FEATURE_ROWS.map((feat) => (\\n              <View key={feat.field} style={s.featureRow}>\\n                <Check size={16} color={colors.success} />\\n                <Text style={s.featureText}>{feat.label}</Text>\\n                <Text style={s.featureValue}>\\n                  {formatLimit(config[feat.field] as number)}\\n                </Text>\\n              </View>\\n            ))}\\n\\n            <Text style={s.productsLabel}>Available Products</Text>\\n            <Text style={s.productsText}>{formatProducts(config.products)}</Text>\\n\\n            <TouchableOpacity\\n              style={[\\n                s.purchaseButton,\\n                isCurrent && s.purchaseButtonCurrent,\\n                isDisabled && s.purchaseButtonDisabled,\\n              ]}\\n              onPress={() => handlePurchase(tierKey)}\\n              disabled={isDisabled}\\n            >\\n              {isPurchasing ? (\\n                <ActivityIndicator color=\\\"#fff\\\" />\\n              ) : isCurrent ? (\\n                <View style={s.currentBadge}>\\n                  <Check size={18} color={colors.success} />\\n                  <Text style={s.purchaseButtonTextCurrent}>Current Plan</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              ) : tierKey === 'free' ? (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>Free Forever</Text>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>\\n                  Subscribe to {config.name} - ${config.price}/mo\\n                </Text>\\n              )}\\n            </TouchableOpacity>\\n          </View>\\n        );\\n      })}\\n\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.restoreButton} onPress={handleRestore} disabled={isLoading}>\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <ActivityIndicator color={colors.textMuted} />\\n        ) : (\\n          <Text style={s.restoreText}>Restore Purchases</Text>\\n        )}\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n    </ScrollView>\\n  );\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n\n--- RESULT ---\nBoth files are created and verified. Here is a summary of what was built:\n\n---\n\n## File 1: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx`\n\n**RevenueCat Billing Provider** -- 150 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Context interface** (`BillingContextType`) exposes: `tier`, `isSubscribed`, `offerings`, `purchasePackage`, `restorePurchases`, `isLoading`, `canUseProduct`, `checkUsageLimit`\n- **Initialization** (lines 38-55): Calls `Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY })` on mount, then immediately fetches offerings and customer info to determine the starting tier.\n- **User identification** (lines 58-69): When `user?.id` changes (from `useAuth()`), calls `Purchases.logIn(user.id)` to associate the Supabase user with RevenueCat and re-reads the tier from the returned `customerInfo`.\n- **Live listener** (lines 72-80): Registers `Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener` so tier changes made externally (e.g., from App Store subscription management) are reflected in real time. Cleans up on unmount.\n- **`determineTier` helper** (lines 24-29): Checks `customerInfo.entitlements.active` for `'business'` first, then `'pro'`, defaulting to `'free'`.\n- **`purchasePackage`** (lines 82-94): Wraps `Purchases.purchasePackage()`, sets loading state, updates tier on success, and silently swallows user-cancelled errors (via `error.userCancelled`).\n- **`restorePurchases`** (lines 96-106): Wraps `Purchases.restorePurchases()`, updates tier from the restored `CustomerInfo`.\n- **`canUseProduct`** (lines 110-116): Checks whether the current tier's `products` array includes the given product type string.\n- **`checkUsageLimit`** (lines 118-126): Compares a numeric usage count against the tier's configured limit for a given field; returns `true` if unlimited (`-1`) or if usage is below the limit.\n- **`useBilling()` hook** (lines 146-150): Standard context consumer with a descriptive error if used outside the provider.\n\nAll types (`TierName`, `TIERS`, `REVENUECAT_API_KEY`) are imported from `@/constants/config`, and `useAuth` from `@/providers/AuthProvider`, matching the existing codebase patterns.\n\n---\n\n## File 2: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx`\n\n**Paywall Screen** -- 276 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Imports**: Uses `TIERS` and `TierName` from `@/constants/config`, `useBilling` from `@/providers/BillingProvider`, `useTheme` from `@/providers/ThemeProvider`, and `{ Check, Crown, Star, Zap }` from `lucide-react-native`.\n- **Tier cards**: Renders all three tiers (Free, Pro at $29/mo, Business at $99/mo) using a `TIER_KEYS` array and a `TIER_META` record that maps each tier to an icon, tagline, and optional badge label (\"Most Popular\" for Pro, \"Best Value\" for Business).\n- **Feature comparison**: Each card shows letter generations/mo, image generations/mo, and letters sent/mo with values pulled directly from `TIERS[tierKey]`, formatted via `formatLimit()` (which renders `-1` as \"Unlimited\"). An \"Available Products\" section lists the product types in human-readable form.\n- **Purchase flow**: The \"Subscribe\" button calls `handlePurchase(tierKey)`, which looks up the matching `PurchasesPackage` from `offerings.current.availablePackages` by matching on the tier name in the identifier, then delegates to `purchasePackage(pkg)` from the billing context. Shows a success alert and navigates back.\n- **Current plan indicator**: If a tier matches `currentTier`, the button shows a green \"Current Plan\" label with a check icon and is disabled.\n- **Loading states**: Per-tier `purchasing` state shows an `ActivityIndicator` on the button being purchased. The global `isLoading` from billing disables all buttons.\n- **Restore purchases**: A button at the bottom calls `restorePurchases()` from the billing context, with error handling via `Alert`.\n- **Close button**: Top-right close button calls `router.back()`.\n- **Styling**: Uses the same `const s = StyleSheet.create({...})` pattern inside the component body with `colors` from `useTheme()`, consistent with `send.tsx`, `settings.tsx`, and other existing screens. Uses `colors.card`, `colors.border`, `colors.primary`, `colors.success`, `colors.successLight`, `colors.text`, `colors.textSecondary`, `colors.textMuted`, `colors.surface`, and `colors.background`.\n- **Modal presentation**: The file is created at `app/paywall.tsx`. Expo Router will auto-register it. The existing `_layout.tsx` was not modified as requested -- in Expo Router, the screen will render as a regular stack screen and can be presented modally by adding a `<Stack.Screen name=\"paywall\" options={{ presentation: 'modal' }} />` entry to `_layout.tsx` when ready.\n</output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c21e72c-e8bd-4a15-a613-a3101b4dd352","uuid":"1e484fa1-9944-455f-b57e-90fc86d5ae80","tool_use_result":{"retrieval_status":"success","task":{"task_id":"a0f9a54","task_type":"local_agent","status":"completed","description":"Create BillingProvider and paywall","output":"[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.tsx\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.ts\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/config.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AuthProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/send.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/colors.ts\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react';\\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\\nimport Purchases, {\\n  type PurchasesOfferings,\\n  type PurchasesPackage,\\n  type CustomerInfo,\\n} from 'react-native-purchases';\\nimport { REVENUECAT_API_KEY, TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useAuth } from '@/providers/AuthProvider';\\n\\ninterface BillingContextType {\\n  tier: TierName;\\n  isSubscribed: boolean;\\n  offerings: PurchasesOfferings | null;\\n  purchasePackage: (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => Promise<void>;\\n  restorePurchases: () => Promise<void>;\\n  isLoading: boolean;\\n  canUseProduct: (productType: string) => boolean;\\n  checkUsageLimit: (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free) => boolean;\\n}\\n\\nconst BillingContext = createContext<BillingContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nfunction determineTier(customerInfo: CustomerInfo): TierName {\\n  const entitlements = customerInfo.entitlements.active;\\n  if (entitlements['business']) return 'business';\\n  if (entitlements['pro']) return 'pro';\\n  return 'free';\\n}\\n\\nexport function BillingProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\n  const { user } = useAuth();\\n  const [tier, setTier] = useState<TierName>('free');\\n  const [offerings, setOfferings] = useState<PurchasesOfferings | null>(null);\\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\\n\\n  // Initialize RevenueCat on mount\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function init() {\\n      try {\\n        Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY });\\n\\n        const fetchedOfferings = await Purchases.getOfferings();\\n        setOfferings(fetchedOfferings);\\n\\n        const customerInfo = await Purchases.getCustomerInfo();\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('BillingProvider init error:', error);\\n      } finally {\\n        setIsLoading(false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    init();\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Identify user when auth changes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function identify() {\\n      if (!user?.id) return;\\n      try {\\n        const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.logIn(user.id);\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('RevenueCat identify error:', error);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    identify();\\n  }, [user?.id]);\\n\\n  // Listen for customer info updates\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const listener = (info: CustomerInfo) => {\\n      setTier(determineTier(info));\\n    };\\n    Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    return () => {\\n      Purchases.removeCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const purchasePackage = useCallback(async (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error: any) {\\n      if (!error.userCancelled) {\\n        throw error;\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const restorePurchases = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const customerInfo = await Purchases.restorePurchases();\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      throw error;\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const isSubscribed = tier !== 'free';\\n\\n  const canUseProduct = useCallback(\\n    (productType: string): boolean => {\\n      const tierConfig = TIERS[tier];\\n      return tierConfig.products.includes(productType as any);\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  const checkUsageLimit = useCallback(\\n    (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free): boolean => {\\n      const limit = TIERS[tier][field];\\n      if (typeof limit !== 'number') return false;\\n      if (limit === -1) return true; // unlimited\\n      return usage < limit;\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  return (\\n    <BillingContext.Provider\\n      value={{\\n        tier,\\n        isSubscribed,\\n        offerings,\\n        purchasePackage,\\n        restorePurchases,\\n        isLoading,\\n        canUseProduct,\\n        checkUsageLimit,\\n      }}\\n    >\\n      {children}\\n    </BillingContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function useBilling() {\\n  const context = useContext(BillingContext);\\n  if (!context) throw new Error('useBilling must be used within BillingProvider');\\n  return context;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport {\\n  View,\\n  Text,\\n  ScrollView,\\n  TouchableOpacity,\\n  StyleSheet,\\n  Alert,\\n  ActivityIndicator,\\n} from 'react-native';\\nimport { useRouter } from 'expo-router';\\nimport { TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useBilling } from '@/providers/BillingProvider';\\nimport { useTheme } from '@/providers/ThemeProvider';\\nimport { Check, Crown, Star, Zap } from 'lucide-react-native';\\n\\nconst TIER_KEYS: TierName[] = ['free', 'pro', 'business'];\\n\\nconst TIER_META: Record<TierName, { icon: typeof Crown; tagline: string; badge: string | null }> = {\\n  free: { icon: Zap, tagline: 'Get started with the basics', badge: null },\\n  pro: { icon: Star, tagline: 'For individuals who send regularly', badge: 'Most Popular' },\\n  business: { icon: Crown, tagline: 'Unlimited power for your business', badge: 'Best Value' },\\n};\\n\\nconst FEATURE_ROWS: { label: string; field: keyof typeof TIERS.free }[] = [\\n  { label: 'Letter generations / mo', field: 'letterGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Image generations / mo', field: 'imageGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Letters sent / mo', field: 'lettersSent' },\\n];\\n\\nfunction formatLimit(value: number): string {\\n  if (value === -1) return 'Unlimited';\\n  return String(value);\\n}\\n\\nfunction formatProducts(products: readonly string[]): string {\\n  const names: Record<string, string> = {\\n    postcard: 'Postcards',\\n    letter: 'Letters',\\n    greeting: 'Greeting Cards',\\n    windowless_letter: 'Windowless Letters',\\n    giftcard: 'Gift Cards',\\n  };\\n  return products.map((p) => names[p] || p).join(', ');\\n}\\n\\nexport default function PaywallScreen() {\\n  const { colors } = useTheme();\\n  const router = useRouter();\\n  const {\\n    tier: currentTier,\\n    offerings,\\n    purchasePackage,\\n    restorePurchases,\\n    isLoading,\\n  } = useBilling();\\n\\n  const [purchasing, setPurchasing] = useState<TierName | null>(null);\\n\\n  const handlePurchase = async (tierKey: TierName) => {\\n    if (tierKey === 'free' || tierKey === currentTier) return;\\n\\n    const currentOffering = offerings?.current;\\n    if (!currentOffering) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', 'Subscription packages are not available right now. Please try again later.');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Match the RevenueCat package identifier to the tier\\n    const pkg = currentOffering.availablePackages.find((p) =>\\n      p.identifier.toLowerCase().includes(tierKey),\\n    );\\n\\n    if (!pkg) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', `The ${TIERS[tierKey].name} package could not be found.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    setPurchasing(tierKey);\\n    try {\\n      await purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      Alert.alert('Success', `You are now on the ${TIERS[tierKey].name} plan!`, [\\n        { text: 'OK', onPress: () => router.back() },\\n      ]);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Purchase Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Something went wrong.');\\n    } finally {\\n      setPurchasing(null);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleRestore = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      await restorePurchases();\\n      Alert.alert('Restored', 'Your purchases have been restored.');\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Restore Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Could not restore purchases.');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const s = StyleSheet.create({\\n    container: { flex: 1, backgroundColor: colors.background },\\n    content: { padding: 16, paddingBottom: 60 },\\n    header: { fontSize: 28, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 8 },\\n    subtitle: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textSecondary, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 6, marginBottom: 24 },\\n    card: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.card,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      borderWidth: 1,\\n      borderColor: colors.border,\\n      padding: 20,\\n      marginBottom: 16,\\n    },\\n    cardHighlighted: {\\n      borderColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderWidth: 2,\\n    },\\n    badgeContainer: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: -12,\\n      alignSelf: 'center',\\n      left: 0,\\n      right: 0,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n    },\\n    badge: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      paddingHorizontal: 14,\\n      paddingVertical: 4,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n    },\\n    badgeText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 12, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    cardHeader: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    tierName: { fontSize: 22, fontWeight: '700', color: colors.text },\\n    tagline: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textMuted, marginBottom: 12 },\\n    priceRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'baseline', marginBottom: 16 },\\n    price: { fontSize: 36, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text },\\n    priceUnit: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textMuted, marginLeft: 4 },\\n    divider: { height: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth, backgroundColor: colors.border, marginVertical: 14 },\\n    featureRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 10 },\\n    featureText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textSecondary, flex: 1 },\\n    featureValue: { fontSize: 14, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.text },\\n    productsLabel: { fontSize: 13, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.textMuted, marginTop: 4, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    productsText: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textSecondary, lineHeight: 18 },\\n    purchaseButton: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n      paddingVertical: 14,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n      marginTop: 16,\\n    },\\n    purchaseButtonDisabled: { opacity: 0.5 },\\n    purchaseButtonCurrent: { backgroundColor: colors.successLight },\\n    purchaseButtonText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 16, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    purchaseButtonTextCurrent: { color: colors.success },\\n    currentBadge: {\\n      flexDirection: 'row',\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      gap: 6,\\n    },\\n    restoreButton: {\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      paddingVertical: 16,\\n      marginTop: 8,\\n    },\\n    restoreText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textMuted, textDecorationLine: 'underline' },\\n    closeButton: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: 16,\\n      right: 16,\\n      zIndex: 10,\\n      width: 32,\\n      height: 32,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      backgroundColor: colors.surface,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n    },\\n    closeText: { fontSize: 18, color: colors.textSecondary, fontWeight: '600' },\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <ScrollView style={s.container} contentContainerStyle={s.content}>\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.closeButton} onPress={() => router.back()}>\\n        <Text style={s.closeText}>X</Text>\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n\\n      <Text style={s.header}>Choose Your Plan</Text>\\n      <Text style={s.subtitle}>Unlock more letters, designs, and products</Text>\\n\\n      {TIER_KEYS.map((tierKey) => {\\n        const config = TIERS[tierKey];\\n        const meta = TIER_META[tierKey];\\n        const Icon = meta.icon;\\n        const isCurrent = tierKey === currentTier;\\n        const isHighlighted = tierKey === 'pro';\\n        const isPurchasing = purchasing === tierKey;\\n        const isDisabled = isLoading || isPurchasing || isCurrent || tierKey === 'free';\\n\\n        return (\\n          <View key={tierKey} style={[s.card, isHighlighted && s.cardHighlighted]}>\\n            {meta.badge && (\\n              <View style={s.badgeContainer}>\\n                <View style={s.badge}>\\n                  <Text style={s.badgeText}>{meta.badge}</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              </View>\\n            )}\\n\\n            <View style={s.cardHeader}>\\n              <Icon size={24} color={colors.primary} />\\n              <Text style={s.tierName}>{config.name}</Text>\\n            </View>\\n            <Text style={s.tagline}>{meta.tagline}</Text>\\n\\n            <View style={s.priceRow}>\\n              <Text style={s.price}>\\n                {config.price === 0 ? 'Free' : `$${config.price}`}\\n              </Text>\\n              {config.price > 0 && <Text style={s.priceUnit}>/mo</Text>}\\n            </View>\\n\\n            <View style={s.divider} />\\n\\n            {FEATURE_ROWS.map((feat) => (\\n              <View key={feat.field} style={s.featureRow}>\\n                <Check size={16} color={colors.success} />\\n                <Text style={s.featureText}>{feat.label}</Text>\\n                <Text style={s.featureValue}>\\n                  {formatLimit(config[feat.field] as number)}\\n                </Text>\\n              </View>\\n            ))}\\n\\n            <Text style={s.productsLabel}>Available Products</Text>\\n            <Text style={s.productsText}>{formatProducts(config.products)}</Text>\\n\\n            <TouchableOpacity\\n              style={[\\n                s.purchaseButton,\\n                isCurrent && s.purchaseButtonCurrent,\\n                isDisabled && s.purchaseButtonDisabled,\\n              ]}\\n              onPress={() => handlePurchase(tierKey)}\\n              disabled={isDisabled}\\n            >\\n              {isPurchasing ? (\\n                <ActivityIndicator color=\\\"#fff\\\" />\\n              ) : isCurrent ? (\\n                <View style={s.currentBadge}>\\n                  <Check size={18} color={colors.success} />\\n                  <Text style={s.purchaseButtonTextCurrent}>Current Plan</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              ) : tierKey === 'free' ? (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>Free Forever</Text>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>\\n                  Subscribe to {config.name} - ${config.price}/mo\\n                </Text>\\n              )}\\n            </TouchableOpacity>\\n          </View>\\n        );\\n      })}\\n\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.restoreButton} onPress={handleRestore} disabled={isLoading}>\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <ActivityIndicator color={colors.textMuted} />\\n        ) : (\\n          <Text style={s.restoreText}>Restore Purchases</Text>\\n        )}\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n    </ScrollView>\\n  );\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n\n--- RESULT ---\nBoth files are created and verified. Here is a summary of what was built:\n\n---\n\n## File 1: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx`\n\n**RevenueCat Billing Provider** -- 150 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Context interface** (`BillingContextType`) exposes: `tier`, `isSubscribed`, `offerings`, `purchasePackage`, `restorePurchases`, `isLoading`, `canUseProduct`, `checkUsageLimit`\n- **Initialization** (lines 38-55): Calls `Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY })` on mount, then immediately fetches offerings and customer info to determine the starting tier.\n- **User identification** (lines 58-69): When `user?.id` changes (from `useAuth()`), calls `Purchases.logIn(user.id)` to associate the Supabase user with RevenueCat and re-reads the tier from the returned `customerInfo`.\n- **Live listener** (lines 72-80): Registers `Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener` so tier changes made externally (e.g., from App Store subscription management) are reflected in real time. Cleans up on unmount.\n- **`determineTier` helper** (lines 24-29): Checks `customerInfo.entitlements.active` for `'business'` first, then `'pro'`, defaulting to `'free'`.\n- **`purchasePackage`** (lines 82-94): Wraps `Purchases.purchasePackage()`, sets loading state, updates tier on success, and silently swallows user-cancelled errors (via `error.userCancelled`).\n- **`restorePurchases`** (lines 96-106): Wraps `Purchases.restorePurchases()`, updates tier from the restored `CustomerInfo`.\n- **`canUseProduct`** (lines 110-116): Checks whether the current tier's `products` array includes the given product type string.\n- **`checkUsageLimit`** (lines 118-126): Compares a numeric usage count against the tier's configured limit for a given field; returns `true` if unlimited (`-1`) or if usage is below the limit.\n- **`useBilling()` hook** (lines 146-150): Standard context consumer with a descriptive error if used outside the provider.\n\nAll types (`TierName`, `TIERS`, `REVENUECAT_API_KEY`) are imported from `@/constants/config`, and `useAuth` from `@/providers/AuthProvider`, matching the existing codebase patterns.\n\n---\n\n## File 2: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx`\n\n**Paywall Screen** -- 276 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Imports**: Uses `TIERS` and `TierName` from `@/constants/config`, `useBilling` from `@/providers/BillingProvider`, `useTheme` from `@/providers/ThemeProvider`, and `{ Check, Crown, Star, Zap }` from `lucide-react-native`.\n- **Tier cards**: Renders all three tiers (Free, Pro at $29/mo, Business at $99/mo) using a `TIER_KEYS` array and a `TIER_META` record that maps each tier to an icon, tagline, and optional badge label (\"Most Popular\" for Pro, \"Best Value\" for Business).\n- **Feature comparison**: Each card shows letter generations/mo, image generations/mo, and letters sent/mo with values pulled directly from `TIERS[tierKey]`, formatted via `formatLimit()` (which renders `-1` as \"Unlimited\"). An \"Available Products\" section lists the product types in human-readable form.\n- **Purchase flow**: The \"Subscribe\" button calls `handlePurchase(tierKey)`, which looks up the matching `PurchasesPackage` from `offerings.current.availablePackages` by matching on the tier name in the identifier, then delegates to `purchasePackage(pkg)` from the billing context. Shows a success alert and navigates back.\n- **Current plan indicator**: If a tier matches `currentTier`, the button shows a green \"Current Plan\" label with a check icon and is disabled.\n- **Loading states**: Per-tier `purchasing` state shows an `ActivityIndicator` on the button being purchased. The global `isLoading` from billing disables all buttons.\n- **Restore purchases**: A button at the bottom calls `restorePurchases()` from the billing context, with error handling via `Alert`.\n- **Close button**: Top-right close button calls `router.back()`.\n- **Styling**: Uses the same `const s = StyleSheet.create({...})` pattern inside the component body with `colors` from `useTheme()`, consistent with `send.tsx`, `settings.tsx`, and other existing screens. Uses `colors.card`, `colors.border`, `colors.primary`, `colors.success`, `colors.successLight`, `colors.text`, `colors.textSecondary`, `colors.textMuted`, `colors.surface`, and `colors.background`.\n- **Modal presentation**: The file is created at `app/paywall.tsx`. Expo Router will auto-register it. The existing `_layout.tsx` was not modified as requested -- in Expo Router, the screen will render as a regular stack screen and can be presented modally by adding a `<Stack.Screen name=\"paywall\" options={{ presentation: 'modal' }} />` entry to `_layout.tsx` when ready.\n","prompt":"Create two files for the SteadyLetters iOS Expo app at /Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios:\n\n1. **providers/BillingProvider.tsx** - RevenueCat billing provider with:\n   - Import Purchases from 'react-native-purchases'\n   - Import REVENUECAT_API_KEY from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useAuth from '@/providers/AuthProvider'\n   - React context exposing: tier (TierName), isSubscribed, offerings, purchasePackage, restorePurchases, isLoading\n   - Initialize Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY }) on mount\n   - Identify user with Supabase user.id when auth changes\n   - Check entitlements to determine tier ('pro' or 'business' entitlements, default 'free')\n   - purchasePackage function calls Purchases.purchasePackage()\n   - restorePurchases function calls Purchases.restorePurchases()\n   - Gate features: canUseProduct(productType) checks tier\n   - checkUsageLimit(usage, field) compares against TIERS limits\n   - useBilling() hook\n\n2. **app/paywall.tsx** - Paywall screen with:\n   - Import TIERS, TierName from '@/constants/config'\n   - Import useBilling from '@/providers/BillingProvider'\n   - Import useTheme from '@/providers/ThemeProvider'\n   - Display Free, Pro ($29/mo), Business ($99/mo) tiers in cards\n   - Feature comparison list for each tier\n   - Purchase buttons that call purchasePackage\n   - Restore purchases button at bottom\n   - Loading state while purchasing\n   - Current plan indicator\n   - Modal presentation style\n   - Register as modal in app/_layout.tsx (DO NOT modify _layout.tsx, just create paywall.tsx)\n   - Use lucide-react-native icons: Check, Crown, Star, Zap\n\nUse real RevenueCat SDK patterns. Use the same styling patterns as other screens (useTheme(), StyleSheet.create, colors object). Import TierName from '@/constants/config'.","result":"[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.tsx\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Glob] {\"pattern\":\"**/*.ts\",\"path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/config.ts\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/AuthProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/_layout.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/send.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/constants/colors.ts\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react';\\nimport { Platform } from 'react-native';\\nimport Purchases, {\\n  type PurchasesOfferings,\\n  type PurchasesPackage,\\n  type CustomerInfo,\\n} from 'react-native-purchases';\\nimport { REVENUECAT_API_KEY, TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useAuth } from '@/providers/AuthProvider';\\n\\ninterface BillingContextType {\\n  tier: TierName;\\n  isSubscribed: boolean;\\n  offerings: PurchasesOfferings | null;\\n  purchasePackage: (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => Promise<void>;\\n  restorePurchases: () => Promise<void>;\\n  isLoading: boolean;\\n  canUseProduct: (productType: string) => boolean;\\n  checkUsageLimit: (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free) => boolean;\\n}\\n\\nconst BillingContext = createContext<BillingContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nfunction determineTier(customerInfo: CustomerInfo): TierName {\\n  const entitlements = customerInfo.entitlements.active;\\n  if (entitlements['business']) return 'business';\\n  if (entitlements['pro']) return 'pro';\\n  return 'free';\\n}\\n\\nexport function BillingProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\\n  const { user } = useAuth();\\n  const [tier, setTier] = useState<TierName>('free');\\n  const [offerings, setOfferings] = useState<PurchasesOfferings | null>(null);\\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\\n\\n  // Initialize RevenueCat on mount\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function init() {\\n      try {\\n        Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY });\\n\\n        const fetchedOfferings = await Purchases.getOfferings();\\n        setOfferings(fetchedOfferings);\\n\\n        const customerInfo = await Purchases.getCustomerInfo();\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('BillingProvider init error:', error);\\n      } finally {\\n        setIsLoading(false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    init();\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Identify user when auth changes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    async function identify() {\\n      if (!user?.id) return;\\n      try {\\n        const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.logIn(user.id);\\n        setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        console.error('RevenueCat identify error:', error);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    identify();\\n  }, [user?.id]);\\n\\n  // Listen for customer info updates\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const listener = (info: CustomerInfo) => {\\n      setTier(determineTier(info));\\n    };\\n    Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    return () => {\\n      Purchases.removeCustomerInfoUpdateListener(listener);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const purchasePackage = useCallback(async (pkg: PurchasesPackage) => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const { customerInfo } = await Purchases.purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error: any) {\\n      if (!error.userCancelled) {\\n        throw error;\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const restorePurchases = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setIsLoading(true);\\n    try {\\n      const customerInfo = await Purchases.restorePurchases();\\n      setTier(determineTier(customerInfo));\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      throw error;\\n    } finally {\\n      setIsLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const isSubscribed = tier !== 'free';\\n\\n  const canUseProduct = useCallback(\\n    (productType: string): boolean => {\\n      const tierConfig = TIERS[tier];\\n      return tierConfig.products.includes(productType as any);\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  const checkUsageLimit = useCallback(\\n    (usage: number, field: keyof typeof TIERS.free): boolean => {\\n      const limit = TIERS[tier][field];\\n      if (typeof limit !== 'number') return false;\\n      if (limit === -1) return true; // unlimited\\n      return usage < limit;\\n    },\\n    [tier],\\n  );\\n\\n  return (\\n    <BillingContext.Provider\\n      value={{\\n        tier,\\n        isSubscribed,\\n        offerings,\\n        purchasePackage,\\n        restorePurchases,\\n        isLoading,\\n        canUseProduct,\\n        checkUsageLimit,\\n      }}\\n    >\\n      {children}\\n    </BillingContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function useBilling() {\\n  const context = useContext(BillingContext);\\n  if (!context) throw new Error('useBilling must be used within BillingProvider');\\n  return context;\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Write] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\",\"content\":\"import React, { useState } from 'react';\\nimport {\\n  View,\\n  Text,\\n  ScrollView,\\n  TouchableOpacity,\\n  StyleSheet,\\n  Alert,\\n  ActivityIndicator,\\n} from 'react-native';\\nimport { useRouter } from 'expo-router';\\nimport { TIERS, type TierName } from '@/constants/config';\\nimport { useBilling } from '@/providers/BillingProvider';\\nimport { useTheme } from '@/providers/ThemeProvider';\\nimport { Check, Crown, Star, Zap } from 'lucide-react-native';\\n\\nconst TIER_KEYS: TierName[] = ['free', 'pro', 'business'];\\n\\nconst TIER_META: Record<TierName, { icon: typeof Crown; tagline: string; badge: string | null }> = {\\n  free: { icon: Zap, tagline: 'Get started with the basics', badge: null },\\n  pro: { icon: Star, tagline: 'For individuals who send regularly', badge: 'Most Popular' },\\n  business: { icon: Crown, tagline: 'Unlimited power for your business', badge: 'Best Value' },\\n};\\n\\nconst FEATURE_ROWS: { label: string; field: keyof typeof TIERS.free }[] = [\\n  { label: 'Letter generations / mo', field: 'letterGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Image generations / mo', field: 'imageGenerations' },\\n  { label: 'Letters sent / mo', field: 'lettersSent' },\\n];\\n\\nfunction formatLimit(value: number): string {\\n  if (value === -1) return 'Unlimited';\\n  return String(value);\\n}\\n\\nfunction formatProducts(products: readonly string[]): string {\\n  const names: Record<string, string> = {\\n    postcard: 'Postcards',\\n    letter: 'Letters',\\n    greeting: 'Greeting Cards',\\n    windowless_letter: 'Windowless Letters',\\n    giftcard: 'Gift Cards',\\n  };\\n  return products.map((p) => names[p] || p).join(', ');\\n}\\n\\nexport default function PaywallScreen() {\\n  const { colors } = useTheme();\\n  const router = useRouter();\\n  const {\\n    tier: currentTier,\\n    offerings,\\n    purchasePackage,\\n    restorePurchases,\\n    isLoading,\\n  } = useBilling();\\n\\n  const [purchasing, setPurchasing] = useState<TierName | null>(null);\\n\\n  const handlePurchase = async (tierKey: TierName) => {\\n    if (tierKey === 'free' || tierKey === currentTier) return;\\n\\n    const currentOffering = offerings?.current;\\n    if (!currentOffering) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', 'Subscription packages are not available right now. Please try again later.');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Match the RevenueCat package identifier to the tier\\n    const pkg = currentOffering.availablePackages.find((p) =>\\n      p.identifier.toLowerCase().includes(tierKey),\\n    );\\n\\n    if (!pkg) {\\n      Alert.alert('Unavailable', `The ${TIERS[tierKey].name} package could not be found.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    setPurchasing(tierKey);\\n    try {\\n      await purchasePackage(pkg);\\n      Alert.alert('Success', `You are now on the ${TIERS[tierKey].name} plan!`, [\\n        { text: 'OK', onPress: () => router.back() },\\n      ]);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Purchase Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Something went wrong.');\\n    } finally {\\n      setPurchasing(null);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleRestore = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      await restorePurchases();\\n      Alert.alert('Restored', 'Your purchases have been restored.');\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      Alert.alert('Restore Failed', error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Could not restore purchases.');\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const s = StyleSheet.create({\\n    container: { flex: 1, backgroundColor: colors.background },\\n    content: { padding: 16, paddingBottom: 60 },\\n    header: { fontSize: 28, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 8 },\\n    subtitle: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textSecondary, textAlign: 'center', marginTop: 6, marginBottom: 24 },\\n    card: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.card,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      borderWidth: 1,\\n      borderColor: colors.border,\\n      padding: 20,\\n      marginBottom: 16,\\n    },\\n    cardHighlighted: {\\n      borderColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderWidth: 2,\\n    },\\n    badgeContainer: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: -12,\\n      alignSelf: 'center',\\n      left: 0,\\n      right: 0,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n    },\\n    badge: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      paddingHorizontal: 14,\\n      paddingVertical: 4,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n    },\\n    badgeText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 12, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    cardHeader: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    tierName: { fontSize: 22, fontWeight: '700', color: colors.text },\\n    tagline: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textMuted, marginBottom: 12 },\\n    priceRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'baseline', marginBottom: 16 },\\n    price: { fontSize: 36, fontWeight: '800', color: colors.text },\\n    priceUnit: { fontSize: 15, color: colors.textMuted, marginLeft: 4 },\\n    divider: { height: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth, backgroundColor: colors.border, marginVertical: 14 },\\n    featureRow: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 10, marginBottom: 10 },\\n    featureText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textSecondary, flex: 1 },\\n    featureValue: { fontSize: 14, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.text },\\n    productsLabel: { fontSize: 13, fontWeight: '600', color: colors.textMuted, marginTop: 4, marginBottom: 4 },\\n    productsText: { fontSize: 13, color: colors.textSecondary, lineHeight: 18 },\\n    purchaseButton: {\\n      backgroundColor: colors.primary,\\n      borderRadius: 12,\\n      paddingVertical: 14,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n      marginTop: 16,\\n    },\\n    purchaseButtonDisabled: { opacity: 0.5 },\\n    purchaseButtonCurrent: { backgroundColor: colors.successLight },\\n    purchaseButtonText: { color: '#fff', fontSize: 16, fontWeight: '700' },\\n    purchaseButtonTextCurrent: { color: colors.success },\\n    currentBadge: {\\n      flexDirection: 'row',\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      gap: 6,\\n    },\\n    restoreButton: {\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      paddingVertical: 16,\\n      marginTop: 8,\\n    },\\n    restoreText: { fontSize: 14, color: colors.textMuted, textDecorationLine: 'underline' },\\n    closeButton: {\\n      position: 'absolute',\\n      top: 16,\\n      right: 16,\\n      zIndex: 10,\\n      width: 32,\\n      height: 32,\\n      borderRadius: 16,\\n      backgroundColor: colors.surface,\\n      alignItems: 'center',\\n      justifyContent: 'center',\\n    },\\n    closeText: { fontSize: 18, color: colors.textSecondary, fontWeight: '600' },\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <ScrollView style={s.container} contentContainerStyle={s.content}>\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.closeButton} onPress={() => router.back()}>\\n        <Text style={s.closeText}>X</Text>\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n\\n      <Text style={s.header}>Choose Your Plan</Text>\\n      <Text style={s.subtitle}>Unlock more letters, designs, and products</Text>\\n\\n      {TIER_KEYS.map((tierKey) => {\\n        const config = TIERS[tierKey];\\n        const meta = TIER_META[tierKey];\\n        const Icon = meta.icon;\\n        const isCurrent = tierKey === currentTier;\\n        const isHighlighted = tierKey === 'pro';\\n        const isPurchasing = purchasing === tierKey;\\n        const isDisabled = isLoading || isPurchasing || isCurrent || tierKey === 'free';\\n\\n        return (\\n          <View key={tierKey} style={[s.card, isHighlighted && s.cardHighlighted]}>\\n            {meta.badge && (\\n              <View style={s.badgeContainer}>\\n                <View style={s.badge}>\\n                  <Text style={s.badgeText}>{meta.badge}</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              </View>\\n            )}\\n\\n            <View style={s.cardHeader}>\\n              <Icon size={24} color={colors.primary} />\\n              <Text style={s.tierName}>{config.name}</Text>\\n            </View>\\n            <Text style={s.tagline}>{meta.tagline}</Text>\\n\\n            <View style={s.priceRow}>\\n              <Text style={s.price}>\\n                {config.price === 0 ? 'Free' : `$${config.price}`}\\n              </Text>\\n              {config.price > 0 && <Text style={s.priceUnit}>/mo</Text>}\\n            </View>\\n\\n            <View style={s.divider} />\\n\\n            {FEATURE_ROWS.map((feat) => (\\n              <View key={feat.field} style={s.featureRow}>\\n                <Check size={16} color={colors.success} />\\n                <Text style={s.featureText}>{feat.label}</Text>\\n                <Text style={s.featureValue}>\\n                  {formatLimit(config[feat.field] as number)}\\n                </Text>\\n              </View>\\n            ))}\\n\\n            <Text style={s.productsLabel}>Available Products</Text>\\n            <Text style={s.productsText}>{formatProducts(config.products)}</Text>\\n\\n            <TouchableOpacity\\n              style={[\\n                s.purchaseButton,\\n                isCurrent && s.purchaseButtonCurrent,\\n                isDisabled && s.purchaseButtonDisabled,\\n              ]}\\n              onPress={() => handlePurchase(tierKey)}\\n              disabled={isDisabled}\\n            >\\n              {isPurchasing ? (\\n                <ActivityIndicator color=\\\"#fff\\\" />\\n              ) : isCurrent ? (\\n                <View style={s.currentBadge}>\\n                  <Check size={18} color={colors.success} />\\n                  <Text style={s.purchaseButtonTextCurrent}>Current Plan</Text>\\n                </View>\\n              ) : tierKey === 'free' ? (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>Free Forever</Text>\\n              ) : (\\n                <Text style={s.purchaseButtonText}>\\n                  Subscribe to {config.name} - ${config.price}/mo\\n                </Text>\\n              )}\\n            </TouchableOpacity>\\n          </View>\\n        );\\n      })}\\n\\n      <TouchableOpacity style={s.restoreButton} onPress={handleRestore} disabled={isLoading}>\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <ActivityIndicator color={colors.textMuted} />\\n        ) : (\\n          <Text style={s.restoreText}>Restore Purchases</Text>\\n        )}\\n      </TouchableOpacity>\\n    </ScrollView>\\n  );\\n}\\n\"}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: TodoWrite] {\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Create providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating providers/BillingProvider.tsx with RevenueCat integration\"},{\"content\":\"Create app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating app/paywall.tsx paywall screen\"}]}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n[Tool: Read] {\"file_path\":\"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx\"}\n\n--- RESULT ---\nBoth files are created and verified. Here is a summary of what was built:\n\n---\n\n## File 1: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/providers/BillingProvider.tsx`\n\n**RevenueCat Billing Provider** -- 150 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Context interface** (`BillingContextType`) exposes: `tier`, `isSubscribed`, `offerings`, `purchasePackage`, `restorePurchases`, `isLoading`, `canUseProduct`, `checkUsageLimit`\n- **Initialization** (lines 38-55): Calls `Purchases.configure({ apiKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY })` on mount, then immediately fetches offerings and customer info to determine the starting tier.\n- **User identification** (lines 58-69): When `user?.id` changes (from `useAuth()`), calls `Purchases.logIn(user.id)` to associate the Supabase user with RevenueCat and re-reads the tier from the returned `customerInfo`.\n- **Live listener** (lines 72-80): Registers `Purchases.addCustomerInfoUpdateListener` so tier changes made externally (e.g., from App Store subscription management) are reflected in real time. Cleans up on unmount.\n- **`determineTier` helper** (lines 24-29): Checks `customerInfo.entitlements.active` for `'business'` first, then `'pro'`, defaulting to `'free'`.\n- **`purchasePackage`** (lines 82-94): Wraps `Purchases.purchasePackage()`, sets loading state, updates tier on success, and silently swallows user-cancelled errors (via `error.userCancelled`).\n- **`restorePurchases`** (lines 96-106): Wraps `Purchases.restorePurchases()`, updates tier from the restored `CustomerInfo`.\n- **`canUseProduct`** (lines 110-116): Checks whether the current tier's `products` array includes the given product type string.\n- **`checkUsageLimit`** (lines 118-126): Compares a numeric usage count against the tier's configured limit for a given field; returns `true` if unlimited (`-1`) or if usage is below the limit.\n- **`useBilling()` hook** (lines 146-150): Standard context consumer with a descriptive error if used outside the provider.\n\nAll types (`TierName`, `TIERS`, `REVENUECAT_API_KEY`) are imported from `@/constants/config`, and `useAuth` from `@/providers/AuthProvider`, matching the existing codebase patterns.\n\n---\n\n## File 2: `/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/KindLetters/ios/app/paywall.tsx`\n\n**Paywall Screen** -- 276 lines\n\nKey implementation details:\n\n- **Imports**: Uses `TIERS` and `TierName` from `@/constants/config`, `useBilling` from `@/providers/BillingProvider`, `useTheme` from `@/providers/ThemeProvider`, and `{ Check, Crown, Star, Zap }` from `lucide-react-native`.\n- **Tier cards**: Renders all three tiers (Free, Pro at $29/mo, Business at $99/mo) using a `TIER_KEYS` array and a `TIER_META` record that maps each tier to an icon, tagline, and optional badge label (\"Most Popular\" for Pro, \"Best Value\" for Business).\n- **Feature comparison**: Each card shows letter generations/mo, image generations/mo, and letters sent/mo with values pulled directly from `TIERS[tierKey]`, formatted via `formatLimit()` (which renders `-1` as \"Unlimited\"). An \"Available Products\" section lists the product types in human-readable form.\n- **Purchase flow**: The \"Subscribe\" button calls `handlePurchase(tierKey)`, which looks up the matching `PurchasesPackage` from `offerings.current.availablePackages` by matching on the tier name in the identifier, then delegates to `purchasePackage(pkg)` from the billing context. Shows a success alert and navigates back.\n- **Current plan indicator**: If a tier matches `currentTier`, the button shows a green \"Current Plan\" label with a check icon and is disabled.\n- **Loading states**: Per-tier `purchasing` state shows an `ActivityIndicator` on the button being purchased. The global `isLoading` from billing disables all buttons.\n- **Restore purchases**: A button at the bottom calls `restorePurchases()` from the billing context, with error handling via `Alert`.\n- **Close button**: Top-right close button calls `router.back()`.\n- **Styling**: Uses the same `const s = StyleSheet.create({...})` pattern inside the component body with `colors` from `useTheme()`, consistent with `send.tsx`, `settings.tsx`, and other existing screens. Uses `colors.card`, `colors.border`, `colors.primary`, `colors.success`, `colors.successLight`, `colors.text`, `colors.textSecondary`, `colors.textMuted`, `colors.surface`, and `colors.background`.\n- **Modal presentation**: The file is created at `app/paywall.tsx`. Expo Router will auto-register it. The existing `_layout.tsx` was not modified as requested -- in Expo Router, the screen will render as a regular stack screen and can be presented modally by adding a `<Stack.Screen name=\"paywall\" options={{ presentation: 'modal' }} />` entry to `_layout.tsx` when ready.\n"}}}
